window.LEVEL_DATA["B2"] = {"ai-02":{"intro":"Bir röportajda şirketin hikâyesini ve misyonunu akıcı ve ikna edici biçimde anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"en":"Roughly one in five people worldwide, well over a billion, lives with some degree of hearing loss.","tr":"Dünya genelinde kabaca her beş kişiden biri, yani bir milyarı rahatça aşan sayıda insan, bir derece işitme kaybıyla yaşıyor."},{"en":"Yet the vast majority of them are never tested, largely because there simply aren't enough audiologists to go around.","tr":"Yine de bunların büyük çoğunluğu hiç test edilmiyor; bunun başlıca nedeni de herkese yetecek kadar odyolog olmaması."},{"en":"In smaller towns, it isn't unusual for people to wait several months just to get an appointment.","tr":"Daha küçük kasabalarda insanların sırf randevu alabilmek için birkaç ay beklemesi alışılmadık bir durum değil."},{"en":"By the time they're finally seen, the problem has often been affecting their work and relationships for years.","tr":"Sonunda muayene olduklarında, sorun çoğu zaman yıllardır işlerini ve ilişkilerini etkiliyor oluyor."},{"en":"Looking at this, we kept coming back to one question.","tr":"Buna bakınca sürekli aynı soruya geri döndük."},{"en":"What if the test could be carried out by a machine, without an expert having to be in the room?","tr":"Ya test, odada bir uzmanın bulunmasına gerek kalmadan bir makine tarafından yapılabilseydi?"},{"en":"That question is what AIHEAR was built on.","tr":"AIHEAR'ın üzerine kurulduğu şey işte bu soru."},{"en":"Today we're a team of six, which is made up of three engineers, a doctor and two business people.","tr":"Bugün üç mühendis, bir doktor ve iki iş insanından oluşan altı kişilik bir ekibiz."},{"en":"Our mission, put simply, is to make hearing tests accessible to everyone, wherever they live.","tr":"Kısaca söylemek gerekirse misyonumuz, işitme testlerini nerede yaşarlarsa yaşasınlar herkes için erişilebilir kılmak."},{"en":"We started in Turkey, but since the problem is global, it seems natural that our market should be too.","tr":"Türkiye'de başladık ama sorun küresel olduğu için pazarımızın da öyle olması doğal görünüyor."},{"en":"If hearing tests were as easy to get as a blood pressure check, I'd say we would have done our job.","tr":"İşitme testi yaptırmak tansiyon ölçtürmek kadar kolay olsaydı, bence işimizi yapmış olurduk."}],"vocab":[{"en":"live with","tr":"...ile yaşamak","ex":"Millions of people live with hearing loss.","def":"to have a condition that continues for a long time"},{"en":"the vast majority","tr":"büyük çoğunluk","ex":"The vast majority of them are never tested.","def":"almost all of a group"},{"en":"to go around","tr":"herkese yetecek kadar","ex":"There aren't enough audiologists to go around.","def":"enough for everyone who needs it"},{"en":"it isn't unusual for","tr":"...alışılmadık bir durum değil","ex":"It isn't unusual for people to wait months.","def":"used to say that something happens quite often"},{"en":"keep coming back to","tr":"sürekli ...e geri dönmek","ex":"We kept coming back to one question.","def":"to return to the same idea again and again"},{"en":"be built on","tr":"...üzerine kurulmak","ex":"AIHEAR was built on a simple question.","def":"to have something as its base or starting point"},{"en":"be made up of","tr":"...den oluşmak","ex":"Our team is made up of six people.","def":"to consist of particular parts or people"},{"en":"put simply","tr":"kısaca söylemek gerekirse","ex":"Put simply, we want everyone to get tested.","def":"said in an easy, clear way"}],"grammar":{"title":"Passive: telling the company story","tr":"Eylemi yapanın değil, eylemin önemli olduğu durumlarda passive kullanılır: be + V3. Şirket hikâyesini anlatırken olayları daha nesnel gösterir.","examples":["The vast majority of them are never tested.","What if the test could be carried out by a machine?","That question is what AIHEAR was built on."]},"questions":[{"q":"Why are most people with hearing loss never tested?","options":["Tests are too dangerous","There aren't enough audiologists to go around","Hearing loss is very rare"],"a":1},{"q":"What does the speaker say about small towns?","options":["People often wait months for an appointment","Every town has an audiologist","Tests there are free"],"a":0},{"q":"Who is on the team?","options":["Six engineers","Two doctors and four engineers","Three engineers, a doctor and two business people"],"a":2},{"q":"What does the blood pressure comparison suggest?","options":["The company also wants to measure blood pressure","They want hearing tests to become routine and easy to get","Blood pressure checks are too expensive"],"a":1},{"q":"Why does the speaker think the market should be global?","options":["Turkey is too small","Investors asked for it","The team lives abroad","The problem itself is global"],"a":3}],"gaps":[{"s":"There simply aren't enough audiologists to go ___.","a":"around","hint":"herkese yetecek kadar"},{"s":"That question is what AIHEAR was built ___.","a":"on","hint":"üzerine kurulmak"},{"s":"Our team is made ___ of three engineers, a doctor and two business people.","a":"up","hint":"oluşmak"}],"order":[{"a":"The vast majority of them are never tested."},{"a":"That question is what AIHEAR was built on."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Herkese yetecek kadar odyolog yok.","en":"There aren't enough audiologists to go around.","keys":["enough audiologists","to go around"]},{"tr":"Ekibimiz altı kişiden oluşuyor.","en":"Our team is made up of six people.","keys":["made up of","six people"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Journalist","personaTr":"Gazeteci","scene":"Bir teknoloji dergisinden bir gazeteci, AIHEAR'ın neden var olduğunu sorguluyor.","turns":[{"ai":"Hearing loss isn't usually seen as a big problem, so why build a company around it?","aiTr":"İşitme kaybı genelde büyük bir sorun olarak görülmez; neden bunun üzerine bir şirket kurdunuz?","hint":"Because one in five people lives with some hearing loss, yet the vast majority are never tested.","keys":["one in five","never tested","vast majority"]},{"ai":"And why aren't they tested?","aiTr":"Peki neden test edilmiyorlar?","hint":"Mainly because there aren't enough audiologists to go around, so in small towns people wait months for an appointment.","keys":["audiologists","to go around","months"]},{"ai":"Where did the idea for AIHEAR actually come from?","aiTr":"AIHEAR fikri aslında nereden çıktı?","hint":"We kept coming back to one question: what if the test could be carried out by a machine, without an expert in the room?","keys":["what if","machine","without an expert"]},{"ai":"If you had to sum up your mission in one sentence, what would it be?","aiTr":"Misyonunuzu tek cümleyle özetlemeniz gerekse, ne olurdu?","hint":"Put simply, it would be to make hearing tests accessible to everyone, wherever they live.","keys":["accessible","everyone","wherever"]}]}},"ai-01":{"intro":"Teknik süreci passive yapılarla, net ve profesyonel bir şekilde açıklıyorsun.","text":[{"en":"An audiometer measures how well someone can hear, and it's one of the most basic tools in hearing care.","tr":"Odyometre, birinin ne kadar iyi duyabildiğini ölçer ve işitme sağlığındaki en temel araçlardan biridir."},{"en":"Traditionally, the test is carried out by a trained audiologist in a quiet room and takes around thirty minutes.","tr":"Geleneksel olarak test, sessiz bir odada eğitimli bir odyolog tarafından yapılır ve yaklaşık otuz dakika sürer."},{"en":"Our audiometer is autonomous, which means the whole test can be run without an expert in the room.","tr":"Bizim odyometremiz otonom; yani tüm test, odada bir uzman olmadan yürütülebilir."},{"en":"The patient simply puts on the headphones and follows the instructions that appear on the screen.","tr":"Hasta sadece kulaklıkları takar ve ekranda beliren talimatları takip eder."},{"en":"Sounds are played at different volumes and frequencies, and the patient presses a button whenever they hear one.","tr":"Farklı ses seviyelerinde ve frekanslarda sesler çalınır ve hasta bir ses duyduğu her an bir düğmeye basar."},{"en":"Each response is analysed by our AI, which adjusts the next sound in real time.","tr":"Her yanıt yapay zekâmız tarafından analiz edilir ve yapay zekâ bir sonraki sesi gerçek zamanlı olarak ayarlar."},{"en":"That way, the test adapts to each patient instead of following a fixed script.","tr":"Böylece test, sabit bir senaryoyu izlemek yerine her hastaya uyum sağlar."},{"en":"At the end, an audiogram is generated automatically, which a doctor can then review.","tr":"Sonunda otomatik olarak bir odyogram oluşturulur ve bir doktor bunu daha sonra inceleyebilir."},{"en":"The whole process takes under ten minutes, which I'd say is about a third of the usual time.","tr":"Tüm süreç on dakikadan kısa sürer; bence bu, normal sürenin yaklaşık üçte biri."},{"en":"Since the AI runs on the device itself, patient data never has to leave the clinic, and it works offline too.","tr":"Yapay zekâ cihazın kendisinde çalıştığı için hasta verilerinin kliniği hiç terk etmesi gerekmez ve cihaz çevrimdışı da çalışır."},{"en":"Software updates are sent about once a month, so the system keeps improving.","tr":"Yazılım güncellemeleri yaklaşık ayda bir gönderilir, böylece sistem sürekli gelişir."}],"vocab":[{"en":"carry out a test","tr":"test yapmak","ex":"The test is usually carried out by an audiologist.","def":"to do or perform a test"},{"en":"trained audiologist","tr":"eğitimli odyolog","ex":"A trained audiologist usually runs the test.","def":"a specialist with professional training in hearing tests"},{"en":"analyse a response","tr":"bir yanıtı analiz etmek","ex":"Each response is analysed by the AI.","def":"to examine something carefully to understand it"},{"en":"adapt to","tr":"...e uyum sağlamak","ex":"The test adapts to each patient.","def":"to change to suit a new situation or person"},{"en":"follow a fixed script","tr":"sabit bir senaryoyu izlemek","ex":"Traditional tests often follow a fixed script.","def":"to do the same steps every time, without change"},{"en":"be generated automatically","tr":"otomatik olarak oluşturulmak","ex":"An audiogram is generated automatically.","def":"to be produced by a machine without human work"},{"en":"review","tr":"incelemek","ex":"A doctor can then review the results.","def":"to look at something carefully to check it"},{"en":"work offline","tr":"çevrimdışı çalışmak","ex":"The device works offline, even in small towns.","def":"to work without an internet connection"},{"en":"keep improving","tr":"sürekli gelişmek","ex":"The system keeps improving with each update.","def":"to continue getting better"}],"grammar":{"title":"Passive: describing a technical process","tr":"Kimin yaptığı değil, ne yapıldığı önemliyse passive (be + V3) kullanılır. Teknik süreçleri anlatırken çok yaygındır.","examples":["The test is carried out by a trained audiologist.","Each response is analysed by our AI.","An audiogram is generated automatically."]},"questions":[{"q":"Who traditionally carries out a hearing test?","options":["The patient","A trained audiologist","A software engineer"],"a":1},{"q":"What happens after each response?","options":["The doctor is called","The test starts again","The AI adjusts the next sound"],"a":2},{"q":"Why does patient data never have to leave the clinic?","options":["The AI runs on the device itself","The test is short","It is deleted once a month"],"a":0},{"q":"What can we infer from 'the test adapts to each patient'?","options":["Every patient hears exactly the same sounds","Different patients may hear a different sequence of sounds","Patients choose their own sounds"],"a":1},{"q":"Roughly how much time does the device save compared to a traditional test?","options":["About five minutes","No time at all","About an hour","About two-thirds of the time"],"a":3}],"gaps":[{"s":"Traditionally, the test is ___ out by a trained audiologist.","a":"carried","hint":"yapılır"},{"s":"The test ___ to each patient instead of following a fixed script.","a":"adapts","hint":"uyum sağlar"},{"s":"Since the AI runs on the device, it works ___ too.","a":"offline","hint":"çevrimdışı"}],"order":[{"a":"Each response is analysed by our AI."},{"a":"An audiogram is generated automatically at the end."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Her yanıt yapay zekâ tarafından analiz edilir.","en":"Each response is analysed by the AI.","keys":["response","by the AI"]},{"tr":"Hasta verilerinin kliniği terk etmesi gerekmez.","en":"Patient data doesn't have to leave the clinic.","keys":["patient data","leave the clinic"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Curious doctor","personaTr":"Meraklı doktor","scene":"Bir fuarda İngiliz bir kulak burun boğaz doktoru cihazı biraz şüpheyle inceliyor ve sorular soruyor.","turns":[{"ai":"So is this one of those apps that replaces the audiologist, or something more serious?","aiTr":"Yani bu, odyoloğun yerini alan o uygulamalardan biri mi, yoksa daha ciddi bir şey mi?","hint":"It's a medical device rather than an app: an autonomous audiometer that runs the whole test without an expert in the room.","keys":["autonomous audiometer","without an expert","medical device"]},{"ai":"How does it decide which sounds to play?","aiTr":"Hangi sesleri çalacağına nasıl karar veriyor?","hint":"Each response is analysed by our AI, which adjusts the next sound in real time, so the test adapts to each patient.","keys":["adjusts","real time","adapts"]},{"ai":"And how long would a typical test take?","aiTr":"Peki tipik bir test ne kadar sürer?","hint":"Under ten minutes, which I'd say is about a third of the usual time.","keys":["ten minutes","third"]},{"ai":"Where does the patient data go? Our hospital is very strict about that.","aiTr":"Hasta verileri nereye gidiyor? Hastanemiz bu konuda çok katı.","hint":"It stays on the device, because the AI runs locally, so the data never has to leave your clinic.","keys":["on the device","locally","leave your clinic"]}]}},"st-02":{"intro":"Küçük bir ekipte iletişimi, sorumlulukları ve suçlama kültüründen kaçınmayı nasıl yönettiğini anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"en":"Running a team of six means there's nowhere to hide, so communication has to be good.","tr":"Altı kişilik bir ekibi yönetmek saklanacak hiçbir yer olmadığı anlamına gelir, bu yüzden iletişimin iyi olması şart."},{"en":"Our week starts with a Monday stand-up, which we try to keep short and focused.","tr":"Haftamız, kısa ve odaklı tutmaya çalıştığımız bir pazartesi toplantısıyla başlar."},{"en":"Each person is asked to cover three things: what they've done, what they're doing next and what's blocking them.","tr":"Herkesten üç şeyi anlatması istenir: ne yaptığı, sırada ne yapacağı ve onu neyin engellediği."},{"en":"I've learned that vague requests tend to get vague results, so every task is given a clear owner and a deadline.","tr":"Belirsiz isteklerin belirsiz sonuçlar doğurduğunu öğrendim, bu yüzden her göreve net bir sorumlu ve bir son tarih verilir."},{"en":"Rather than 'Could you look at the report?', I'd say 'Please finish the test report by Friday.'","tr":"'Rapora bir bakabilir misin?' yerine 'Lütfen test raporunu cumaya kadar bitir.' derim."},{"en":"When something goes wrong, the question isn't who caused it, but how we fix it and stop it happening again.","tr":"Bir şeyler ters gittiğinde soru kimin neden olduğu değil, nasıl düzelteceğimiz ve tekrarlanmasını nasıl önleyeceğimizdir."},{"en":"If people were afraid of being blamed, they'd simply stop telling me about problems.","tr":"İnsanlar suçlanmaktan korksaydı, bana sorunları anlatmayı bırakırlardı."},{"en":"I give feedback often, both positive and negative, and I ask the team to do the same for me.","tr":"Hem olumlu hem olumsuz, sık sık geri bildirim veririm ve ekipten de bana aynısını yapmasını isterim."},{"en":"One of our engineers once told me that I talked too much in meetings, and she was right.","tr":"Mühendislerimizden biri bir keresinde toplantılarda çok fazla konuştuğumu söyledi ve haklıydı."},{"en":"Since then, I've tried to listen more than I talk.","tr":"O zamandan beri konuştuğumdan daha çok dinlemeye çalışıyorum."},{"en":"At the end of the day, they're the experts, and my job is mostly to trust them and clear the way.","tr":"Sonuçta uzman olan onlar; benim işim de çoğunlukla onlara güvenmek ve önlerini açmak."}],"vocab":[{"en":"nowhere to hide","tr":"saklanacak yer olmaması","ex":"In a team of six, there's nowhere to hide.","def":"a situation where everyone can see your work and mistakes"},{"en":"stand-up","tr":"kısa durum toplantısı","ex":"Our week starts with a Monday stand-up.","def":"a short meeting where everyone gives a quick update"},{"en":"vague request","tr":"belirsiz istek","ex":"I try not to send vague requests.","def":"a request that is not clear or exact"},{"en":"a clear owner","tr":"net bir sorumlu","ex":"Every task is given a clear owner.","def":"one person who is responsible for a task"},{"en":"tend to","tr":"-me eğiliminde olmak","ex":"Vague requests tend to get vague results.","def":"to usually do or be something"},{"en":"stop something happening again","tr":"bir şeyin tekrarlanmasını önlemek","ex":"We fix it and stop it happening again.","def":"to make sure a problem does not happen a second time"},{"en":"be afraid of being blamed","tr":"suçlanmaktan korkmak","ex":"If people were afraid of being blamed, they'd hide problems.","def":"to worry that people will say something is your fault"},{"en":"at the end of the day","tr":"sonuçta, nihayetinde","ex":"At the end of the day, they're the experts.","def":"when everything is considered"},{"en":"clear the way","tr":"önünü açmak","ex":"My job is to trust them and clear the way.","def":"to remove problems so that others can move forward"}],"grammar":{"title":"Passive voice: describing how things work","tr":"Bir süreci anlatırken kimin yaptığı değil, ne yapıldığı önemliyse 'be + V3' kullanırız. Ekip kurallarını anlatırken daha nesnel ve kurumsal duyulur.","examples":["Each person is asked to cover three things.","Every task is given a clear owner and a deadline.","If people were afraid of being blamed, they'd stop telling me about problems."]},"questions":[{"q":"What is each person asked to cover at the Monday stand-up?","options":["Their budget for the month","What they've done, what's next and what's blocking them","Their opinion of the manager"],"a":1},{"q":"According to the speaker, what happens when requests are vague?","options":["The results are vague too","People work faster","Deadlines become shorter"],"a":0},{"q":"Why doesn't the speaker look for someone to blame?","options":["Because the company has a legal rule about it","Because mistakes never happen","Because people would stop reporting problems"],"a":2},{"q":"What did one of the engineers tell the speaker?","options":["That the deadlines were too short","That the speaker talked too much in meetings","That she wanted a new task"],"a":1},{"q":"What can we infer about how the speaker sees their own role?","options":["They see their job as supporting the team rather than controlling it","They see themselves as the main expert on every task","They think meetings are a waste of time"],"a":0}],"gaps":[{"s":"In a team of six, there's nowhere to ___.","a":"hide","hint":"saklanmak"},{"s":"Vague requests ___ to get vague results.","a":"tend","hint":"eğiliminde olmak"},{"s":"My job is mostly to trust them and clear the ___.","a":"way","hint":"yol (önünü açmak)"}],"order":[{"a":"Our week starts with a short Monday stand-up."},{"a":"I've tried to listen more than I talk."}],"translate":[{"tr":"İnsanlar suçlanmaktan korksaydı, bana sorunları anlatmayı bırakırlardı.","en":"If people were afraid of being blamed, they'd stop telling me about problems.","keys":["afraid of being blamed","stop telling me"]},{"tr":"Her göreve net bir sorumlu ve bir son tarih verilir.","en":"Every task is given a clear owner and a deadline.","keys":["clear owner","deadline"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"New engineer","personaTr":"Yeni işe başlayan mühendis","scene":"Ekibe bu hafta katılan yeni yazılım mühendisi, ekip kültürünü ve senden ne bekleyeceğini öğrenmek istiyor.","turns":[{"ai":"So how do things usually work around here?","aiTr":"Peki burada işler genelde nasıl yürüyor?","hint":"Our week starts with a short Monday stand-up, where everyone covers what they've done, what's next and what's blocking them.","keys":["stand-up","blocking","Monday"]},{"ai":"What happens if I make a mistake? Will I get in trouble?","aiTr":"Bir hata yaparsam ne olur? Başım derde girer mi?","hint":"No, the question isn't who caused it, but how we fix it and stop it happening again.","keys":["fix it","who caused","happening again"]},{"ai":"How will I know what's expected of me?","aiTr":"Benden ne beklendiğini nasıl bileceğim?","hint":"Every task is given a clear owner and a deadline, and I give feedback often, both positive and negative.","keys":["clear owner","deadline","feedback"]},{"ai":"And if I think you're doing something wrong, can I tell you?","aiTr":"Peki senin yanlış bir şey yaptığını düşünürsem sana söyleyebilir miyim?","hint":"Of course. One of our engineers once told me I talked too much in meetings, and she was right.","keys":["of course","told me","she was right"]}]}},"te-01":{"intro":"Bir konferansta yapay zekânın sağlıktaki yerini, veri yanlılığı riskini ve erişim fırsatını tartışıyorsun.","text":[{"en":"It's often said that AI will replace doctors, but I'd argue that's the wrong way to look at it.","tr":"Yapay zekânın doktorların yerini alacağı sıkça söyleniyor ama bence bu, konuya yanlış bir bakış."},{"en":"AI is best at repetitive tasks, which require speed and consistency rather than judgment.","tr":"Yapay zekâ en çok, muhakemeden çok hız ve tutarlılık gerektiren tekrarlı işlerde başarılı."},{"en":"In radiology, for instance, algorithms are being used to flag suspicious areas on scans so that radiologists can review them first.","tr":"Örneğin radyolojide algoritmalar, radyologlar önce onlara baksın diye taramalardaki şüpheli alanları işaretlemek için kullanılıyor."},{"en":"Such systems don't get tired, and they can process thousands of images in the time it takes a person to read a few.","tr":"Bu tür sistemler yorulmuyor ve bir insanın birkaç görüntüyü okuduğu sürede binlercesini işleyebiliyor."},{"en":"That said, they're only as good as the data they were trained on.","tr":"Bununla birlikte, ancak eğitildikleri veri kadar iyiler."},{"en":"If the training data didn't include enough patients from a certain group, the results for that group would be less reliable.","tr":"Eğitim verisi belirli bir gruptan yeterince hasta içermeseydi, o grup için sonuçlar daha az güvenilir olurdu."},{"en":"That's why the final decision should always be made by a clinician.","tr":"Bu yüzden nihai karar her zaman bir klinisyen tarafından verilmeli."},{"en":"In my view, the biggest impact will be on access rather than on diagnosis itself.","tr":"Bana göre en büyük etki, teşhisin kendisinden çok erişim üzerinde olacak."},{"en":"Around one in five people has some degree of hearing loss, yet most are never tested because there aren't enough audiologists.","tr":"Yaklaşık her beş kişiden birinde bir derece işitme kaybı var, ancak yeterli odyolog olmadığı için çoğu hiç test edilmiyor."},{"en":"Our device, which runs the test without an expert in the room, is designed to close exactly that gap.","tr":"Testi odada bir uzman olmadan yapan cihazımız, tam olarak bu açığı kapatmak için tasarlandı."},{"en":"The AI adjusts the test in real time, and it's improved through software updates that are sent about once a month.","tr":"Yapay zekâ testi gerçek zamanlı olarak ayarlıyor ve yaklaşık ayda bir gönderilen yazılım güncellemeleriyle geliştiriliyor."}],"vocab":[{"en":"replace","tr":"yerini almak","ex":"AI won't replace doctors.","def":"to take the place of someone or something"},{"en":"flag","tr":"işaretlemek, dikkat çekmek","ex":"The algorithm flags suspicious areas on scans.","def":"to mark something so that people notice it"},{"en":"process images","tr":"görüntüleri işlemek","ex":"These systems can process thousands of images an hour.","def":"to analyze a large amount of visual information"},{"en":"only as good as","tr":"ancak … kadar iyi","ex":"AI is only as good as its data.","def":"limited by the quality of something"},{"en":"training data","tr":"eğitim verisi","ex":"The training data must include many different patients.","def":"the information an AI system learns from"},{"en":"reliable","tr":"güvenilir","ex":"The results would be less reliable.","def":"able to be trusted to be accurate"},{"en":"clinician","tr":"klinisyen","ex":"The final decision should be made by a clinician.","def":"a doctor or other health professional who treats patients"},{"en":"close the gap","tr":"açığı kapatmak","ex":"Our device is designed to close the gap in hearing care.","def":"to reduce the difference between what is needed and what exists"},{"en":"in real time","tr":"gerçek zamanlı","ex":"The AI adjusts the test in real time.","def":"immediately, while something is happening"}],"grammar":{"title":"The passive: continuous and modal forms","tr":"Passive her zamanda kullanılabilir: 'are being used' (şu anda yapılıyor), 'should be made' (yapılmalı), 'is designed' (tasarlandı). Odak işi yapanda değil, işin kendisinde olduğunda tercih edilir.","examples":["Algorithms are being used to flag suspicious areas.","The final decision should always be made by a clinician.","Our device is designed to close exactly that gap."]},"questions":[{"q":"What is the speaker's opinion about AI replacing doctors?","options":["It will happen soon","It's the wrong way to see AI","It has already happened"],"a":1},{"q":"How is AI used in radiology, according to the text?","options":["It flags suspicious areas for radiologists to review","It makes the final diagnosis","It replaces radiologists at night"],"a":0},{"q":"What would happen if the training data didn't include enough patients from a group?","options":["The system would stop working","Results for that group would be less reliable","The system would become faster","Nothing would change"],"a":1},{"q":"Why does the speaker mention the shortage of audiologists?","options":["To criticize audiologists","To explain why tests are expensive","To show the problem their device is designed to solve"],"a":2},{"q":"How is the AI in the device improved?","options":["By a technician every week","By the patients themselves","Through software updates about once a month"],"a":2}],"gaps":[{"s":"Algorithms are being used to ___ suspicious areas on scans.","a":"flag","hint":"işaretlemek"},{"s":"They're only as good as the data they were ___ on.","a":"trained","hint":"eğitilmek"},{"s":"The final decision should always be made by a ___.","a":"clinician","hint":"klinisyen"}],"order":[{"a":"AI is best at repetitive tasks."},{"a":"The final decision should be made by a clinician."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Yapay zekâ sistemleri ancak eğitildikleri veri kadar iyidir.","en":"AI systems are only as good as the data they were trained on.","keys":["only as good as","trained on"]},{"tr":"Cihazımız tam olarak bu açığı kapatmak için tasarlandı.","en":"Our device is designed to close exactly that gap.","keys":["is designed","close","gap"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Skeptical doctor","personaTr":"Şüpheci doktor","scene":"Bir konferansta kıdemli ve şüpheci bir doktor yapay zekânın riskleri hakkında seni sorguluyor.","turns":[{"ai":"Be honest: isn't AI going to replace doctors like me?","aiTr":"Dürüst olun: Yapay zekâ benim gibi doktorların yerini almayacak mı?","hint":"I'd argue that's the wrong way to look at it. AI is best at repetitive tasks, and the final decision should always be made by a clinician.","keys":["repetitive tasks","final decision","clinician"]},{"ai":"What worries me is bias. What if the data is bad?","aiTr":"Beni endişelendiren önyargı. Ya veri kötüyse?","hint":"That's a fair point. AI is only as good as the data it was trained on, so if a group were missing, the results would be less reliable.","keys":["only as good as","less reliable","trained"]},{"ai":"So where does AI really make a difference?","aiTr":"Peki yapay zekâ asıl nerede fark yaratıyor?","hint":"In my view, it's access. One in five people has some hearing loss, but most are never tested because there aren't enough audiologists.","keys":["access","one in five","audiologists"]},{"ai":"And your device?","aiTr":"Peki sizin cihazınız?","hint":"It runs the test without an expert in the room, and it's improved through monthly software updates.","keys":["without an expert","software updates","in the room"]}]}},"te-03":{"intro":"Bir hatanın kök nedenini verilerle nasıl bulduğunuzu anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Me","en":"Last week, a few clinics reported that our device was giving inaccurate results at high frequencies.","tr":"Geçen hafta birkaç klinik, cihazımızın yüksek frekanslarda hatalı sonuçlar verdiğini bildirdi."},{"who":"Me","en":"Strangely, the same model worked perfectly in other clinics, so it didn't seem to be a hardware fault.","tr":"İşin garibi, aynı model diğer kliniklerde kusursuz çalışıyordu, yani bir donanım arızası gibi görünmüyordu."},{"who":"Me","en":"Our first instinct was to blame the headphones, but replacing them didn't change anything.","tr":"İlk refleksimiz suçu kulaklıklara atmak oldu, ama onları değiştirmek hiçbir şeyi değiştirmedi."},{"who":"Me","en":"Instead of guessing again, we collected data from every device and compared the clinics that had the issue with those that didn't.","tr":"Yeniden tahmin yürütmek yerine her cihazdan veri topladık ve sorun yaşayan klinikleri yaşamayanlarla karşılaştırdık."},{"who":"Me","en":"The pattern was clear: the errors only occurred in rooms that were cooled by old air conditioners.","tr":"Örüntü netti: hatalar yalnızca eski klimalarla soğutulan odalarda ortaya çıkıyordu."},{"who":"Me","en":"It turned out that these units gave off a high-pitched whine at exactly the frequencies we were testing, which masked the test tones.","tr":"Meğer bu klimalar tam da test ettiğimiz frekanslarda tiz bir vızıltı çıkarıyormuş ve bu ses test tonlarını bastırıyormuş."},{"who":"Me","en":"In other words, patients simply couldn't hear some of the sounds, so the device recorded hearing loss that wasn't there.","tr":"Başka bir deyişle hastalar bazı sesleri duyamıyordu, bu yüzden cihaz aslında olmayan bir işitme kaybı kaydediyordu."},{"who":"Me","en":"The fix was surprisingly simple: a short noise check is now run before every test.","tr":"Çözüm şaşırtıcı derecede basitti: artık her testten önce kısa bir gürültü kontrolü yapılıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"If the room is too noisy, the user is warned before the test begins.","tr":"Oda fazla gürültülüyse kullanıcı test başlamadan önce uyarılıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"We shipped the fix in our next monthly update, and since then the results have been consistent across all clinics.","tr":"Düzeltmeyi bir sonraki aylık güncellemede yayınladık ve o zamandan beri sonuçlar tüm kliniklerde tutarlı."},{"who":"Me","en":"If I had to sum it up, I'd say the lesson is this: let the data guide you, not your assumptions.","tr":"Özetlemem gerekse, dersin şu olduğunu söylerdim: varsayımların değil, veriler sana yol göstersin."}],"vocab":[{"en":"inaccurate","tr":"hatalı, yanlış","ex":"The device was giving inaccurate results.","def":"not correct or exact"},{"en":"first instinct","tr":"ilk refleks, ilk tepki","ex":"Our first instinct was to blame the headphones.","def":"the first thing you feel you should do"},{"en":"pattern","tr":"örüntü","ex":"The pattern was clear.","def":"a regular way in which something happens"},{"en":"occur","tr":"meydana gelmek","ex":"The errors only occurred in some rooms.","def":"to happen"},{"en":"it turned out that","tr":"meğer, sonunda anlaşıldı ki","ex":"It turned out that the air conditioners were the problem.","def":"used to say what you discovered in the end"},{"en":"mask (a sound)","tr":"(bir sesi) bastırmak, örtmek","ex":"The whine masked the test tones.","def":"to stop a sound from being heard clearly"},{"en":"ship a fix","tr":"düzeltmeyi yayınlamak","ex":"We shipped the fix in our next monthly update.","def":"to release a correction to customers"},{"en":"consistent","tr":"tutarlı","ex":"The results have been consistent since then.","def":"the same and reliable every time"},{"en":"assumption","tr":"varsayım","ex":"Let the data guide you, not your assumptions.","def":"something you believe is true without proof"}],"grammar":{"title":"The passive: focus on the action","tr":"İşi kimin yaptığı önemli olmadığında ya da eylemin kendisi daha önemli olduğunda passive kullanılır: be + V3. Teknik anlatımlarda çok yaygındır.","examples":["A short noise check is now run before every test.","The user is warned before the test begins.","The rooms were cooled by old air conditioners."]},"questions":[{"q":"What did the clinics report?","options":["The device was too slow","Inaccurate results at high frequencies","Broken headphones"],"a":1},{"q":"What happened when they replaced the headphones?","options":["The problem got worse","The clinics complained more","Nothing changed"],"a":2},{"q":"Why did the device record hearing loss that wasn't there?","options":["Patients couldn't hear tones masked by the noise","The software had a bug","Patients pressed the button too late"],"a":0},{"q":"What does the speaker suggest about guessing?","options":["It is faster than collecting data","It is always the best first step","It can waste time and point you in the wrong direction"],"a":2},{"q":"How was the fix delivered to customers?","options":["Engineers visited every clinic","In the next monthly software update","New devices were sent out"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"Our first ___ was to blame the headphones.","a":"instinct","hint":"refleks, ilk tepki"},{"s":"The errors only ___ in rooms with old air conditioners.","a":"occurred","hint":"meydana geliyordu"},{"s":"The whine ___ the test tones, so patients couldn't hear them.","a":"masked","hint":"bastırdı"}],"order":[{"a":"A short noise check is now run before every test."},{"a":"Let the data guide you and not your assumptions."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Meğer sorun klimalarmış.","en":"It turned out that the air conditioners were the problem.","keys":["it turned out","air conditioners"]},{"tr":"Oda fazla gürültülüyse kullanıcı uyarılıyor.","en":"If the room is too noisy, the user is warned.","keys":["too noisy","is warned"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Clinic manager","personaTr":"Klinik müdürü","scene":"Sorun yaşayan kliniklerden birinin müdürü ne olduğunu ve sorunun tekrar etmeyeceğinden nasıl emin olabileceğini soruyor.","turns":[{"ai":"Our doctors told me the device was showing hearing loss in patients who seemed fine. What was going on?","aiTr":"Doktorlarımız cihazın, sağlıklı görünen hastalarda işitme kaybı gösterdiğini söyledi. Neler oluyordu?","hint":"It turned out that old air conditioners were making noise at high frequencies, which masked the test tones.","keys":["it turned out","air conditioners","masked","noise"]},{"ai":"How did you work that out?","aiTr":"Bunu nasıl anladınız?","hint":"We collected data from every device and compared the clinics that had the issue with those that didn't.","keys":["collected data","compared","every device"]},{"ai":"What's been done to fix it?","aiTr":"Düzeltmek için ne yapıldı?","hint":"A short noise check is now run before every test, and the user is warned if the room is too noisy.","keys":["noise check","is warned","too noisy"]},{"ai":"Would it help if we replaced our air conditioner?","aiTr":"Klimamızı değiştirsek işe yarar mı?","hint":"If you replaced it, the room would be quieter, but the noise check already protects your results.","keys":["would be quieter","noise check","protects"]}]}},"te-04":{"intro":"İki teknik seçeneğin artılarını ve eksilerini tartıp gerekçeli bir karar veriyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Engineer","en":"Before we lock in the hardware, we need to settle one question: does the AI run on the device or in the cloud?","tr":"Donanımı kesinleştirmeden önce bir soruyu netleştirmemiz gerekiyor: yapay zekâ cihazda mı çalışacak, bulutta mı?"},{"who":"Me","en":"Let's weigh it up properly — what would we gain by going with the cloud?","tr":"Bunu doğru dürüst tartalım — bulutu seçersek ne kazanırız?"},{"who":"Engineer","en":"We'd have far more computing power, and the model could be updated whenever we liked.","tr":"Çok daha fazla işlem gücümüz olur ve model istediğimiz zaman güncellenebilir."},{"who":"Engineer","en":"The downside is that every test would depend on a stable internet connection, which many small clinics simply don't have.","tr":"Dezavantajı, her testin sabit bir internet bağlantısına bağlı olması; birçok küçük klinikte de böyle bir bağlantı yok."},{"who":"Engineer","en":"On top of that, some hospitals have strict rules that don't allow patient data to leave the building.","tr":"Üstelik bazı hastanelerin, hasta verisinin binadan çıkmasına izin vermeyen katı kuralları var."},{"who":"Me","en":"And if the AI ran on the device itself?","tr":"Peki yapay zekâ cihazın kendisinde çalışsaydı?"},{"who":"Engineer","en":"Then the data would never leave the room and the test would work offline, but each unit would need more expensive hardware.","tr":"O zaman veri odadan hiç çıkmaz ve test çevrimdışı çalışırdı, ama her cihaz daha pahalı bir donanıma ihtiyaç duyardı."},{"who":"Me","en":"From what I've heard, privacy is the first thing hospital IT teams ask about, so it seems to me that's where we can't compromise.","tr":"Duyduğum kadarıyla hastane bilgi işlem ekiplerinin ilk sorduğu şey gizlilik, o yüzden bana kalırsa taviz veremeyeceğimiz nokta bu."},{"who":"Me","en":"I'd say we run the AI on the device and push model updates once a month whenever the device is connected.","tr":"Bence yapay zekâyı cihazda çalıştıralım ve cihaz bağlandığında model güncellemelerini ayda bir gönderelim."},{"who":"Engineer","en":"Fair enough — it's a trade-off, but if privacy is what closes the deal, the extra hardware cost is worth paying.","tr":"Haklısın — bu bir ödünleşim, ama anlaşmayı kapattıran şey gizlilikse ek donanım maliyetine değer."}],"vocab":[{"en":"lock in","tr":"kesinleştirmek","ex":"Before we lock in the hardware, we need to decide.","def":"to make a final decision that is hard to change"},{"en":"weigh something up","tr":"bir şeyin artısını eksisini tartmak","ex":"Let's weigh up both options.","def":"to think carefully about the good and bad points"},{"en":"computing power","tr":"işlem gücü","ex":"The cloud gives us more computing power.","def":"how much work a computer can do"},{"en":"downside","tr":"dezavantaj, olumsuz yan","ex":"The downside is the internet connection.","def":"a disadvantage"},{"en":"strict rules","tr":"katı kurallar","ex":"Some hospitals have strict rules about patient data.","def":"rules that must be followed exactly"},{"en":"compromise on something","tr":"...den taviz vermek","ex":"We can't compromise on privacy.","def":"to accept less than you want"},{"en":"push an update","tr":"güncelleme göndermek","ex":"We push updates once a month.","def":"to send new software to devices"},{"en":"close the deal","tr":"anlaşmayı kapatmak","ex":"Privacy is what closes the deal.","def":"to finally agree a sale"},{"en":"be worth (doing)","tr":"değmek","ex":"The extra cost is worth paying.","def":"good enough to justify the cost or effort"}],"grammar":{"title":"Second conditional: comparing options","tr":"Varsayımsal durumları tartışırken second conditional kullanılır: if + past simple, would + fiil. Seçenekleri karşılaştırırken çok işe yarar.","examples":["If the AI ran on the device, the test would work offline.","We'd have far more computing power with the cloud.","If we chose the cloud, every test would depend on the internet."]},"questions":[{"q":"What would the cloud offer?","options":["Lower hardware costs only","More computing power and easy model updates","Better privacy"],"a":1},{"q":"Why could the cloud be a problem for small clinics?","options":["Many don't have a stable internet connection","They don't like new technology","They can't afford a subscription"],"a":0},{"q":"What is the main cost of running the AI on the device?","options":["Slower tests","Less privacy","More expensive hardware for each unit"],"a":2},{"q":"Why does the engineer agree in the end?","options":["The cloud turns out to be too slow","Privacy will help win customers","The device is cheaper to build"],"a":1},{"q":"How will the model be updated?","options":["Monthly, whenever the device is connected","Every day through the cloud","Only when a technician visits"],"a":0}],"gaps":[{"s":"Before we lock ___ the hardware, we need to settle one question.","a":"in","hint":"kesinleştirmek (lock in)"},{"s":"The ___ is that every test would depend on the internet.","a":"downside","hint":"dezavantaj"},{"s":"Privacy is where we can't ___.","a":"compromise","hint":"taviz vermek"}],"order":[{"a":"Some hospitals don't allow patient data to leave the building."},{"a":"The extra hardware cost is worth paying."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Yapay zekâ cihazda çalışsaydı test çevrimdışı çalışırdı.","en":"If the AI ran on the device, the test would work offline.","keys":["if the ai ran","would work offline"]},{"tr":"Gizlilikten taviz veremeyiz.","en":"We can't compromise on privacy.","keys":["compromise on privacy"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Hospital IT manager","personaTr":"Hastane bilgi işlem müdürü","scene":"Bir hastanenin bilgi işlem müdürü cihazınızın veriyi nasıl işlediğini ve neden bulutu seçmediğinizi soruyor.","turns":[{"ai":"Before we go any further, I need to know where patient data is processed.","aiTr":"Daha ileri gitmeden önce hasta verisinin nerede işlendiğini bilmem gerekiyor.","hint":"Everything is processed on the device itself, so patient data never leaves the room.","keys":["on the device","never leaves","processed"]},{"ai":"Most vendors use the cloud these days — why didn't you?","aiTr":"Bugünlerde çoğu tedarikçi bulut kullanıyor — siz neden kullanmadınız?","hint":"We weighed it up carefully, but we decided we couldn't compromise on privacy.","keys":["weighed it up","compromise on privacy","privacy"]},{"ai":"What happens if our internet goes down?","aiTr":"İnternetimiz kesilirse ne olur?","hint":"Nothing changes, because the test works offline.","keys":["works offline","offline","nothing changes"]},{"ai":"And how is the model kept up to date?","aiTr":"Peki model nasıl güncel tutuluyor?","hint":"Updates are pushed once a month whenever the device is connected.","keys":["once a month","pushed","connected"]}]}},"sc-01":{"intro":"Klinik çalışmanın tasarımını edilgen yapılarla, bilimsel ama anlaşılır bir dille anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"en":"Before we could apply for certification, we had to show that our device performs as reliably as a trained audiologist.","tr":"Sertifikaya başvurabilmek için cihazımızın eğitimli bir odyolog kadar güvenilir çalıştığını göstermemiz gerekiyordu."},{"en":"To do this, a clinical study was designed together with two university hospitals.","tr":"Bunun için iki üniversite hastanesiyle birlikte bir klinik çalışma tasarlandı."},{"en":"Our hypothesis was that the two methods would agree in at least 90 percent of cases.","tr":"Hipotezimiz, iki yöntemin vakaların en az yüzde 90'ında aynı sonucu vereceğiydi."},{"en":"A total of 200 participants, aged between 18 and 75, were recruited for the study.","tr":"Çalışmaya 18 ile 75 yaş arasında toplam 200 katılımcı dahil edildi."},{"en":"Each of them was tested twice on the same day, once by our device and once by an audiologist.","tr":"Her biri aynı gün iki kez test edildi: bir kez cihazımızla, bir kez de bir odyolog tarafından."},{"en":"Crucially, the audiologist was not shown the device's results, which made it a blind comparison.","tr":"En önemlisi, odyoloğa cihazın sonuçları gösterilmedi; bu da karşılaştırmayı kör hale getirdi."},{"en":"This mattered because it meant the expert's judgement couldn't be influenced by our data.","tr":"Bu önemliydi, çünkü uzmanın değerlendirmesinin bizim verilerimizden etkilenemeyeceği anlamına geliyordu."},{"en":"As it turned out, the results matched in 94 percent of cases, which comfortably exceeded our target.","tr":"Sonuçta sonuçlar vakaların yüzde 94'ünde eşleşti ve bu, hedefimizi rahatça aştı."},{"en":"In the remaining 6 percent, the differences were minor and none of them changed the diagnosis.","tr":"Kalan yüzde 6'daki farklar küçüktü ve hiçbiri teşhisi değiştirmedi."},{"en":"The findings were published in a medical journal last spring.","tr":"Bulgular geçen bahar bir tıp dergisinde yayımlandı."}],"vocab":[{"en":"perform reliably","tr":"güvenilir şekilde çalışmak","ex":"The device performs as reliably as an expert.","def":"to work well and give the same good results every time"},{"en":"design a study","tr":"bir çalışma tasarlamak","ex":"The study was designed with two university hospitals.","def":"to plan how a study will be done"},{"en":"recruit","tr":"(katılımcı) toplamak, dahil etmek","ex":"200 participants were recruited for the study.","def":"to find people to take part in something"},{"en":"blind comparison","tr":"kör karşılaştırma","ex":"Because the audiologist didn't see our data, it was a blind comparison.","def":"a comparison where one side does not know the other side's result"},{"en":"be influenced by","tr":"...den etkilenmek","ex":"The expert's judgement couldn't be influenced by our data.","def":"to be changed or affected by something"},{"en":"as it turned out","tr":"sonuçta, meğerse","ex":"As it turned out, the results matched in 94 percent of cases.","def":"used to say what finally happened"},{"en":"exceed a target","tr":"hedefi aşmak","ex":"The results comfortably exceeded our target.","def":"to do better than the goal you set"},{"en":"the remaining","tr":"geri kalan","ex":"In the remaining 6 percent, the differences were minor.","def":"the part that is left"},{"en":"findings","tr":"bulgular","ex":"The findings were published last spring.","def":"the results or information discovered by a study"}],"grammar":{"title":"Passive voice: was designed, were recruited","tr":"Bilimsel metinlerde işi kimin yaptığından çok yapılan iş önemlidir; bu yüzden edilgen yapı kullanılır: be + fiilin üçüncü hali (was designed, were published).","examples":["A clinical study was designed with two hospitals.","200 participants were recruited.","The audiologist was not shown the device's results."]},"questions":[{"q":"What did the company have to show before applying for certification?","options":["That the device is cheaper than an audiologist","That the device performs as reliably as an audiologist","That patients prefer the device"],"a":1},{"q":"How many participants were recruited?","options":["100","150","200","250"],"a":2},{"q":"Why was it important that the audiologist didn't see the device's results?","options":["So that the expert's judgement couldn't be influenced","To save time","Because the results were secret"],"a":0},{"q":"What can we infer about the 94 percent result?","options":["It was below the hypothesis","It was higher than the team needed","It was exactly what they expected"],"a":1},{"q":"What was true of the remaining 6 percent?","options":["The device gave no result","Patients had to be retested","The differences were minor and didn't change the diagnosis"],"a":2}],"gaps":[{"s":"A total of 200 participants were ___ for the study.","a":"recruited","hint":"dahil edildi"},{"s":"The results comfortably ___ our target.","a":"exceeded","hint":"aştı"},{"s":"The ___ were published in a medical journal last spring.","a":"findings","hint":"bulgular"}],"order":[{"a":"Each of them was tested twice on the same day."},{"a":"The findings were published in a medical journal."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Çalışma iki üniversite hastanesiyle birlikte tasarlandı.","en":"The study was designed together with two university hospitals.","keys":["was designed","university hospitals"]},{"tr":"Odyoloğa cihazın sonuçları gösterilmedi.","en":"The audiologist was not shown the device's results.","keys":["was not shown","results"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"University researcher","personaTr":"Üniversite araştırmacısı","scene":"Makalenizi okuyan bir araştırmacı çalışmanın tasarımını ve güvenilirliğini sorguluyor.","turns":[{"ai":"I've read your paper with interest. Could you summarise how the study was designed?","aiTr":"Makalenizi ilgiyle okudum. Çalışmanın nasıl tasarlandığını özetleyebilir misiniz?","hint":"Sure. It was designed with two university hospitals, and 200 participants aged 18 to 75 were recruited.","keys":["designed","two university hospitals","200 participants"]},{"ai":"How did you make sure the audiologists weren't biased?","aiTr":"Odyologların taraflı olmadığından nasıl emin oldunuz?","hint":"It was a blind comparison, so the audiologist was never shown the device's results.","keys":["blind comparison","never shown","results"]},{"ai":"And how did the results compare with your hypothesis?","aiTr":"Peki sonuçlar hipotezinizle nasıl karşılaştırılıyor?","hint":"We expected at least 90 percent agreement, and the results matched in 94 percent of cases.","keys":["90 percent","94 percent","matched"]},{"ai":"What happened in the cases where they didn't match?","aiTr":"Eşleşmeyen vakalarda ne oldu?","hint":"The differences were minor, and none of them changed the diagnosis.","keys":["minor","diagnosis"]}]}},"te-02":{"intro":"Bir yatırımcıyla yaptığın konuşmayı aktararak yapay zekâ ile yazılan kodu nasıl denetlediğinizi anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"en":"When we started, every line of our code was written by hand by our three engineers.","tr":"Başladığımızda kodumuzun her satırı üç mühendisimiz tarafından elle yazılıyordu."},{"en":"These days, a large share of our first drafts is generated by AI coding assistants.","tr":"Bugünlerde ilk taslaklarımızın büyük bir kısmı yapay zekâ kod asistanları tarafından üretiliyor."},{"en":"An engineer describes the task in plain English, and the assistant proposes an implementation.","tr":"Bir mühendis görevi sade bir İngilizceyle anlatıyor, asistan da bir uygulama öneriyor."},{"en":"It's also surprisingly good at explaining unfamiliar code and spotting bugs that a tired human might miss.","tr":"Ayrıca yabancı kodu açıklamakta ve yorgun bir insanın gözden kaçırabileceği hataları fark etmekte şaşırtıcı derecede iyi."},{"en":"As a result, features that used to take a week are often finished in a day or two.","tr":"Sonuç olarak eskiden bir hafta süren özellikler çoğu zaman bir iki günde bitiyor."},{"en":"Last month, an investor asked me whether we trusted code that a machine had written.","tr":"Geçen ay bir yatırımcı bana bir makinenin yazdığı koda güvenip güvenmediğimizi sordu."},{"en":"I told her that we didn't trust it blindly, because AI code can look correct and still hide subtle problems.","tr":"Ona körü körüne güvenmediğimizi söyledim, çünkü yapay zekâ kodu doğru görünüp yine de ince sorunlar barındırabilir."},{"en":"Since our software runs on a medical device, every change is reviewed by a human and checked by automated tests before it's deployed.","tr":"Yazılımımız bir tıbbi cihazda çalıştığı için her değişiklik canlıya alınmadan önce bir insan tarafından incelenip otomatik testlerle kontrol ediliyor."},{"en":"Our lead engineer once told me that the assistant had suggested a fix that would have broken the audiogram calculation.","tr":"Baş mühendisimiz bir keresinde asistanın, odyogram hesaplamasını bozacak bir düzeltme önerdiğini anlatmıştı."},{"en":"It was caught in review, which is exactly why we never skip that step.","tr":"Hata incelemede yakalandı; o adımı asla atlamamamızın sebebi de tam olarak bu."},{"en":"I'd say these tools are like having three extra engineers, which is a huge difference for a six-person startup.","tr":"Bence bu araçlar üç ekstra mühendis gibi; altı kişilik bir girişim için bu çok büyük bir fark."}],"vocab":[{"en":"first draft","tr":"ilk taslak","ex":"The assistant writes most of our first drafts.","def":"the first version of something, which will be improved later"},{"en":"generate","tr":"üretmek","ex":"Much of our code is generated by AI.","def":"to produce or create something"},{"en":"propose an implementation","tr":"bir uygulama önermek","ex":"The assistant proposes an implementation in seconds.","def":"to suggest a way of building a feature in code"},{"en":"spot a bug","tr":"bir hatayı fark etmek","ex":"It's good at spotting bugs that humans miss.","def":"to notice an error in code"},{"en":"trust something blindly","tr":"bir şeye körü körüne güvenmek","ex":"We don't trust AI code blindly.","def":"to trust something without checking it"},{"en":"subtle","tr":"ince, fark edilmesi zor","ex":"The code had a subtle problem.","def":"small and difficult to notice"},{"en":"automated tests","tr":"otomatik testler","ex":"Every change is checked by automated tests.","def":"programs that check code automatically"},{"en":"deploy","tr":"canlıya almak","ex":"Nothing is deployed without a review.","def":"to release software so that people can use it"},{"en":"skip a step","tr":"bir adımı atlamak","ex":"We never skip the review step.","def":"to leave out one part of a process"}],"grammar":{"title":"Reported speech: told / asked","tr":"Birinin söylediğini aktarırken zaman genellikle bir adım geriye kayar: trust → trusted, has written → had written. Soru aktarırken 'whether' ya da 'if' kullanılır ve soru düzeni bozulur.","examples":["An investor asked me whether we trusted code that a machine had written.","I told her that we didn't trust it blindly.","Our lead engineer told me that the assistant had suggested a fix."]},"questions":[{"q":"Who produces most of the first drafts today?","options":["The investors","AI coding assistants","External freelancers"],"a":1},{"q":"What did the founder tell the investor?","options":["That they trust AI code completely","That they don't use AI at all","That they don't trust AI code blindly"],"a":2},{"q":"Why is every change reviewed and tested?","options":["Because the software runs on a medical device","Because investors require it","Because the engineers are new"],"a":0},{"q":"What does the story about the audiogram calculation suggest?","options":["The assistant is useless","Human review can catch serious errors that AI introduces","The audiogram calculation is not important","The engineers made the mistake"],"a":1},{"q":"Why does the founder compare the tools to 'three extra engineers'?","options":["Because they cost the same as three salaries","Because they will replace the current engineers","Because they give a small team much more capacity"],"a":2}],"gaps":[{"s":"A large share of our first drafts is ___ by AI coding assistants.","a":"generated","hint":"üretilmek"},{"s":"An investor asked me ___ we trusted code that a machine had written.","a":"whether","hint":"-ip -mediğini"},{"s":"It was caught in review, which is exactly why we never ___ that step.","a":"skip","hint":"atlamak"}],"order":[{"a":"Every change is reviewed by a human."},{"a":"It was caught in review."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Bir yatırımcı bana bir makinenin yazdığı koda güvenip güvenmediğimizi sordu.","en":"An investor asked me whether we trusted code that a machine had written.","keys":["asked me whether","had written"]},{"tr":"Ona körü körüne güvenmediğimizi söyledim.","en":"I told her that we didn't trust it blindly.","keys":["told her","trust it blindly"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Tech investor","personaTr":"Teknoloji yatırımcısı","scene":"Bir teknoloji yatırımcısı, yapay zekâyla yazılan kodun bir tıbbi cihazda ne kadar güvenli olduğunu sorguluyor.","turns":[{"ai":"I've heard you build most of your software with AI. Is that true?","aiTr":"Yazılımınızın çoğunu yapay zekâyla geliştirdiğinizi duydum. Doğru mu?","hint":"Partly. A large share of our first drafts is generated by AI coding assistants, but our engineers review everything.","keys":["first drafts","generated","review"]},{"ai":"Do you trust code that a machine has written?","aiTr":"Bir makinenin yazdığı koda güveniyor musunuz?","hint":"Not blindly. AI code can look correct and still hide subtle problems, so every change is reviewed by a human and checked by automated tests.","keys":["blindly","subtle","automated tests","reviewed"]},{"ai":"Has the review process ever actually caught anything?","aiTr":"İnceleme süreci gerçekten hiç bir şey yakaladı mı?","hint":"Yes. Our lead engineer told me that the assistant had suggested a fix that would have broken the audiogram calculation.","keys":["told me","audiogram","broken"]},{"ai":"What would happen if you stopped using these tools?","aiTr":"Bu araçları kullanmayı bıraksaydınız ne olurdu?","hint":"If we stopped, we'd probably need three more engineers, which is a lot for a six-person startup.","keys":["three more engineers","six-person","we'd"]}]}},"sc-02":{"intro":"Hibe sürecini edilgen yapılarla anlatıyor, hibenin yatırımcı parasına göre avantajını tartışıyorsun.","text":[{"en":"It's easy to forget that not all startup funding comes from investors; grants can play a major role too.","tr":"Girişim finansmanının hepsinin yatırımcılardan gelmediğini unutmak kolay; hibeler de büyük rol oynayabilir."},{"en":"Unlike an investment, a grant doesn't have to be paid back, and no equity is given away.","tr":"Yatırımın aksine hibenin geri ödenmesi gerekmez ve hiç hisse verilmez."},{"en":"Last year, we applied for a European innovation grant aimed at health technology projects.","tr":"Geçen yıl sağlık teknolojisi projelerine yönelik bir Avrupa inovasyon hibesine başvurduk."},{"en":"The application was demanding: we were asked to describe the problem, our solution, the team and a detailed budget.","tr":"Başvuru zahmetliydi: sorunu, çözümümüzü, ekibi ve ayrıntılı bir bütçeyi anlatmamız istendi."},{"en":"We also had to demonstrate the impact, in other words how many people would benefit from our device.","tr":"Ayrıca etkiyi, yani cihazımızdan kaç kişinin fayda göreceğini kanıtlamamız gerekiyordu."},{"en":"This was where our numbers helped, since roughly one in five people has some degree of hearing loss.","tr":"Burada rakamlarımız işimize yaradı, çünkü yaklaşık her beş kişiden birinde bir derece işitme kaybı var."},{"en":"The review process took four months, after which we were invited to present to a jury.","tr":"Değerlendirme süreci dört ay sürdü; ardından bir jüriye sunum yapmaya davet edildik."},{"en":"We were eventually awarded 250,000 euros, which can only be spent on research and clinical validation.","tr":"Sonunda bize 250.000 euro verildi; bu para yalnızca araştırma ve klinik doğrulama için harcanabiliyor."},{"en":"If we had relied on investors alone, we would have given away far more equity at a much earlier stage.","tr":"Sadece yatırımcılara güvenseydik, çok daha erken bir aşamada çok daha fazla hisse vermiş olurduk."},{"en":"Grants are slow and time-consuming, but I'd say they're one of the best ways to fund early-stage research.","tr":"Hibeler yavaş ve zaman alıcıdır, ama bence erken aşama araştırmayı finanse etmenin en iyi yollarından biridir."}],"vocab":[{"en":"play a major role","tr":"büyük rol oynamak","ex":"Grants can play a major role in early funding.","def":"to be very important in a situation"},{"en":"give away equity","tr":"hisse vermek","ex":"With a grant, no equity is given away.","def":"to give part of your company's ownership to someone"},{"en":"aimed at","tr":"...e yönelik","ex":"The grant is aimed at health technology projects.","def":"intended for a particular group or purpose"},{"en":"demanding","tr":"zahmetli, zorlu","ex":"The application was demanding.","def":"needing a lot of time, effort or skill"},{"en":"demonstrate the impact","tr":"etkiyi kanıtlamak","ex":"We had to demonstrate the impact of our device.","def":"to show clearly what effect something will have"},{"en":"be awarded","tr":"(hibe, ödül) verilmek","ex":"We were awarded 250,000 euros.","def":"to be officially given money or a prize"},{"en":"rely on","tr":"...e dayanmak, güvenmek","ex":"We didn't want to rely on investors alone.","def":"to depend on someone or something"},{"en":"time-consuming","tr":"zaman alıcı","ex":"Grant applications are time-consuming.","def":"taking a lot of time"},{"en":"early-stage","tr":"erken aşama","ex":"Grants are ideal for early-stage research.","def":"at the beginning of development"}],"grammar":{"title":"Passive voice with modals: doesn't have to be paid back, can be spent","tr":"Edilgen yapı modal fiillerle de kullanılır: modal + be + fiilin üçüncü hali (can be spent, has to be paid back). Kuralları ve koşulları resmi biçimde anlatmak için idealdir.","examples":["A grant doesn't have to be paid back.","The money can only be spent on research.","We were asked to describe a detailed budget."]},"questions":[{"q":"According to the text, how is a grant different from an investment?","options":["It must be repaid within a year","It doesn't have to be paid back and no equity is given away","It is only available to large companies"],"a":1},{"q":"Why did the hearing-loss figure help the application?","options":["It showed the device's potential impact","It reduced the budget","It shortened the review"],"a":0},{"q":"What happened after the four-month review?","options":["They received the money straight away","They were asked to reapply","They were invited to present to a jury"],"a":2},{"q":"What can we infer about the founder's view of investor funding?","options":["They want to avoid investors entirely","They think investors are too slow","They want to sell the company","They value grants because they protect equity early on"],"a":3},{"q":"What can the 250,000 euros be spent on?","options":["Marketing","Research and clinical validation","Office rent"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"Unlike an investment, a grant doesn't have to be paid ___.","a":"back","hint":"geri"},{"s":"We also had to ___ the impact of our device.","a":"demonstrate","hint":"kanıtlamak"},{"s":"We were eventually ___ 250,000 euros.","a":"awarded","hint":"verildi"}],"order":[{"a":"Grants can play a major role too."},{"a":"We were invited to present to a jury."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Hiç hisse verilmez.","en":"No equity is given away.","keys":["equity","given away"]},{"tr":"Değerlendirme süreci dört ay sürdü.","en":"The review process took four months.","keys":["review process","four months"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Grant jury member","personaTr":"Hibe jürisi üyesi","scene":"Jüri karşısındasın. Etkiyi, bütçeyi ve neden yatırımcı yerine hibe istediğini savunuyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"Thanks for coming in. In a nutshell, what impact would your project have?","aiTr":"Geldiğiniz için teşekkürler. Kısaca projenizin etkisi ne olur?","hint":"Roughly one in five people has some hearing loss, yet most are never tested, so our device could reach millions of people.","keys":["one in five","never tested","millions"]},{"ai":"The budget is quite large. How exactly would the money be spent?","aiTr":"Bütçe oldukça büyük. Para tam olarak nasıl harcanacak?","hint":"It would be spent on research and clinical validation, which is exactly what's needed before certification.","keys":["research","clinical validation","certification"]},{"ai":"Wouldn't it be easier to raise this money from investors?","aiTr":"Bu parayı yatırımcılardan toplamak daha kolay olmaz mıydı?","hint":"Possibly, but if we relied only on investors, we would have to give away a lot of equity at a very early stage.","keys":["give away","equity","early stage"]},{"ai":"And why are you the right team to deliver this?","aiTr":"Peki bu işi başaracak doğru ekip neden sizsiniz?","hint":"We've already built a working prototype, and the team combines engineering, medical and business skills.","keys":["prototype","engineering","medical"]}]}},"ai-04":{"intro":"Bir yatırımcıya onaylanmış kuruluşu, klinik kanıtı ve sertifikasyonun en büyük riskini açıklıyorsun.","text":[{"en":"No medical device can be placed on the European market until it has been certified.","tr":"Hiçbir tıbbi cihaz sertifika almadan Avrupa pazarına sürülemez."},{"en":"For us, that means getting the CE mark first, with FDA approval for the US following later.","tr":"Bizim için bu, önce CE işaretini almak, ABD için FDA onayının da ardından gelmesi demek."},{"en":"Our audiometer is classified as Class IIa, which is the medium-risk category under EU rules.","tr":"Odyometremiz, AB kurallarına göre orta risk kategorisi olan Sınıf IIa olarak sınıflandırılıyor."},{"en":"Because of that, it has to be assessed by an independent organization known as a notified body.","tr":"Bu nedenle, onaylanmış kuruluş denen bağımsız bir kurum tarafından değerlendirilmesi gerekiyor."},{"en":"The key requirement is clinical evidence, in other words proof that the device is safe and does what we claim.","tr":"Temel şart klinik kanıt, yani cihazın güvenli olduğunun ve iddia ettiğimiz şeyi yaptığının kanıtı."},{"en":"Our study, which was carried out at two university hospitals, compared our results with those of a trained audiologist.","tr":"İki üniversite hastanesinde yürütülen çalışmamız, sonuçlarımızı eğitimli bir odyoloğun sonuçlarıyla karşılaştırdı."},{"en":"The results matched in 94% of cases, and the small differences in the rest didn't change the diagnosis.","tr":"Sonuçlar vakaların %94'ünde eşleşti; geri kalanlardaki küçük farklar teşhisi değiştirmedi."},{"en":"On top of that, we're required to run a quality management system and keep detailed technical documentation.","tr":"Bunun yanında bir kalite yönetim sistemi işletmemiz ve ayrıntılı teknik dokümantasyon tutmamız gerekiyor."},{"en":"Our regulatory consultant, who has guided several similar devices through the process, says we're on track.","tr":"Benzer birkaç cihazı bu süreçten geçirmiş olan mevzuat danışmanımız, doğru yolda olduğumuzu söylüyor."},{"en":"I'd say the biggest risk is time, because certification often takes longer than planned.","tr":"Bence en büyük risk zaman, çünkü sertifikasyon çoğu zaman planlanandan uzun sürüyor."},{"en":"If it were up to us, we'd be on the market tomorrow, but realistically we're aiming for the end of next year.","tr":"Bize kalsa yarın piyasada olurduk ama gerçekçi olmak gerekirse gelecek yılın sonunu hedefliyoruz."}],"vocab":[{"en":"place on the market","tr":"piyasaya sürmek","ex":"A device cannot be placed on the market without the CE mark.","def":"to make a product available for sale for the first time"},{"en":"be classified as","tr":"...olarak sınıflandırılmak","ex":"Our audiometer is classified as Class IIa.","def":"to be officially put into a group or category"},{"en":"notified body","tr":"onaylanmış kuruluş","ex":"A notified body has to assess our device.","def":"an independent organization that checks medical devices for EU certification"},{"en":"clinical evidence","tr":"klinik kanıt","ex":"The notified body will look closely at our clinical evidence.","def":"data from studies with patients that shows a device is safe and works"},{"en":"carry out a study","tr":"çalışma yürütmek","ex":"We carried out the study at two university hospitals.","def":"to do a piece of research"},{"en":"technical documentation","tr":"teknik dokümantasyon","ex":"We keep detailed technical documentation for every version of the device.","def":"detailed documents that describe how a product is designed, built and tested"},{"en":"be on track","tr":"doğru yolda olmak, plana uygun ilerlemek","ex":"Our consultant says we're on track.","def":"to be making the progress you expected"},{"en":"take longer than planned","tr":"planlanandan uzun sürmek","ex":"Certification often takes longer than planned.","def":"to need more time than you expected"},{"en":"aim for","tr":"hedeflemek","ex":"We're aiming for the end of next year.","def":"to try to achieve a particular result or date"}],"grammar":{"title":"The passive in regulatory language","tr":"Passive (be + V3), işi kimin yaptığı değil işin kendisi önemli olduğunda kullanılır. Resmî ve mevzuat dilinde çok yaygındır; yapan kişi gerekirse 'by' ile eklenir.","examples":["Our audiometer is classified as Class IIa.","It has to be assessed by a notified body.","The study was carried out at two university hospitals."]},"questions":[{"q":"Why does the audiometer need to be assessed by a notified body?","options":["Because it will be sold in the US","Because it is a Class IIa device","Because the study was small"],"a":1},{"q":"What happened in the 6% of cases where the results were different?","options":["The diagnosis changed","The patients were tested again","The differences were small and didn't change the diagnosis"],"a":2},{"q":"What does the consultant think?","options":["The company is on track","The company should give up","The study must be repeated"],"a":0},{"q":"What can we infer about the founder's attitude to the timeline?","options":["They are sure it will finish early","They are hopeful but realistic about possible delays","They don't care about the deadline","They think FDA approval comes first"],"a":1},{"q":"Which market does the company want to enter first?","options":["The United States","Asia","South America","Europe"],"a":3}],"gaps":[{"s":"Our audiometer is ___ as Class IIa.","a":"classified","hint":"sınıflandırılmak"},{"s":"It has to be assessed by a notified ___.","a":"body","hint":"kuruluş"},{"s":"Certification often takes longer than ___.","a":"planned","hint":"planlanan"}],"order":[{"a":"The study was carried out at two university hospitals."},{"a":"Our consultant says we are on track."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Cihazımız Sınıf IIa olarak sınıflandırılıyor.","en":"Our device is classified as Class IIa.","keys":["classified as","Class IIa"]},{"tr":"Bence en büyük risk zaman.","en":"I'd say the biggest risk is time.","keys":["I'd say","biggest risk"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Investor","personaTr":"Yatırımcı (durum tespiti)","scene":"Bir yatırımcı yatırım öncesi incelemede sertifikasyon sürecini ve risklerini soruyor.","turns":[{"ai":"What exactly stands between you and the European market?","aiTr":"Sizinle Avrupa pazarı arasında tam olarak ne var?","hint":"The CE mark. Our device is classified as Class IIa, so it has to be assessed by a notified body.","keys":["CE mark","Class IIa","notified body"]},{"ai":"How strong is your clinical evidence?","aiTr":"Klinik kanıtınız ne kadar güçlü?","hint":"Quite strong, I'd say. Our study at two university hospitals matched a trained audiologist in 94% of cases.","keys":["94","study","matched"]},{"ai":"What's the biggest risk in the process?","aiTr":"Süreçteki en büyük risk ne?","hint":"Time. Certification often takes longer than planned, but our consultant says we're on track.","keys":["takes longer","on track","time"]},{"ai":"If the CE mark were delayed by six months, what would you do?","aiTr":"CE işareti altı ay gecikseydi ne yapardınız?","hint":"If that happened, we would keep our costs low and use the funding to cover the extra months.","keys":["would","costs","funding"]}]}},"st-03":{"intro":"Doğrudan satış ile distribütör arasındaki kararı, gerekçeleri ve ekibin görüşleriyle birlikte anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"en":"Last month, we were faced with one of the toughest calls we've had to make so far.","tr":"Geçen ay şimdiye kadar vermek zorunda kaldığımız en zor kararlardan biriyle karşı karşıya kaldık."},{"en":"The question was whether to sell our device directly to hospitals or to hand sales over to a distributor that already knows the market.","tr":"Soru, cihazımızı doğrudan hastanelere mi satacağımız, yoksa satışı pazarı zaten bilen bir distribütöre mi devredeceğimizdi."},{"en":"Selling directly would have given us better margins, but it would also have meant building a sales team from scratch.","tr":"Doğrudan satış bize daha iyi kâr marjları sağlardı ama aynı zamanda sıfırdan bir satış ekibi kurmak anlamına gelirdi."},{"en":"The distributor, on the other hand, would take a 20% commission, which seemed like a lot at first.","tr":"Öte yandan distribütör yüzde 20 komisyon alacaktı ve bu ilk başta fazla gibi görünüyordu."},{"en":"What they offered in return was something we couldn't build ourselves: established relationships with hospitals and clinics.","tr":"Karşılığında sundukları şey kendi başımıza kuramayacağımız bir şeydi: hastaneler ve kliniklerle oturmuş ilişkiler."},{"en":"The pros and cons were debated for two weeks, and everyone on the team was asked for their view.","tr":"Artılar ve eksiler iki hafta boyunca tartışıldı ve ekipteki herkesin görüşü soruldu."},{"en":"Our engineers said they would rather focus on the product than spend their days on sales calls.","tr":"Mühendislerimiz günlerini satış görüşmeleriyle geçirmektense ürüne odaklanmayı tercih ettiklerini söylediler."},{"en":"I'd say that was what tipped the balance in the end.","tr":"Bence sonunda dengeyi değiştiren de bu oldu."},{"en":"If we had unlimited time and money, I'd probably sell directly, but we simply don't.","tr":"Sınırsız zamanımız ve paramız olsaydı muhtemelen doğrudan satardım ama ne yazık ki yok."},{"en":"For a startup, speed matters more than margin, and a bigger player could easily get there first.","tr":"Bir girişim için hız kâr marjından daha önemli ve daha büyük bir oyuncu kolayca bizden önce davranabilir."},{"en":"It wasn't an easy decision, but I'm fairly confident it was the right one.","tr":"Kolay bir karar değildi ama doğru olduğundan oldukça eminim."}],"vocab":[{"en":"a tough call","tr":"zor bir karar","ex":"It was one of the toughest calls we've had to make.","def":"a difficult decision"},{"en":"hand over","tr":"devretmek","ex":"We decided to hand sales over to a distributor.","def":"to give responsibility for something to someone else"},{"en":"margin","tr":"kâr marjı","ex":"Selling directly would give us better margins.","def":"the difference between what something costs and what you sell it for"},{"en":"from scratch","tr":"sıfırdan","ex":"We'd have to build a sales team from scratch.","def":"from the very beginning, with nothing"},{"en":"commission","tr":"komisyon","ex":"The distributor takes a 20% commission.","def":"a percentage of each sale paid to the seller"},{"en":"established relationships","tr":"oturmuş ilişkiler","ex":"They have established relationships with hospitals.","def":"business connections that have existed for a long time"},{"en":"would rather","tr":"-meyi tercih etmek","ex":"Our engineers would rather focus on the product.","def":"would prefer to"},{"en":"tip the balance","tr":"dengeyi değiştirmek, belirleyici olmak","ex":"That was what tipped the balance.","def":"to be the factor that decides the result"},{"en":"get there first","tr":"önce davranmak, ilk varmak","ex":"A bigger player could get there first.","def":"to do or reach something before your competitors"}],"grammar":{"title":"Second conditional: imagining a different situation","tr":"'If + past simple, would + fiil' ile gerçek olmayan ya da düşük ihtimalli durumları hayal ederiz. Burada aslında olmayan bir durumu anlatıyor: sınırsız zaman ve para.","examples":["If we had unlimited time and money, I'd probably sell directly.","If we sold directly, we'd need a big sales team."]},"questions":[{"q":"What was the main disadvantage of selling directly?","options":["Lower margins","Building a sales team from scratch","Losing the engineers"],"a":1},{"q":"What did the distributor offer in return for the commission?","options":["Established relationships with hospitals and clinics","A lower price for the device","Free marketing"],"a":0},{"q":"What did the engineers say?","options":["They wanted to make sales calls","They wanted higher salaries","They'd rather focus on the product"],"a":2},{"q":"Why does the speaker add 'but we simply don't'?","options":["To show that direct sales are illegal","To admit the company lacks the time and money to sell directly","To complain about the distributor"],"a":1},{"q":"How does the speaker feel about the decision now?","options":["Fairly confident it was right","Sure it was a mistake","Completely indifferent"],"a":0}],"gaps":[{"s":"It would have meant building a sales team from ___.","a":"scratch","hint":"sıfırdan"},{"s":"The distributor would take a 20% ___.","a":"commission","hint":"komisyon"},{"s":"I'd say that was what tipped the ___ in the end.","a":"balance","hint":"denge"}],"order":[{"a":"For a startup speed matters more than margin."},{"a":"The pros and cons were debated for two weeks."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Sınırsız zamanımız ve paramız olsaydı muhtemelen doğrudan satardım.","en":"If we had unlimited time and money, I'd probably sell directly.","keys":["unlimited time and money","sell directly"]},{"tr":"Mühendislerimiz ürüne odaklanmayı tercih ettiklerini söylediler.","en":"Our engineers said they would rather focus on the product.","keys":["would rather","focus on the product"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Co-founder","personaTr":"Kurucu ortak","scene":"Kurucu ortağın kararı hâlâ sorguluyor ve neden distribütörü seçtiğinizi tekrar konuşmak istiyor.","turns":[{"ai":"Honestly, I still think we'd make more money selling directly.","aiTr":"Açıkçası, doğrudan satarak daha çok para kazanacağımızı hâlâ düşünüyorum.","hint":"You're right about the margins, but it would mean building a sales team from scratch.","keys":["margins","from scratch","sales team"]},{"ai":"A 20% commission is a lot, though, isn't it?","aiTr":"Ama yüzde 20 komisyon çok fazla, değil mi?","hint":"It seemed like a lot at first, but what they offer in return is established relationships with hospitals and clinics.","keys":["established relationships","in return","hospitals"]},{"ai":"What did the rest of the team think?","aiTr":"Ekibin geri kalanı ne düşündü?","hint":"Our engineers said they would rather focus on the product than spend their days on sales calls.","keys":["engineers said","would rather","product"]},{"ai":"So, if you had to sum it up, why the distributor?","aiTr":"Peki özetlemen gerekse, neden distribütör?","hint":"For a startup, speed matters more than margin, and a bigger player could easily get there first.","keys":["speed","margin","get there first"]}]}},"li-01":{"intro":"Pasaport kontrolünde ve otelde dolaylı sorularla, daha akıcı ve kibar konuşuyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Officer","en":"Good morning, could you tell me the purpose of your visit?","tr":"Günaydın, ziyaretinizin amacını söyleyebilir misiniz?"},{"who":"Me","en":"I'm here on business, attending a conference on medical technology.","tr":"İş için buradayım; medikal teknoloji üzerine bir konferansa katılıyorum."},{"who":"Officer","en":"And how long do you intend to stay in the country?","tr":"Peki ülkede ne kadar kalmayı düşünüyorsunuz?"},{"who":"Me","en":"Only four days, as I'm flying back on Friday.","tr":"Sadece dört gün, çünkü cuma günü dönüyorum."},{"who":"Officer","en":"Everything seems to be in order, so enjoy your stay.","tr":"Her şey yolunda görünüyor; iyi konaklamalar."},{"who":"Me","en":"Hi, I believe there's a reservation under the name {name}.","tr":"Merhaba, sanırım {name} adına bir rezervasyon var."},{"who":"Receptionist","en":"Yes, I've found it, so could I just see your passport, please?","tr":"Evet, buldum; pasaportunuzu bir görebilir miyim, lütfen?"},{"who":"Me","en":"Here you are, and could you tell me whether breakfast is included?","tr":"Buyurun; kahvaltının dahil olup olmadığını söyleyebilir misiniz?"},{"who":"Receptionist","en":"It is, and it's served from 7 to 10 every morning.","tr":"Dahil; her sabah 7'den 10'a kadar servis ediliyor."},{"who":"Receptionist","en":"You're in room 512 on the fifth floor, and this is your key card.","tr":"Beşinci kattaki 512 numaralı odadasınız, bu da anahtar kartınız."},{"who":"Me","en":"Great, and would you mind telling me the wifi password?","tr":"Harika; wifi şifresini söyler misiniz, rica etsem?"}],"vocab":[{"en":"be here on business","tr":"iş için burada olmak","ex":"I'm here on business this week.","def":"to be visiting a place for work"},{"en":"intend to","tr":"...mayı düşünmek, niyetinde olmak","ex":"How long do you intend to stay?","def":"to plan to do something"},{"en":"be in order","tr":"usulüne uygun olmak, yolunda olmak","ex":"Everything seems to be in order.","def":"to be correct and as it should be"},{"en":"I believe there's...","tr":"sanırım ... var","ex":"I believe there's a reservation under my name.","def":"a polite, slightly careful way to say that something exists"},{"en":"reservation under the name","tr":"... adına rezervasyon","ex":"There's a reservation under the name {name}.","def":"a booking saved with a person's name"},{"en":"whether","tr":"-ip -mediğini","ex":"Could you tell me whether breakfast is included?","def":"used to talk about a choice between two possibilities, like 'if'"},{"en":"be served","tr":"servis edilmek","ex":"Breakfast is served from 7 to 10.","def":"to be given to guests to eat or drink"},{"en":"key card","tr":"anahtar kart","ex":"This is your key card for room 512.","def":"a plastic card used to open a hotel room"},{"en":"Would you mind + -ing?","tr":"...ebilir misiniz, rica etsem?","ex":"Would you mind telling me the wifi password?","def":"a very polite way to ask someone to do something"}],"grammar":{"title":"Indirect questions: Could you tell me whether...?","tr":"Dolaylı sorular daha kibardır. 'Could you tell me...' ya da 'Would you mind telling me...' ile başlar; ardından gelen kısımda soru düzeni bozulur ve normal cümle sırası kullanılır (whether breakfast is included).","examples":["Could you tell me whether breakfast is included?","Could you tell me the purpose of your visit?","Would you mind telling me the wifi password?"]},"questions":[{"q":"What is the purpose of the speaker's trip?","options":["Tourism","A medical technology conference","A job interview"],"a":1},{"q":"Why is the speaker staying only four days?","options":["The hotel is full","The conference is cancelled","They are flying back on Friday"],"a":2},{"q":"What does \"Everything seems to be in order\" suggest?","options":["The officer is satisfied with the answers","There is a problem with the passport","The speaker must wait for a second check"],"a":0},{"q":"Where is room 512?","options":["On the ground floor","On the fifth floor","Next to the restaurant"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"Could you tell me ___ breakfast is included?","a":"whether","hint":"-ip -mediğini"},{"s":"Breakfast is ___ from 7 to 10.","a":"served","hint":"servis ediliyor"},{"s":"Would you mind ___ me the wifi password?","a":"telling","hint":"söylemek"}],"order":[{"a":"Everything seems to be in order."},{"a":"I'm flying back on Friday."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Kahvaltının dahil olup olmadığını söyleyebilir misiniz?","en":"Could you tell me whether breakfast is included?","keys":["whether","breakfast","included"]},{"tr":"Sanırım {name} adına bir rezervasyon var.","en":"I believe there's a reservation under the name {name}.","keys":["I believe","reservation"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Hotel receptionist","personaTr":"Otel resepsiyonisti","scene":"Berlin'de uzun bir günün sonunda otele giriş yapıyorsun; kibar ve dolaylı sorular soruyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"Good evening! You must have had a long day. Are you checking in?","aiTr":"İyi akşamlar! Uzun bir gün geçirmiş olmalısınız. Giriş mi yapıyorsunuz?","hint":"Yes, I believe there's a reservation under the name {name}.","keys":["reservation","under the name","believe"]},{"ai":"Here it is. Could I take a quick copy of your passport?","aiTr":"İşte burada. Pasaportunuzun hızlıca bir kopyasını alabilir miyim?","hint":"Of course, here you are. Could you tell me whether breakfast is included?","keys":["here you are","whether","breakfast"]},{"ai":"It is, from 7 to 10. You're in 512, on the fifth floor. Anything else I can help with?","aiTr":"Dahil, 7'den 10'a kadar. Beşinci kattaki 512'desiniz. Yardımcı olabileceğim başka bir şey var mı?","hint":"Would you mind telling me the wifi password? I still have some work to finish tonight.","keys":["would you mind","wifi","work"]},{"ai":"Not at all, it's on the back of your key card. Will you need a taxi in the morning?","aiTr":"Ne demek, anahtar kartınızın arkasında yazıyor. Sabah taksiye ihtiyacınız olacak mı?","hint":"Yes, please. Could you book one to the conference centre for 8 o'clock?","keys":["book","conference","8 o'clock"]}]}},"co-01":{"intro":"Bir konferansta sağlık sektöründen biriyle tanışıyor, girişimini ilgi çekici ve profesyonel bir şekilde tanıtıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Me","en":"Hi, I don't think we've been introduced — I'm {name}.","tr":"Merhaba, sanırım tanıştırılmadık; ben {name}."},{"who":"Sarah","en":"Lovely to meet you, {name} — I'm Sarah, and I work for a hospital group in the UK.","tr":"Tanıştığımıza çok memnun oldum {name}; ben Sarah, İngiltere'de bir hastane grubunda çalışıyorum."},{"who":"Me","en":"I run AIHEAR, a medical device startup from Turkey that's tackling the shortage of audiologists.","tr":"Odyolog eksikliğine çözüm arayan, Türkiye merkezli bir tıbbi cihaz girişimi olan AIHEAR'ı yönetiyorum."},{"who":"Sarah","en":"So what kind of device are we talking about?","tr":"Peki nasıl bir cihazdan bahsediyoruz?"},{"who":"Me","en":"It's an audiometer that runs the entire test on its own, so no expert needs to be in the room.","tr":"Testin tamamını kendi başına yapan bir odyometre, bu yüzden odada bir uzmanın bulunmasına gerek yok."},{"who":"Me","en":"I'd describe it as a self-service hearing test that's completed in under ten minutes.","tr":"Bunu on dakikadan kısa sürede tamamlanan self servis bir işitme testi olarak tanımlayabilirim."},{"who":"Sarah","en":"That could be really useful for us, since patients are being kept waiting for months for a basic hearing test.","tr":"Bu bizim için gerçekten faydalı olabilir, çünkü hastalar basit bir işitme testi için aylarca bekletiliyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"That's exactly the gap we're trying to close, and I'd be happy to tell you more.","tr":"Kapatmaya çalıştığımız boşluk tam olarak bu ve size daha fazlasını anlatmaktan memnuniyet duyarım."},{"who":"Me","en":"Why don't I leave you my card, and we can pick this up after the next session?","tr":"Size kartımı bırakayım, bir sonraki oturumdan sonra konuya kaldığımız yerden devam edelim mi?"},{"who":"Sarah","en":"I'd like that — I'll come and find you once the panel has finished.","tr":"Bunu isterim; panel bittiğinde gelip sizi bulurum."}],"vocab":[{"en":"be introduced","tr":"tanıştırılmak","ex":"I don't think we've been introduced.","def":"to be formally presented to someone you have not met"},{"en":"run a company","tr":"bir şirketi yönetmek","ex":"I run a medical device startup.","def":"to manage and be in charge of a business"},{"en":"tackle","tr":"(bir sorunla) uğraşmak, çözmeye çalışmak","ex":"We're tackling the shortage of audiologists.","def":"to deal with a difficult problem"},{"en":"shortage of","tr":"...eksikliği","ex":"There is a shortage of audiologists.","def":"a situation where there is not enough of something"},{"en":"on its own","tr":"kendi başına","ex":"The device runs the entire test on its own.","def":"without help from anyone"},{"en":"keep someone waiting","tr":"birini bekletmek","ex":"Patients are being kept waiting for months.","def":"to make someone wait for a long time"},{"en":"close a gap","tr":"bir boşluğu kapatmak","ex":"That's exactly the gap we're trying to close.","def":"to fix a difference between what is needed and what exists"},{"en":"pick something up","tr":"kaldığı yerden devam etmek","ex":"We can pick this up after the next session.","def":"to continue a conversation or activity later"},{"en":"panel","tr":"panel (konuşmacı grubu)","ex":"I'll find you once the panel has finished.","def":"a group of experts who discuss a topic in front of an audience"}],"grammar":{"title":"The passive in everyday business talk","tr":"Eylemi kimin yaptığı önemli değilse veya belliyse edilgen yapı kullanılır: 'be + V3'. Süren durumlar için 'are being kept' gibi biçimler kullanılır.","examples":["I don't think we've been introduced.","The test is completed in under ten minutes.","Patients are being kept waiting for months."]},"questions":[{"q":"What problem is AIHEAR tackling?","options":["The high price of hearing aids","The shortage of audiologists","Slow internet in hospitals"],"a":1},{"q":"How long does the test take?","options":["About half an hour","Several hours","Under ten minutes"],"a":2},{"q":"Why is Sarah interested?","options":["Her patients wait months for a hearing test","She wants to invest in startups","She is looking for a new job"],"a":0},{"q":"What can we infer from Sarah's last line?","options":["She is trying to end the conversation politely","She genuinely wants to continue the conversation later","She will miss the panel"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"It's a medical device startup that's ___ the shortage of audiologists.","a":"tackling","hint":"çözmeye çalışmak"},{"s":"Patients are being kept ___ for months.","a":"waiting","hint":"beklemek"},{"s":"That's exactly the ___ we're trying to close.","a":"gap","hint":"boşluk"}],"order":[{"a":"I don't think we have been introduced."},{"a":"We can pick this up after the next session."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Hastalar aylarca bekletiliyor.","en":"Patients are being kept waiting for months.","keys":["kept waiting","months"]},{"tr":"Size kartımı bırakayım.","en":"Let me leave you my card.","keys":["leave you my card"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Clinic chain manager","personaTr":"Klinik zinciri yöneticisi","scene":"İrlanda'da bir klinik zinciri yöneten Emma ile bir oturum arasında tanışıyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"Hi, I'm Emma, and I run a chain of clinics in Ireland. I don't think we've been introduced.","aiTr":"Merhaba, ben Emma; İrlanda'da bir klinik zinciri yönetiyorum. Sanırım tanıştırılmadık.","hint":"Lovely to meet you, Emma. I'm {name}, and I run AIHEAR, a medical device startup from Turkey.","keys":["lovely to meet","run","startup","Turkey"]},{"ai":"So what's the idea behind it?","aiTr":"Peki arkasındaki fikir ne?","hint":"We've built an audiometer that runs the whole test on its own, so no expert needs to be in the room.","keys":["audiometer","on its own","expert"]},{"ai":"Our patients are being kept waiting for months. Could it help with that?","aiTr":"Hastalarımız aylarca bekletiliyor. Buna yardımı olabilir mi?","hint":"That's exactly the gap we're trying to close, since a test is completed in under ten minutes.","keys":["gap","ten minutes","exactly"]},{"ai":"I'm afraid I have to run to the next panel.","aiTr":"Korkarım bir sonraki panele koşmam gerekiyor.","hint":"Of course. Why don't I leave you my card, and we can pick this up afterwards?","keys":["card","pick this up","afterwards"]}]}},"st-01":{"intro":"Olası bir ortağa ürününün nasıl çalıştığını, hangi sorunu çözdüğünü ve neden ortak aradığını anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Partner","en":"So, what's the story behind your company?","tr":"Peki, şirketinizin hikayesi ne?"},{"who":"Me","en":"We're a medtech startup from Turkey, and we've developed an AI-assisted audiometer that runs a full hearing test on its own.","tr":"Türkiye'den bir medikal teknoloji girişimiyiz ve tam bir işitme testini kendi başına yapan, yapay zekâ destekli bir odyometre geliştirdik."},{"who":"Me","en":"The patient simply presses a button whenever they hear a sound, and the AI adjusts the test in real time.","tr":"Hasta bir ses duyduğunda sadece bir düğmeye basıyor, yapay zekâ da testi gerçek zamanlı olarak ayarlıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"At the end, an audiogram is produced in under ten minutes, with no expert needed in the room.","tr":"Sonunda, odada bir uzmana gerek kalmadan on dakikadan kısa sürede bir odyogram çıkarılıyor."},{"who":"Partner","en":"Who would you say is your main customer?","tr":"Sizce asıl müşteriniz kim?"},{"who":"Me","en":"I'd say it's hospitals, clinics and hearing aid shops, which are often short of audiologists.","tr":"Bence hastaneler, klinikler ve işitme cihazı mağazaları; bunlarda genellikle odyolog sıkıntısı var."},{"who":"Me","en":"In smaller towns, patients are often kept waiting for months just to get an appointment.","tr":"Küçük şehirlerde hastalar sadece randevu alabilmek için çoğu zaman aylarca bekletiliyor."},{"who":"Partner","en":"And who's on the team?","tr":"Peki ekipte kimler var?"},{"who":"Me","en":"We're a lean team of six: three engineers, a doctor and two of us on the business side.","tr":"Altı kişilik, küçük ama verimli bir ekibiz: üç mühendis, bir doktor ve iş tarafında iki kişi."},{"who":"Me","en":"If we found the right partners in Europe, we could grow much faster than we would on our own.","tr":"Avrupa'da doğru ortakları bulsak, tek başımıza olacağından çok daha hızlı büyüyebilirdik."},{"who":"Me","en":"That's really why I wanted to talk to you today.","tr":"Aslında bugün seninle konuşmak istememin nedeni de bu."}],"vocab":[{"en":"AI-assisted","tr":"yapay zekâ destekli","ex":"We've developed an AI-assisted audiometer.","def":"helped or partly run by artificial intelligence"},{"en":"on its own","tr":"kendi başına","ex":"The device runs a full hearing test on its own.","def":"without help from anyone else"},{"en":"in real time","tr":"gerçek zamanlı olarak","ex":"The AI adjusts the test in real time.","def":"immediately, while things are happening"},{"en":"audiogram","tr":"odyogram (işitme grafiği)","ex":"An audiogram is produced in under ten minutes.","def":"a chart that shows how well someone hears"},{"en":"be short of","tr":"...sıkıntısı çekmek, eksiği olmak","ex":"Many clinics are short of audiologists.","def":"to not have enough of something"},{"en":"get an appointment","tr":"randevu almak","ex":"People wait for months to get an appointment.","def":"to arrange a time to see a doctor or expert"},{"en":"lean team","tr":"küçük ve verimli ekip","ex":"We're a lean team of six.","def":"a small team that works efficiently with few resources"},{"en":"on the business side","tr":"iş tarafında","ex":"Two of us work on the business side.","def":"working on sales, money or strategy rather than technology"},{"en":"I'd say","tr":"bence, diyebilirim ki","ex":"I'd say our main customers are clinics.","def":"a polite way to give your opinion"}],"grammar":{"title":"Passive voice: focusing on the result","tr":"İşi kimin yaptığı değil, sonucun kendisi önemliyse 'be + V3' ile pasif kullanırız. Bir ürünü ya da bir sorunu anlatırken çok doğal durur.","examples":["An audiogram is produced in under ten minutes.","Patients are often kept waiting for months."]},"questions":[{"q":"What does the AI do during the test?","options":["It talks to the patient","It adjusts the test in real time","It calls an audiologist"],"a":1},{"q":"How long does it take to get an audiogram?","options":["Over an hour","About thirty minutes","Under ten minutes"],"a":2},{"q":"Why are clinics a good market for the device, according to the speaker?","options":["They are often short of audiologists","They have too many patients from big cities","They want cheaper headphones"],"a":0},{"q":"What can we infer about the speaker's goal in this conversation?","options":["They want to sell the company","They hope the listener could become a partner in Europe","They are looking for a job"],"a":1},{"q":"How many people work on the business side?","options":["One","Three","Two"],"a":2}],"gaps":[{"s":"The AI adjusts the test in real ___.","a":"time","hint":"gerçek zamanlı"},{"s":"Hospitals and clinics are often ___ of audiologists.","a":"short","hint":"...sıkıntısı çekmek"},{"s":"We're a ___ team of six.","a":"lean","hint":"küçük ve verimli"}],"order":[{"a":"An audiogram is produced in under ten minutes."},{"a":"That's really why I wanted to talk to you."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Avrupa'da doğru ortakları bulsak çok daha hızlı büyüyebilirdik.","en":"If we found the right partners in Europe, we could grow much faster.","keys":["right partners","grow much faster"]},{"tr":"Odyogram on dakikadan kısa sürede çıkarılıyor.","en":"The audiogram is produced in under ten minutes.","keys":["audiogram is produced","under ten minutes"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Potential partner","personaTr":"Olası iş ortağı","scene":"Bir konferansta kahve molasında Almanya'dan bir klinik zinciri yöneticisiyle tanışıyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"So, what's the story behind your company?","aiTr":"Peki, şirketinizin hikayesi ne?","hint":"We're a medtech startup from Turkey, and we've developed an AI-assisted audiometer that runs a hearing test on its own.","keys":["audiometer","AI","hearing test"]},{"ai":"What makes it different from a normal hearing test?","aiTr":"Normal bir işitme testinden farkı ne?","hint":"The AI adjusts the test in real time, and an audiogram is produced in under ten minutes with no expert in the room.","keys":["real time","no expert","ten minutes"]},{"ai":"Who would you say is your main customer?","aiTr":"Sizce asıl müşteriniz kim?","hint":"I'd say it's hospitals, clinics and hearing aid shops, which are often short of audiologists.","keys":["clinics","hospitals","short of"]},{"ai":"And what would you need from someone like me?","aiTr":"Peki benim gibi birinden neye ihtiyacınız olur?","hint":"If we found the right partners in Europe, we could grow much faster than we would on our own.","keys":["partners","grow","Europe"]}]}},"co-02":{"intro":"Konferanstan sonra Sarah'ya profesyonel, akıcı ve somut bir sonraki adım öneren bir e-posta yazıyorsun.","text":[{"en":"Subject: Following up from MedTech Europe","tr":"Konu: MedTech Europe sonrası takip"},{"en":"Dear Sarah,","tr":"Sevgili Sarah,"},{"en":"It was a pleasure meeting you at MedTech Europe yesterday.","tr":"Dün MedTech Europe'ta sizinle tanışmak bir zevkti."},{"en":"I really enjoyed our conversation about the waiting lists your hospitals are facing, which is exactly the problem we're working on.","tr":"Hastanelerinizin karşı karşıya olduğu bekleme listeleri hakkındaki sohbetimizden çok keyif aldım; bu tam da üzerinde çalıştığımız sorun."},{"en":"As promised, I've attached a short presentation that explains how our autonomous audiometer works.","tr":"Söz verdiğim gibi, otonom odyometremizin nasıl çalıştığını anlatan kısa bir sunum ekledim."},{"en":"If it would be useful, I'd be happy to arrange a short online demo for you and your team.","tr":"Faydalı olacaksa, size ve ekibinize kısa bir çevrimiçi demo ayarlamaktan memnuniyet duyarım."},{"en":"Would next Tuesday or Wednesday afternoon suit you, or is there another time that would work better?","tr":"Gelecek salı veya çarşamba öğleden sonra size uyar mı, yoksa daha uygun olacak başka bir zaman var mı?"},{"en":"In the meantime, please don't hesitate to get in touch if you have any questions.","tr":"Bu arada herhangi bir sorunuz olursa lütfen benimle iletişime geçmekten çekinmeyin."},{"en":"I look forward to hearing from you.","tr":"Sizden haber almayı dört gözle bekliyorum."},{"en":"Best regards, {name}","tr":"Saygılarımla, {name}"}],"vocab":[{"en":"It was a pleasure meeting you.","tr":"Sizinle tanışmak bir zevkti.","ex":"It was a pleasure meeting you yesterday.","def":"a polite, slightly formal way to say you enjoyed meeting someone"},{"en":"face a problem","tr":"bir sorunla karşı karşıya olmak","ex":"Many hospitals are facing long waiting lists.","def":"to have to deal with a difficult situation"},{"en":"as promised","tr":"söz verildiği gibi","ex":"As promised, I've attached the slides.","def":"in the way that you said you would"},{"en":"arrange a demo","tr":"demo ayarlamak","ex":"I'd be happy to arrange a demo for your team.","def":"to organise a meeting where you show how a product works"},{"en":"suit","tr":"uymak, uygun olmak","ex":"Would Wednesday afternoon suit you?","def":"to be convenient for someone"},{"en":"in the meantime","tr":"bu arada","ex":"In the meantime, feel free to read the presentation.","def":"in the period before something planned happens"},{"en":"don't hesitate to","tr":"...mekten çekinmeyin","ex":"Please don't hesitate to contact me.","def":"a polite way of encouraging someone to do something"},{"en":"get in touch","tr":"iletişime geçmek","ex":"Get in touch if you have any questions.","def":"to contact someone"}],"grammar":{"title":"Relative clauses: that / which","tr":"Bir şeyi daha ayrıntılı tanımlamak için 'that' veya 'which' ile yan cümle kurulur. Virgülden sonra gelen 'which', önceki fikrin tamamına da gönderme yapabilir.","examples":["I've attached a presentation that explains how our audiometer works.","We talked about waiting lists, which is exactly the problem we're working on.","Is there another time that would work better?"]},"questions":[{"q":"How does the writer connect the conversation to the company?","options":["Sarah's waiting lists are the problem the company is working on","Sarah wants to invest in the company","Sarah works for a competitor"],"a":0},{"q":"What does the presentation explain?","options":["The company's prices","How the autonomous audiometer works","The programme of the conference"],"a":1},{"q":"What does the writer suggest as the next step?","options":["A visit to Turkey","A phone call tonight","A short online demo"],"a":2},{"q":"What can you infer about the writer's attitude to Sarah's time?","options":["They are impatient and demanding","They are flexible and want to make it easy for her","They don't mind if the demo never happens"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"It was a ___ meeting you at MedTech Europe yesterday.","a":"pleasure","hint":"zevk, memnuniyet"},{"s":"Would next Tuesday or Wednesday afternoon ___ you?","a":"suit","hint":"uymak"},{"s":"Please don't ___ to get in touch if you have any questions.","a":"hesitate","hint":"çekinmek"}],"order":[{"a":"I'd be happy to arrange a short online demo."},{"a":"Is there another time that would work better?"}],"translate":[{"tr":"Bu arada herhangi bir sorunuz olursa benimle iletişime geçmekten çekinmeyin.","en":"In the meantime, don't hesitate to get in touch if you have any questions.","keys":["in the meantime","don't hesitate","get in touch"]},{"tr":"Size uygun başka bir zaman var mı?","en":"Is there another time that would suit you?","keys":["another time","suit you"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Sarah (by email)","personaTr":"Sarah (e-posta ile)","scene":"Sarah e-postana olumlu cevap veriyor; demo için ayrıntıları profesyonel bir dille netleştiriyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"Hi {name}, thanks for following up so quickly. The presentation was really helpful, and a demo would be great.","aiTr":"Merhaba {name}, bu kadar hızlı dönüş yaptığınız için teşekkürler. Sunum çok faydalıydı, bir demo harika olur.","hint":"I'm glad it was helpful. Would next Tuesday or Wednesday afternoon suit you, or is there another time that works better?","keys":["suit you","Tuesday","Wednesday","another time"]},{"ai":"Wednesday at 2 pm works for me. Who do you think should join from our side?","aiTr":"Çarşamba 14:00 bana uyar. Sizce bizim taraftan kim katılmalı?","hint":"I'd suggest your clinic manager and an audiologist, since they're the people who would use the device.","keys":["clinic manager","audiologist","suggest"]},{"ai":"Makes sense. Could you send me something to put in the calendar?","aiTr":"Mantıklı. Takvime ekleyebileceğim bir şey gönderebilir misiniz?","hint":"Of course, I'll send you a calendar invitation with the meeting link today.","keys":["calendar invitation","meeting link","send"]},{"ai":"Perfect, see you on Wednesday.","aiTr":"Mükemmel, çarşamba görüşürüz.","hint":"Great, see you then. In the meantime, don't hesitate to get in touch if you have any questions.","keys":["in the meantime","get in touch","see you"]}]}},"fu-01":{"intro":"Bir sağlık teknolojisi konferansındaki panelde, şüpheci bir doktora yapay zekânın klinisyenlerin yerini almaması, onları desteklemesi gerektiğini savunuyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Dr. Weber","en":"Every conference I go to, someone claims that AI will make doctors like me redundant within ten years.","tr":"Gittiğim her konferansta biri, yapay zekânın on yıl içinde benim gibi doktorları gereksiz kılacağını iddia ediyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"I'd say that's the wrong question, because AI should be designed to support clinicians, not replace them.","tr":"Bence soru yanlış, çünkü yapay zekâ klinisyenlerin yerini almak için değil, onları desteklemek için tasarlanmalı."},{"who":"Me","en":"Admittedly, it has real strengths: it's fast, it's consistent, and it doesn't get tired at the end of a long shift.","tr":"Kabul etmek gerekir ki gerçek güçlü yanları var: hızlı, tutarlı ve uzun bir vardiyanın sonunda yorulmuyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"But it still makes mistakes, and a model is only as good as the data it was trained on.","tr":"Ama yine de hata yapıyor ve bir model ancak eğitildiği veri kadar iyi."},{"who":"Me","en":"If it were trained on biased or incomplete data, it would make biased decisions without anyone noticing.","tr":"Taraflı ya da eksik verilerle eğitilseydi, kimse fark etmeden taraflı kararlar verirdi."},{"who":"Me","en":"That's why the final decision, and the responsibility that comes with it, should stay with a human.","tr":"Bu yüzden nihai karar ve beraberinde gelen sorumluluk bir insanda kalmalı."},{"who":"Me","en":"Trust matters too, since patients want to be treated by someone who can explain what's happening and why.","tr":"Güven de önemli, çünkü hastalar neler olduğunu ve nedenini açıklayabilen biri tarafından tedavi edilmek ister."},{"who":"Me","en":"Take our device as an example: it's an audiometer that runs a full hearing test in under ten minutes, with no expert in the room.","tr":"Cihazımızı örnek alalım: odada uzman olmadan, tam bir işitme testini on dakikadan kısa sürede yapan bir odyometre."},{"who":"Me","en":"The audiologist isn't replaced; instead, they're freed up to focus on the complex cases that genuinely need their expertise.","tr":"Odyoloğun yerine kimse geçmiyor; aksine, uzmanlığına gerçekten ihtiyaç duyan karmaşık vakalara odaklanması için zamanı açılıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"So, in my view, AI won't replace doctors, but it will change how they spend their time.","tr":"Yani bence yapay zekâ doktorların yerini almayacak, ama zamanlarını nasıl kullandıklarını değiştirecek."}],"vocab":[{"en":"make someone redundant","tr":"birini gereksiz kılmak, işsiz bırakmak","ex":"Will AI make doctors redundant?","def":"to cause someone to lose their job because they are no longer needed"},{"en":"clinician","tr":"klinisyen","ex":"AI should support clinicians.","def":"a doctor, nurse or other professional who treats patients"},{"en":"consistent","tr":"tutarlı","ex":"AI is fast and consistent.","def":"always behaving or performing in the same way"},{"en":"long shift","tr":"uzun vardiya","ex":"Doctors get tired at the end of a long shift.","def":"a long period of work, often in a hospital"},{"en":"be trained on","tr":"... ile eğitilmek","ex":"The model was trained on clinical data.","def":"(of an AI model) to learn from a particular set of data"},{"en":"biased","tr":"taraflı, önyargılı","ex":"Biased data leads to biased decisions.","def":"unfairly favouring some people or results over others"},{"en":"come with","tr":"beraberinde gelmek","ex":"Responsibility comes with the final decision.","def":"to be a natural part of something"},{"en":"free someone up","tr":"birine zaman açmak","ex":"The device frees audiologists up for complex cases.","def":"to give someone time for other things"},{"en":"expertise","tr":"uzmanlık","ex":"Complex cases need an audiologist's expertise.","def":"special skill or knowledge in a particular area"}],"grammar":{"title":"The passive, including with modal verbs","tr":"Passive (be + V3), işi kimin yaptığından çok ne yapılması gerektiğine odaklanır. Modal fiillerle: modal + be + V3 (should be designed). Tartışmalarda tarafsız ve profesyonel bir ton verir.","examples":["AI should be designed to support clinicians.","A model is only as good as the data it was trained on.","The audiologist isn't replaced; they're freed up to focus on complex cases."]},"questions":[{"q":"What is Dr. Weber worried about?","options":["That AI devices are too expensive","That AI will make doctors redundant","That conferences are too long"],"a":1},{"q":"Which strength of AI does the speaker mention?","options":["It never needs data","It is always right","It doesn't get tired"],"a":2},{"q":"What could happen if an AI were trained on biased data?","options":["It would make biased decisions","It would stop working","It would become faster"],"a":0},{"q":"Why does the speaker mention their own audiometer?","options":["To sell it to Dr. Weber","To show that AI can take over routine work and leave complex cases to experts","To prove that AI never makes mistakes"],"a":1},{"q":"What does the speaker predict at the end?","options":["AI will replace doctors within ten years","Doctors will stop using AI","AI will change how doctors spend their time"],"a":2}],"gaps":[{"s":"AI should be designed to support ___, not replace them.","a":"clinicians","hint":"klinisyenler"},{"s":"A model is only as good as the data it was ___ on.","a":"trained","hint":"eğitildi"},{"s":"They're freed up to focus on the complex cases that need their ___.","a":"expertise","hint":"uzmanlık"}],"order":[{"a":"AI should be designed to support clinicians."},{"a":"The final decision should stay with a human."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Taraflı verilerle eğitilseydi, taraflı kararlar verirdi.","en":"If it were trained on biased data, it would make biased decisions.","keys":["were trained","biased data","would make"]},{"tr":"Odyolog devre dışı kalmıyor; aksine karmaşık vakalara odaklanması için zamanı açılıyor.","en":"The audiologist isn't replaced; they're freed up to focus on complex cases.","keys":["isn't replaced","freed up","complex cases"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Skeptical doctor on the panel","personaTr":"Paneldeki şüpheci doktor","scene":"Panelde şüpheci bir doktor, girişimlerin doktorları devre dışı bırakmaya çalıştığını düşünüyor. Görüşünü kanıtlarla savunuyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"With all due respect, aren't start-ups like yours simply trying to cut doctors out of the process?","aiTr":"Kusura bakmayın ama sizin gibi girişimler doktorları süreçten çıkarmaya çalışmıyor mu?","hint":"Not at all. I'd say AI should be designed to support clinicians, not replace them.","keys":["support clinicians","not replace","not at all"]},{"ai":"But if the algorithm gets it wrong, who takes the blame?","aiTr":"Ama algoritma yanılırsa suçu kim üstlenecek?","hint":"The final decision, and the responsibility that comes with it, should stay with a human.","keys":["final decision","responsibility","stay with a human"]},{"ai":"And how do you know your system isn't biased?","aiTr":"Sisteminizin taraflı olmadığını nereden biliyorsunuz?","hint":"A model is only as good as its data, so we test it carefully; in our clinical study it matched a trained audiologist in 94% of cases.","keys":["only as good as","94","clinical study"]},{"ai":"So what's actually in it for audiologists?","aiTr":"Peki odyologlar bundan aslında ne kazanıyor?","hint":"The device takes over the routine tests, which frees them up to focus on complex cases.","keys":["routine tests","frees them up","complex cases"]}]}},"ab-01":{"intro":"Berlin'de daire görüyorsun: kira, faturalar, depozito, sözleşme süresi, belgeler, evcil hayvan ve gürültü konusunu konuşuyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Landlord","en":"Come on in—the kitchen and bathroom were completely renovated last spring, so everything is practically new.","tr":"Buyurun girin; mutfak ve banyo geçen bahar baştan sona yenilendi, yani her şey neredeyse yeni."},{"who":"Me","en":"I have to say, it's a lot brighter than it looked in the listing.","tr":"Söylemeliyim ki ilanda göründüğünden çok daha aydınlık."},{"who":"Me","en":"Could I just check what's included in the €1,200?","tr":"1.200 avroya nelerin dahil olduğunu bir teyit edebilir miyim?"},{"who":"Landlord","en":"Heating and water are covered, but the internet isn't, so you'd need to sign up with a provider yourself.","tr":"Isınma ve su dahil, internet değil; yani bir sağlayıcıya kendiniz abone olmanız gerekir."},{"who":"Landlord","en":"As for the deposit, I usually ask for three months' rent, which comes to €3,600.","tr":"Depozitoya gelince, genelde üç aylık kira istiyorum; bu da 3.600 avro ediyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"Would you be open to splitting that into three monthly instalments, since the move has already cost me quite a bit?","tr":"Taşınma bana zaten epey pahalıya patladığı için bunu üç aylık taksite bölmeye açık olur musunuz?"},{"who":"Landlord","en":"That's perfectly reasonable—most of my tenants do it that way, actually.","tr":"Gayet makul; aslında kiracılarımın çoğu böyle yapıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"And is there a minimum period on the contract?","tr":"Peki sözleşmede asgari bir süre var mı?"},{"who":"Landlord","en":"There's a two-year minimum, and the flat will be available from 1 November.","tr":"En az iki yıl; daire de 1 Kasım'dan itibaren boş olacak."},{"who":"Landlord","en":"I'd need to see your passport and proof of income, although company papers would be accepted instead of payslips.","tr":"Pasaportunuzu ve gelir belgenizi görmem gerekir, ama maaş bordrosu yerine şirket belgeleri de kabul edilir."},{"who":"Me","en":"That's a relief, because as a founder I don't actually get regular payslips yet.","tr":"İçim rahatladı, çünkü kurucu olarak henüz düzenli maaş bordrosu almıyorum."}],"vocab":[{"en":"listing","tr":"ilan","ex":"It's brighter than it looked in the listing.","def":"an advert for a flat or house that is for rent or sale"},{"en":"be covered","tr":"dahil olmak, karşılanmak","ex":"Heating and water are covered by the rent.","def":"to be paid for or included"},{"en":"sign up with a provider","tr":"bir sağlayıcıya abone olmak","ex":"You'd need to sign up with an internet provider.","def":"to become a customer of a company that supplies a service"},{"en":"come to","tr":"(toplam) etmek, tutmak","ex":"Three months' rent comes to €3,600.","def":"to add up to a total amount"},{"en":"be open to","tr":"...e açık olmak","ex":"Would you be open to splitting the deposit?","def":"to be willing to consider something"},{"en":"split into instalments","tr":"taksitlere bölmek","ex":"Could we split the deposit into three instalments?","def":"to divide a payment into smaller parts paid over time"},{"en":"minimum period","tr":"asgari süre","ex":"There's a minimum period of two years.","def":"the shortest time you must stay or keep an agreement"},{"en":"payslip","tr":"maaş bordrosu","ex":"I don't get regular payslips yet.","def":"a document from your employer that shows how much you were paid"},{"en":"that's a relief","tr":"içim rahatladı","ex":"Company papers are fine? That's a relief.","def":"used when you stop worrying about something"}],"grammar":{"title":"The passive: be + past participle","tr":"Eylemi kimin yaptığı önemli olmadığında edilgen yapı kullanırız: be + V3. Ev ilanlarında ve resmi konuşmalarda çok yaygındır.","examples":["The kitchen was renovated last spring.","Heating and water are covered.","Company papers would be accepted instead of payslips."]},"questions":[{"q":"What was renovated last spring?","options":["The whole building","The kitchen and bathroom","Only the balcony","The bedroom"],"a":1},{"q":"How does the landlord react to the instalment request?","options":["She says most of her tenants do it","She asks for a higher rent","She refuses politely"],"a":0},{"q":"What will the tenant have to arrange themselves?","options":["Heating","Water","An internet provider"],"a":2},{"q":"Why is the speaker relieved at the end?","options":["The rent is lower than expected","They can't show payslips, but company papers are accepted","The flat is available immediately"],"a":1},{"q":"Why does the speaker probably ask to split the deposit?","options":["Moving has already been expensive","They don't trust the landlord","The flat needs repairs"],"a":0}],"gaps":[{"s":"The kitchen and bathroom ___ completely renovated last spring.","a":"were","hint":"-di (edilgen, geçmiş)"},{"s":"Three months' rent ___ €3,600.","a":"comes to","hint":"ediyor, tutuyor"},{"s":"Would you be ___ to splitting that into three instalments?","a":"open","hint":"açık, istekli"}],"order":[{"a":"There's a two-year minimum on the contract."},{"a":"Company papers would be accepted instead of payslips."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Depozitoyu üç aylık taksite bölmeye açık olur musunuz?","en":"Would you be open to splitting the deposit into three monthly instalments?","keys":["open to","splitting","instalments"]},{"tr":"Isınma ve su kiraya dahil, ama internet değil.","en":"Heating and water are covered by the rent, but the internet isn't.","keys":["covered","internet isn't"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Landlord","personaTr":"Ev sahibi","scene":"Daire turunun sonundasın. Ev sahibi Bayan Becker karar vermeden önce seninle konuşmak istiyor.","turns":[{"ai":"So, now that you've seen the place, what's your impression?","aiTr":"Evet, daireyi gördünüz; izleniminiz nedir?","hint":"I'd say it's brighter than it looked in the listing, and I love the renovated kitchen.","keys":["brighter","listing","kitchen","love"]},{"ai":"Just so you know, I don't allow dogs, although a cat would be fine. Is that an issue?","aiTr":"Bilginiz olsun, köpeğe izin vermiyorum ama kedi olabilir. Bu sorun olur mu?","hint":"Not at all, I don't have any pets, so it wouldn't be an issue.","keys":["not at all","don't have any pets","no pets"]},{"ai":"Is there anything else you'd like to know before you decide?","aiTr":"Karar vermeden önce bilmek istediğiniz başka bir şey var mı?","hint":"Yes, how noisy does it get, especially at night?","keys":["noisy","noise","at night"]},{"ai":"The bedroom faces the courtyard, though the bar on the corner can get loud on Fridays. Would that put you off?","aiTr":"Yatak odası avluya bakıyor, ama köşedeki bar cuma günleri gürültülü olabiliyor. Bu sizi caydırır mı?","hint":"If it were only on Fridays, I don't think it would bother me much.","keys":["bother","only on Fridays","fine"]}]}},"ab-02":{"intro":"Berlin'e şirketinin Avrupa ofisini açmak için taşındın; bankada hem kişisel hem ticari hesap için koşulları öğreniyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Clerk","en":"Good morning—are you here to open an account?","tr":"Günaydın, hesap açmak için mi geldiniz?"},{"who":"Me","en":"Yes, I've recently relocated to Berlin to set up my company's European office, so I'll need both a personal and a business account.","tr":"Evet, şirketimin Avrupa ofisini kurmak için kısa süre önce Berlin'e taşındım, o yüzden hem kişisel hem de ticari bir hesaba ihtiyacım olacak."},{"who":"Clerk","en":"Before we do anything, could I check that you've registered your address, since we can't open an account without it?","tr":"Bir şey yapmadan önce adresinizi kaydettirdiğinizi kontrol edebilir miyim, çünkü o olmadan hesap açamıyoruz."},{"who":"Me","en":"I have—here's the registration certificate, along with my passport and residence permit.","tr":"Kaydettirdim; işte adres kayıt belgesi, pasaportum ve oturma iznimle birlikte."},{"who":"Clerk","en":"That's all we need for the personal account, which is free provided at least €1,000 is paid in each month.","tr":"Kişisel hesap için ihtiyacımız olan bu kadar; her ay en az 1.000 avro yatırılması şartıyla hesap ücretsiz."},{"who":"Clerk","en":"If less comes in, a monthly fee of €5 is charged.","tr":"Daha az para gelirse aylık 5 avro ücret alınır."},{"who":"Me","en":"And how is the business account different, apart from the price?","tr":"Peki ticari hesap, fiyatı dışında nasıl farklı?"},{"who":"Clerk","en":"It's designed for company transactions, so your business money is kept separate from your personal finances, and it costs €15 a month.","tr":"Şirket işlemleri için tasarlanmış, böylece şirketinizin parası kişisel paranızdan ayrı tutulur; aylık ücreti de 15 avro."},{"who":"Clerk","en":"However, it can only be opened once your company has been entered in the commercial register.","tr":"Ancak şirketiniz ticaret siciline kaydedildikten sonra açılabilir."},{"who":"Me","en":"I was told that would take another week, so I'll book an appointment for then.","tr":"Bunun bir hafta daha süreceği söylendi, o yüzden o zamana bir randevu alacağım."},{"who":"Clerk","en":"In the meantime, your debit card will be sent by post, and the PIN will be posted separately for security reasons.","tr":"Bu arada banka kartınız postayla gönderilecek, şifreniz de güvenlik nedeniyle ayrıca postalanacak."}],"vocab":[{"en":"relocate","tr":"(iş için) taşınmak","ex":"I've recently relocated to Berlin.","def":"to move to a new place to live or work"},{"en":"provided","tr":"...şartıyla, ...mesi koşuluyla","ex":"It's free provided €1,000 is paid in each month.","def":"only if"},{"en":"be paid in","tr":"(hesaba) yatırılmak","ex":"At least €1,000 is paid in each month.","def":"to be put into a bank account"},{"en":"charge a fee","tr":"ücret almak","ex":"A fee of €5 is charged if less comes in.","def":"to ask someone to pay money for a service"},{"en":"personal finances","tr":"kişisel mali işler","ex":"Keep company money separate from your personal finances.","def":"the money you earn, spend and save for yourself"},{"en":"commercial register","tr":"ticaret sicili","ex":"The company has been entered in the commercial register.","def":"an official list of the companies in a country"},{"en":"book an appointment","tr":"randevu almak","ex":"I'll book an appointment for next week.","def":"to arrange a time to meet someone"},{"en":"in the meantime","tr":"bu arada","ex":"In the meantime, your card will be sent by post.","def":"while you are waiting for something else to happen"},{"en":"for security reasons","tr":"güvenlik nedeniyle","ex":"The PIN is posted separately for security reasons.","def":"in order to keep something safe"}],"grammar":{"title":"The passive: is paid, will be sent, can be opened","tr":"Bankalar ve resmi kurumlar, işi kimin yaptığından çok ne olduğunu vurgulamak için edilgen yapıyı sever: be + V3. Zaman ve modal fiil 'be' ile gösterilir.","examples":["A monthly fee of €5 is charged.","Your debit card will be sent by post.","It can only be opened once your company has been registered."]},"questions":[{"q":"Why does the speaker need two accounts?","options":["They're setting up their company's European office","They have two flats","Their partner needs one"],"a":0},{"q":"What happens if less than €1,000 comes in?","options":["The account is closed","A €5 fee is charged","The card is cancelled"],"a":1},{"q":"Why must the business account wait?","options":["The speaker has no passport","The bank is too busy","The company isn't in the commercial register yet"],"a":2},{"q":"Why is the PIN probably sent separately from the card?","options":["So that someone who steals one letter can't use the card","Because the post is slow","Because the PIN isn't ready yet"],"a":0},{"q":"What can we infer about the speaker's plans for next week?","options":["They'll fly back to Turkey","They'll return to the bank for the business account","They'll close the personal account"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"It's free provided at least €1,000 is ___ in each month.","a":"paid","hint":"yatırılmak"},{"s":"If less comes in, a monthly fee of €5 is ___.","a":"charged","hint":"alınır, tahsil edilir"},{"s":"The PIN will be posted separately for security ___.","a":"reasons","hint":"nedenler"}],"order":[{"a":"I'll need both a personal and a business account."},{"a":"The PIN will be posted separately."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Hesap, şirket ticaret siciline kaydedildikten sonra açılabilir.","en":"The account can be opened once the company has been entered in the commercial register.","keys":["can be opened","commercial register"]},{"tr":"Bu arada kartınız postayla gönderilecek.","en":"In the meantime, your card will be sent by post.","keys":["in the meantime","will be sent","by post"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Bank clerk","personaTr":"Banka memuru","scene":"Bankadasın; memur hesap açma sürecini anlatıyor ve sana birkaç soru soruyor.","turns":[{"ai":"Morning! What brings you in today?","aiTr":"Günaydın! Bugün sizi buraya ne getirdi?","hint":"I've just relocated to Berlin, so I'd like to open a personal account.","keys":["relocated","open","personal account"]},{"ai":"Have you got your registration certificate with you? We can't do anything without it.","aiTr":"Adres kayıt belgeniz yanınızda mı? O olmadan hiçbir şey yapamıyoruz.","hint":"Yes, I registered last week, and I've also brought my passport and residence permit.","keys":["registered","brought","residence permit"]},{"ai":"Would you like online banking? Most of our customers use the app rather than coming in.","aiTr":"İnternet bankacılığı ister misiniz? Müşterilerimizin çoğu şubeye gelmek yerine uygulamayı kullanıyor.","hint":"Definitely, I'd much rather do everything on my phone if possible.","keys":["definitely","rather","on my phone"]},{"ai":"Great, you'll be sent a temporary password by text message, which you change when you first log in. Anything else?","aiTr":"Harika; kısa mesajla geçici bir şifre gönderilecek, ilk girişte onu değiştiriyorsunuz. Başka bir şey var mı?","hint":"I think that's everything, but I'll be back next week for the business account.","keys":["that's everything","business account","be back"]}]}},"ab-04":{"intro":"Komşun Lena ile merdivende sohbet ediyorsun, pazartesi de kahve makinesinin başında iş arkadaşın Tom'la; havadan kültürel farklara, davetlere kadar konuşuyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Lena","en":"Hi, you must be the person who's just moved into the third floor—I'm Lena, from directly above you.","tr":"Merhaba, üçüncü kata yeni taşınan kişi sen olmalısın; ben Lena, tam üst katından."},{"who":"Me","en":"Lovely to meet you, I'm {name}, and I hope my moving boxes weren't too noisy last week.","tr":"Tanıştığımıza çok sevindim, ben {name}; umarım geçen hafta taşınma kutularım çok gürültü yapmamıştır."},{"who":"Lena","en":"Not at all—and isn't it nice to finally see some sun, even if it's bitterly cold?","tr":"Hiç de değil; hem dondurucu soğuk olsa da nihayet biraz güneş görmek güzel değil mi?"},{"who":"Lena","en":"It seems like it's rained every single day this week.","tr":"Bu hafta her gün yağmur yağmış gibi geliyor."},{"who":"Lena","en":"So what's brought you to Berlin, if you don't mind me asking?","tr":"Sormamda sakınca yoksa, seni Berlin'e ne getirdi?"},{"who":"Me","en":"I'm from Istanbul, and I've been sent—well, I've sent myself—to open the European office of my health-tech startup.","tr":"İstanbulluyum ve sağlık teknolojisi girişimimin Avrupa ofisini açmak için gönderildim; yani, kendimi gönderdim."},{"who":"Me","en":"I love how green the city is, although I learned the hard way that everything closes on Sundays.","tr":"Şehrin bu kadar yeşil olmasına bayılıyorum, ama pazar günleri her şeyin kapandığını acı tecrübeyle öğrendim."},{"who":"Lena","en":"Well, we're having a barbecue in the courtyard on Sunday, which would be a good chance to meet everyone in the building.","tr":"O zaman pazar günü avluda mangal yapıyoruz; binadaki herkesle tanışmak için iyi bir fırsat olur."},{"who":"Tom","en":"So, how was your first proper weekend in Berlin?","tr":"Eee, Berlin'deki ilk gerçek hafta sonun nasıldı?"},{"who":"Me","en":"Better than I expected—my neighbours invited me to a barbecue and told me Berliners only seem cold at first.","tr":"Beklediğimden iyiydi; komşularım beni mangala davet etti ve Berlinlilerin sadece ilk başta soğuk göründüğünü söylediler."},{"who":"Tom","en":"That's true, and if you fancy it, a few of us are going for a drink on Friday after work.","tr":"Doğru; canın isterse cuma iş çıkışı birkaçımız bir şeyler içmeye gidiyoruz."}],"vocab":[{"en":"moving boxes","tr":"taşınma kutuları","ex":"I hope my moving boxes weren't too noisy.","def":"boxes you use to carry your things to a new home"},{"en":"bitterly cold","tr":"dondurucu soğuk","ex":"It's sunny but bitterly cold.","def":"extremely cold"},{"en":"if you don't mind me asking","tr":"sormamda sakınca yoksa","ex":"Where are you from, if you don't mind me asking?","def":"a polite way to start a personal question"},{"en":"learn the hard way","tr":"acı tecrübeyle öğrenmek","ex":"I learned the hard way that shops close on Sundays.","def":"to learn something through an unpleasant experience"},{"en":"a good chance to","tr":"...için iyi bir fırsat","ex":"The barbecue is a good chance to meet everyone.","def":"a good opportunity to do something"},{"en":"proper","tr":"gerçek, doğru dürüst","ex":"It was my first proper weekend in Berlin.","def":"real or complete"},{"en":"seem cold","tr":"soğuk görünmek","ex":"Berliners only seem cold at first.","def":"to appear unfriendly"},{"en":"fancy","tr":"canı istemek","ex":"If you fancy it, come for a drink.","def":"to want to do or have something (informal)"}],"grammar":{"title":"Relative clauses: who, which","tr":"Bir kişi ya da şey hakkında ek bilgi vermek için 'who' (insanlar) ve 'which' (şeyler, durumlar) kullanırız. 'Which' bütün bir cümleyi de niteleyebilir.","examples":["You must be the person who's just moved in.","We're having a barbecue, which would be a good chance to meet everyone.","Tom is the colleague who invited me for a drink."]},"questions":[{"q":"Where exactly does Lena live?","options":["Directly above the speaker","Next to the office","On the ground floor"],"a":0},{"q":"Why does the speaker mention the moving boxes?","options":["To ask for help","To apologise in case they were noisy","To complain about the stairs"],"a":1},{"q":"What does 'well, I've sent myself' tell us about the speaker?","options":["They work for a big corporation","They lost their job","They are the boss of their own company"],"a":2},{"q":"Why does Lena think the barbecue is a good idea for the speaker?","options":["The food is free","It's a chance to meet everyone in the building","It's her birthday"],"a":1},{"q":"What does Tom invite the speaker to?","options":["A drink on Friday after work","A barbecue on Sunday","A meeting"],"a":0}],"gaps":[{"s":"Isn't it nice to see some sun, even if it's ___ cold?","a":"bitterly","hint":"dondurucu"},{"s":"I learned the hard ___ that everything closes on Sundays.","a":"way","hint":"acı tecrübeyle"},{"s":"If you ___ it, a few of us are going for a drink.","a":"fancy","hint":"canın isterse"}],"order":[{"a":"Berliners only seem cold at first."},{"a":"It's a good chance to meet everyone."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Sormamda sakınca yoksa, seni Berlin'e ne getirdi?","en":"What's brought you to Berlin, if you don't mind me asking?","keys":["brought you to Berlin","don't mind me asking"]},{"tr":"Pazar günleri her şeyin kapandığını acı tecrübeyle öğrendim.","en":"I learned the hard way that everything closes on Sundays.","keys":["learned the hard way","closes on Sundays"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Neighbour (Lena)","personaTr":"Komşu (Lena)","scene":"Cumartesi sabahı merdivende tam üst katındaki komşun Lena ile karşılaşıyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"Hi, you must be the person who's just moved in downstairs—I'm Lena.","aiTr":"Merhaba, alt kata yeni taşınan kişi sen olmalısın; ben Lena.","hint":"That's me, I'm {name}, and I hope my moving boxes weren't too noisy.","keys":["that's me","moving boxes","noisy"]},{"ai":"Not at all! So, what's brought you to Berlin, if you don't mind me asking?","aiTr":"Hiç de değil! Peki, sormamda sakınca yoksa, seni Berlin'e ne getirdi?","hint":"I'm opening the European office of my health-tech startup, which is both exciting and a bit scary.","keys":["European office","startup","exciting"]},{"ai":"And what do you make of the city so far?","aiTr":"Peki şimdiye kadar şehir hakkında ne düşünüyorsun?","hint":"I love how green it is, although I learned the hard way that shops close on Sundays.","keys":["green","learned the hard way","Sundays"]},{"ai":"We're having a barbecue in the courtyard on Sunday—would you like to join us?","aiTr":"Pazar günü avluda mangal yapıyoruz; bize katılmak ister misin?","hint":"I'd love to, and if nobody minds, I'll bring some baklava from a Turkish bakery.","keys":["I'd love to","baklava","join"]}]}},"ab-03":{"intro":"Telefonla randevu alıyorsun ve muayenede belirtilerini ayrıntılı anlatıyorsun; doktor nedenini açıklıyor ve tavsiye veriyor.","text":[{"who":"Receptionist","en":"Dr Hoffmann's practice—how can I help?","tr":"Dr. Hoffmann'ın muayenehanesi, nasıl yardımcı olabilirim?"},{"who":"Me","en":"I've been having lower back pain for about three weeks, and I was wondering if the doctor could see me this week.","tr":"Yaklaşık üç haftadır bel ağrım var; doktorun beni bu hafta görüp göremeyeceğini merak ediyordum."},{"who":"Receptionist","en":"If it's not urgent, the earliest I can offer you is Thursday at 9:30.","tr":"Acil değilse size verebileceğim en erken randevu perşembe saat 9.30."},{"who":"Receptionist","en":"Please bring your health insurance card, which will be scanned at reception.","tr":"Lütfen sağlık sigortası kartınızı getirin; resepsiyonda okutulacak."},{"who":"Doctor","en":"So, tell me what's been going on.","tr":"Evet, anlatın bakalım, neler oluyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"The pain started shortly after I began working twelve-hour days at my kitchen table, because our office furniture still hasn't been delivered.","tr":"Ağrı, ofis mobilyalarımız hâlâ teslim edilmediği için mutfak masasında günde on iki saat çalışmaya başlamamdan kısa süre sonra başladı."},{"who":"Me","en":"By the evening it's around six out of ten, and it seems to get worse whenever I've been sitting for a long time.","tr":"Akşama doğru on üzerinden altı civarında oluyor ve uzun süre oturduğumda daha da kötüleşiyor gibi."},{"who":"Me","en":"I'd also say my sleep has suffered, as I tend to wake up at four and can't get back to sleep.","tr":"Uykumun da bundan etkilendiğini söyleyebilirim; genelde dörtte uyanıyorum ve tekrar uyuyamıyorum."},{"who":"Doctor","en":"Your muscles are extremely tight, which is very common in people who spend long hours at a desk, but there's no sign of anything serious.","tr":"Kaslarınız aşırı gergin; bu, masa başında uzun saatler geçirenlerde çok yaygın, ama ciddi bir şeyin belirtisi yok."},{"who":"Doctor","en":"I'm going to prescribe a pain-relief gel, which can be picked up at any pharmacy.","tr":"Ağrı kesici bir jel yazacağım; herhangi bir eczaneden alınabilir."},{"who":"Doctor","en":"If I were you, I'd get up every hour, walk for half an hour a day and keep screens out of the bedroom after ten.","tr":"Yerinizde olsam her saat kalkardım, günde yarım saat yürürdüm ve saat ondan sonra ekranları yatak odasından uzak tutardım."}],"vocab":[{"en":"I was wondering if","tr":"acaba ... diye merak ediyordum","ex":"I was wondering if the doctor could see me this week.","def":"a polite way to ask for something"},{"en":"urgent","tr":"acil","ex":"If it's not urgent, you can come on Thursday.","def":"needing attention very soon"},{"en":"go on","tr":"olmak, yaşanmak","ex":"Tell me what's been going on.","def":"to happen"},{"en":"get worse","tr":"kötüleşmek","ex":"The pain gets worse when I sit for a long time.","def":"to become more serious or unpleasant"},{"en":"suffer","tr":"kötü etkilenmek, zarar görmek","ex":"My sleep has suffered because of the pain.","def":"to become worse because of a situation"},{"en":"get back to sleep","tr":"tekrar uykuya dalmak","ex":"I wake up at four and can't get back to sleep.","def":"to fall asleep again after waking up"},{"en":"no sign of","tr":"...belirtisi yok","ex":"There's no sign of anything serious.","def":"no evidence that something exists or is happening"},{"en":"prescribe","tr":"reçete etmek, (ilaç) yazmak","ex":"I'm going to prescribe a pain-relief gel.","def":"to say officially what medicine a patient should take"}],"grammar":{"title":"Giving advice: If I were you, I'd…","tr":"Tavsiye verirken ikinci tip koşul kalıbını kullanırız: 'If I were you, I'd + fiil'. 'I' ile bile 'were' kullanılır; anlamı 'Senin yerinde olsam…'.","examples":["If I were you, I'd get up every hour.","If I were you, I'd keep screens out of the bedroom.","If I had a proper desk, my back wouldn't hurt so much."]},"questions":[{"q":"Why is the speaker working at the kitchen table?","options":["They prefer it","The office furniture hasn't been delivered","The flat has no other room"],"a":1},{"q":"When does the pain get worse?","options":["After sitting for a long time","In the morning","After walking"],"a":0},{"q":"What is the speaker's sleep problem?","options":["They can't fall asleep at night","They sleep too long","They wake at four and can't get back to sleep"],"a":2},{"q":"What does the doctor suggest is the main cause?","options":["A serious injury","Long hours at a desk","Too much walking","Bad food"],"a":1},{"q":"Why does the doctor probably advise keeping screens out of the bedroom?","options":["To help the speaker sleep better","To save electricity","To protect the screens"],"a":0}],"gaps":[{"s":"I was ___ if the doctor could see me this week.","a":"wondering","hint":"merak ediyordum"},{"s":"Our office furniture still hasn't been ___.","a":"delivered","hint":"teslim edilmek"},{"s":"If I ___ you, I'd get up every hour.","a":"were","hint":"olsaydım"}],"order":[{"a":"There's no sign of anything serious."},{"a":"The gel can be picked up at any pharmacy."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Yerinizde olsam her saat kalkardım.","en":"If I were you, I'd get up every hour.","keys":["if I were you","every hour"]},{"tr":"Uykum da bundan kötü etkilendi.","en":"My sleep has suffered too.","keys":["sleep","suffered"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Doctor","personaTr":"Doktor","scene":"Dr. Hoffmann'ın muayene odasındasın. Doktor belirtilerini ayrıntılı soruyor.","turns":[{"ai":"Good morning—so what brings you in today?","aiTr":"Günaydın, bugün sizi buraya ne getirdi?","hint":"I've been having lower back pain for about three weeks, and my sleep has suffered too.","keys":["lower back pain","three weeks","sleep"]},{"ai":"Would you say it's getting worse, or has it stayed about the same?","aiTr":"Sizce kötüleşiyor mu, yoksa aşağı yukarı aynı mı kaldı?","hint":"I'd say it's about the same, but it gets worse when I've been sitting for a long time.","keys":["about the same","gets worse","sitting"]},{"ai":"Have you been taking anything for it?","aiTr":"Bunun için bir şey alıyor muydunuz?","hint":"Just ibuprofen a few times a week, which helps for a few hours, but then the pain comes back.","keys":["ibuprofen","a few times a week","comes back"]},{"ai":"Right, I'll prescribe a gel, and if I were you, I'd take a break every hour. Any questions?","aiTr":"Peki, bir jel yazacağım; yerinizde olsam her saat mola verirdim. Sorunuz var mı?","hint":"Yes, what should I do if it hasn't improved in a couple of weeks?","keys":["improved","couple of weeks","what should I do"]}]}},"li-03":{"intro":"İlk yıldaki tükenmişlik deneyimini ve enerjini korumak için koyduğun üç kuralı anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Me","en":"During my first year as a founder, I was working fourteen-hour days and getting by on five hours' sleep.","tr":"Kurucu olarak ilk yılımda günde on dört saat çalışıyor ve beş saatlik uykuyla idare ediyordum."},{"who":"Me","en":"At the time, it seemed perfectly normal, which is probably why I didn't notice the quality of my decisions slipping.","tr":"O zamanlar bu bana gayet normal geliyordu; muhtemelen kararlarımın kalitesinin düştüğünü bu yüzden fark etmedim."},{"who":"Me","en":"It turns out that a tired brain isn't just slower; it also tends to pick the easy answer rather than the right one.","tr":"Anlaşılan o ki yorgun bir beyin sadece yavaşlamıyor; doğru cevap yerine kolay cevabı seçme eğiliminde de oluyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"Eventually I realised that energy, not time, was the resource that needed managing.","tr":"Sonunda yönetilmesi gereken kaynağın zaman değil, enerji olduğunu fark ettim."},{"who":"Me","en":"These days I stick to three simple rules.","tr":"Bugünlerde üç basit kurala bağlı kalıyorum."},{"who":"Me","en":"The first is that I sleep at least seven hours, and no emails are answered after 10 pm.","tr":"Birincisi, en az yedi saat uyuyorum ve gece 10'dan sonra hiçbir e-postaya cevap verilmiyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"The second is that my most important task is done in the morning, before meetings, while my mind is still fresh.","tr":"İkincisi, en önemli işim sabah, toplantılardan önce, zihnim hâlâ dinçken yapılıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"The third is a thirty-minute walk every day, which is when many of my best ideas tend to come.","tr":"Üçüncüsü, her gün otuz dakikalık bir yürüyüş; en iyi fikirlerimin çoğu genellikle o sırada geliyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"If I went back to my old habits, I'd probably burn out within months.","tr":"Eski alışkanlıklarıma dönsem muhtemelen birkaç ay içinde tükenirdim."},{"who":"Me","en":"A startup is a marathon, not a sprint, and a founder who burns out takes the company down with them.","tr":"Girişim bir sprint değil, maratondur; tükenen bir kurucu şirketi de kendisiyle birlikte batırır."}],"vocab":[{"en":"get by on","tr":"... ile idare etmek","ex":"I was getting by on five hours' sleep.","def":"to manage with only a small amount of something"},{"en":"slip","tr":"düşmek, kötüleşmek","ex":"The quality of my decisions was slipping.","def":"to become gradually worse"},{"en":"it turns out that","tr":"anlaşılan o ki","ex":"It turns out that tired people choose the easy answer.","def":"used to say that something is true, often surprisingly"},{"en":"resource","tr":"kaynak","ex":"Energy is a resource that needs managing.","def":"something valuable you can use, like money, time or energy"},{"en":"stick to","tr":"...e bağlı kalmak","ex":"I stick to three simple rules.","def":"to keep doing what you planned or decided"},{"en":"tend to","tr":"...me eğiliminde olmak","ex":"My best ideas tend to come during a walk.","def":"to usually do something or usually happen"},{"en":"burn out","tr":"tükenmek","ex":"I'd probably burn out within months.","def":"to become exhausted or ill from working too hard"},{"en":"take something down with you","tr":"birlikte batırmak","ex":"A founder who burns out takes the company down with them.","def":"to cause something to fail together with you"},{"en":"a marathon, not a sprint","tr":"sprint değil, maraton","ex":"Building a company is a marathon, not a sprint.","def":"something that needs long, steady effort, not a quick burst"}],"grammar":{"title":"The passive in everyday routines","tr":"Eylemi yapanın değil eylemin önemli olduğu durumlarda passive (be + V3) kullanılır: 'no emails are answered', 'my most important task is done'. Bu, kuralları kişisel bir tercih değil, sistemli bir düzen gibi gösterir.","examples":["No emails are answered after 10 pm.","My most important task is done in the morning.","Energy has to be managed like any other resource."]},"questions":[{"q":"How much did the founder sleep in the first year?","options":["About seven hours","About five hours","About ten hours"],"a":1},{"q":"According to the text, what does a tired brain tend to do?","options":["Avoid all decisions","Work faster than usual","Choose the easy answer over the right one"],"a":2},{"q":"What did the founder eventually realise?","options":["Energy, not time, needed managing","More hours meant more success","Meetings were the main problem"],"a":0},{"q":"Why didn't the founder notice the problem at first?","options":["The team hid it","Long hours seemed normal at the time","The decisions were actually good"],"a":1},{"q":"What does 'takes the company down with them' mean?","options":["The company suffers if the founder burns out","The founder sells the company","The founder moves the company abroad"],"a":0}],"gaps":[{"s":"I was getting ___ on five hours' sleep.","a":"by","hint":"idare etmek"},{"s":"These days I ___ to three simple rules.","a":"stick","hint":"bağlı kalmak"},{"s":"Many of my best ideas ___ to come during a walk.","a":"tend","hint":"eğiliminde olmak"}],"order":[{"a":"These days I stick to three simple rules."},{"a":"My most important task is done in the morning."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Eski alışkanlıklarıma dönsem muhtemelen tükenirdim.","en":"If I went back to my old habits, I would probably burn out.","keys":["went back","old habits","burn out"]},{"tr":"Gece 10'dan sonra hiçbir e-postaya cevap verilmez.","en":"No emails are answered after 10 pm.","keys":["no emails","are answered"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Young founder","personaTr":"Genç kurucu","scene":"Genç bir girişimci tükenmenin eşiğinde ve senden tavsiye istiyor. Deneyimini paylaşıp uygulanabilir öneriler veriyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"I'm working around the clock and I feel exhausted, but everyone says that's just startup life.","aiTr":"Gece gündüz çalışıyorum ve bitkin hissediyorum, ama herkes bunun girişim hayatı olduğunu söylüyor.","hint":"I used to think the same, but it turns out a tired brain tends to make worse decisions.","keys":["used to","tired brain","worse decisions","turns out"]},{"ai":"So what would you do if you were in my position?","aiTr":"Benim yerimde olsan ne yapardın?","hint":"If I were you, I'd protect your sleep first: at least seven hours, and no emails after 10 pm.","keys":["if i were you","at least seven hours","no emails"]},{"ai":"But my calendar is full of meetings from nine to six.","aiTr":"Ama takvimim dokuzdan altıya kadar toplantılarla dolu.","hint":"Then block the first hours of the morning for your most important task, before any meetings start.","keys":["block","morning","most important task"]},{"ai":"And how do I switch off after work?","aiTr":"Peki işten sonra kafamı nasıl boşaltırım?","hint":"I'd recommend a thirty-minute walk every day; that's when many of my best ideas come.","keys":["walk","thirty minute","every day","best ideas"]}]}},"ai-05":{"intro":"Fiyat itirazını, veri güvenliği sorusunu ve servis endişesini profesyonelce karşılıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Buyer","en":"We've been looking at your audiometer, and to be honest, the price is what's holding us back.","tr":"Odyometrenizi inceliyoruz ve açıkçası bizi tutan şey fiyat."},{"who":"Me","en":"I understand: the device is 4,000 euros, plus a software subscription of 99 euros a month per clinic.","tr":"Anlıyorum: Cihaz 4.000 euro, buna klinik başına ayda 99 euroluk yazılım aboneliği ekleniyor."},{"who":"Buyer","en":"That's considerably more than the conventional audiometers we currently use.","tr":"Bu, şu anda kullandığımız klasik odyometrelerden hatırı sayılır ölçüde fazla."},{"who":"Me","en":"It is, but I'd say the upfront price is only part of the picture.","tr":"Öyle, ama bence ilk ödenen fiyat resmin yalnızca bir parçası."},{"who":"Me","en":"If every test still needed an audiologist, I'd agree, but ours doesn't, so your audiologists can focus on the patients who really need them.","tr":"Her test hâlâ bir odyolog gerektirseydi size katılırdım ama bizimki gerektirmiyor; böylece odyologlarınız onlara gerçekten ihtiyacı olan hastalara odaklanabilir."},{"who":"Buyer","en":"Our IT department will want to know how patient data is handled.","tr":"BT departmanımız hasta verilerinin nasıl işlendiğini bilmek isteyecek."},{"who":"Me","en":"The AI runs on the device itself, so the data never has to leave your hospital, and it works offline too.","tr":"Yapay zekâ cihazın kendi üzerinde çalışıyor, yani verilerin hastanenizden hiç çıkması gerekmiyor; ayrıca internetsiz de çalışıyor."},{"who":"Buyer","en":"And what if something went wrong after installation?","tr":"Peki kurulumdan sonra bir şeyler ters giderse?"},{"who":"Me","en":"You'd be covered by a two-year warranty, and most issues can be resolved remotely with a software update.","tr":"İki yıllık garanti kapsamında olursunuz ve çoğu sorun bir yazılım güncellemesiyle uzaktan çözülebiliyor."},{"who":"Buyer","en":"If we went ahead, how quickly could your team get us up and running?","tr":"İlerlemeye karar verirsek ekibiniz bizi ne kadar hızlı çalışır hale getirebilir?"},{"who":"Me","en":"Installation would take about an hour and we'd train your staff the same day, but I'd suggest starting with a free one-month trial.","tr":"Kurulum yaklaşık bir saat sürer ve personelinizi aynı gün eğitiriz, ama bir aylık ücretsiz denemeyle başlamanızı öneririm."}],"vocab":[{"en":"hold back","tr":"geri tutmak, frenlemek","ex":"The price is what's holding us back.","def":"to stop someone from doing something"},{"en":"upfront price","tr":"peşin ödenen fiyat, ilk maliyet","ex":"The upfront price is only part of the picture.","def":"the amount you pay at the start"},{"en":"software subscription","tr":"yazılım aboneliği","ex":"There's a software subscription of 99 euros a month.","def":"a regular payment that lets you keep using software"},{"en":"part of the picture","tr":"resmin bir parçası","ex":"Price is only part of the picture.","def":"only one aspect of a situation"},{"en":"handle data","tr":"veriyi işlemek","ex":"We need to know how patient data is handled.","def":"to collect, store and use information"},{"en":"be covered by a warranty","tr":"garanti kapsamında olmak","ex":"You're covered by a two-year warranty.","def":"to have repairs paid for by the seller for a period of time"},{"en":"resolve an issue","tr":"bir sorunu çözmek","ex":"Most issues can be resolved remotely.","def":"to find a solution to a problem"},{"en":"go ahead","tr":"ilerlemek, karar verip başlamak","ex":"If we went ahead, when could you start?","def":"to decide to do something you have been considering"},{"en":"up and running","tr":"çalışır durumda","ex":"We can get you up and running in a day.","def":"working properly and in use"}],"grammar":{"title":"Second conditional: if + past, would","tr":"Gerçek dışı ya da şimdilik varsayımsal durumlar için: If + past simple, would + fiil. Satışta karşı tarafa baskı yapmadan 'diyelim ki' diye konuşmayı sağlar.","examples":["If every test still needed an audiologist, I'd agree with you.","If we went ahead, how quickly could your team get us up and running?","If something went wrong, you'd be covered by a two-year warranty."]},"questions":[{"q":"What is the buyer's main concern at the start?","options":["The size of the device","The price","The training","The warranty"],"a":1},{"q":"Why is the upfront price 'only part of the picture', according to the founder?","options":["The software is free","Prices will fall next year","No audiologist is needed for every test, so their time is freed up"],"a":2},{"q":"Why should the IT department feel reassured?","options":["Patient data stays in the hospital because the AI runs on the device","The data is stored in the cloud","The device doesn't collect any data"],"a":0},{"q":"What can we infer from the buyer's question 'If we went ahead…'?","options":["The buyer has already signed a contract","The buyer is seriously considering a purchase","The buyer has decided not to buy","The buyer only wants a lower price"],"a":1},{"q":"What does the founder suggest as a next step?","options":["A meeting with investors","A larger order","A discount","A free one-month trial"],"a":3}],"gaps":[{"s":"To be honest, the price is what's holding us ___.","a":"back","hint":"geri (tutmak)"},{"s":"Most issues can be ___ remotely with a software update.","a":"resolved","hint":"çözülmek"},{"s":"If we ___ ahead, how quickly could your team get us up and running?","a":"went","hint":"ilerlemek (go ahead, geçmiş hâli)"}],"order":[{"a":"The upfront price is only part of the picture."},{"a":"Your audiologists can focus on the patients who really need them."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Hasta verilerinin nasıl işlendiğini bilmek isteyecekler.","en":"They'll want to know how patient data is handled.","keys":["patient data","handled"]},{"tr":"Her test hâlâ bir odyolog gerektirseydi size katılırdım.","en":"If every test still needed an audiologist, I'd agree with you.","keys":["needed","I'd agree"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Procurement manager","personaTr":"Hastane satın alma müdürü","scene":"Yabancı bir özel hastanenin satın alma müdürü fiyat, veri güvenliği ve servis konusunda seni zorluyor.","turns":[{"ai":"Frankly, your price is higher than we expected. Can you justify it?","aiTr":"Açıkçası fiyatınız beklediğimizden yüksek. Bunu gerekçelendirebilir misiniz?","hint":"I'd say the upfront price is only part of the picture. Since no audiologist is needed for every test, your audiologists can focus on the patients who really need them.","keys":["part of the picture","audiologist","focus"]},{"ai":"How is patient data handled?","aiTr":"Hasta verileri nasıl işleniyor?","hint":"The AI runs on the device itself, so the data never has to leave your hospital, and it works offline.","keys":["on the device","offline","leave your hospital"]},{"ai":"What would happen if the device stopped working?","aiTr":"Cihaz çalışmayı durdursaydı ne olurdu?","hint":"You'd be covered by a two-year warranty, and most issues can be resolved remotely with a software update.","keys":["warranty","remotely","software update"]},{"ai":"If we went ahead, what would the next step be?","aiTr":"İlerlemeye karar verirsek bir sonraki adım ne olurdu?","hint":"I'd suggest starting with a free one-month trial. Installation would take about an hour, and we'd train your staff the same day.","keys":["trial","installation","train your staff"]}]}},"li-02":{"intro":"Bir 'hayır'ın arkasındaki üç nedeni ve reddedilen bir teklifi zamanla nasıl 'evet'e çevirdiğini anlatıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Me","en":"I've learned that when a customer says no, it's rarely about the product itself.","tr":"Şunu öğrendim: bir müşteri hayır dediğinde, mesele nadiren ürünün kendisidir."},{"who":"Me","en":"In most cases, a 'no' can be traced back to one of three things: trust, understanding or timing.","tr":"Çoğu durumda bir 'hayır'ın kökeninde üç şeyden biri vardır: güven, anlama ya da zamanlama."},{"who":"Me","en":"Trust tends to be built through small signals, such as a clear website, a quick reply or a customer who recommends you.","tr":"Güven genellikle küçük işaretlerle oluşur: net bir web sitesi, hızlı bir cevap ya da sizi tavsiye eden bir müşteri gibi."},{"who":"Me","en":"Understanding depends on how simply you explain things.","tr":"Anlaşılmak, işleri ne kadar sade anlattığınıza bağlıdır."},{"who":"Me","en":"If a buyer needed an engineer to make sense of your pitch, you would already have lost them.","tr":"Bir alıcı sunumunuzu anlamak için bir mühendise ihtiyaç duysaydı, onu çoktan kaybetmiş olurdunuz."},{"who":"Me","en":"Timing, on the other hand, is all about pain: people only switch when the old way becomes too painful to live with.","tr":"Zamanlama ise tamamen sıkıntıyla ilgilidir: insanlar ancak eski yöntem katlanılmaz hale gelince değişir."},{"who":"Me","en":"Before every meeting, I ask myself three questions: why should they trust me, will they get it in a minute, and what's hurting them today?","tr":"Her toplantıdan önce kendime üç soru sorarım: bana neden güvensinler, bir dakikada anlarlar mı ve bugün canlarını sıkan ne?"},{"who":"Me","en":"Last year, a clinic that had shown real interest turned us down.","tr":"Geçen yıl, gerçekten ilgi göstermiş bir klinik bizi geri çevirdi."},{"who":"Me","en":"We stayed in touch, though, and three months later their waiting list had grown so long that the timing was suddenly right.","tr":"Yine de iletişimi koparmadık ve üç ay sonra bekleme listeleri o kadar uzamıştı ki zamanlama birden doğru hale geldi."},{"who":"Me","en":"When we asked again, they agreed almost immediately.","tr":"Tekrar sorduğumuzda neredeyse hemen kabul ettiler."},{"who":"Me","en":"So I'd say a 'no' today is often just a 'not yet'.","tr":"Bu yüzden bugünkü bir 'hayır'ın çoğu zaman sadece 'henüz değil' olduğunu söyleyebilirim."}],"vocab":[{"en":"turn someone down","tr":"birini geri çevirmek","ex":"A clinic turned us down last year.","def":"to refuse an offer or a request"},{"en":"be traced back to","tr":"kökeni ...e dayanmak","ex":"Most refusals can be traced back to trust.","def":"to have a particular cause or starting point"},{"en":"make sense of","tr":"anlamlandırmak, çözmek","ex":"The buyer couldn't make sense of the pitch.","def":"to understand something that is difficult or unclear"},{"en":"build trust","tr":"güven oluşturmak","ex":"Trust tends to be built through small signals.","def":"to make people feel they can rely on you"},{"en":"switch","tr":"geçmek, değiştirmek","ex":"People only switch when the old way hurts.","def":"to change from one thing to another"},{"en":"stay in touch","tr":"irtibatta kalmak","ex":"We stayed in touch for three months.","def":"to keep communicating with someone"},{"en":"waiting list","tr":"bekleme listesi","ex":"Their waiting list had grown very long.","def":"a list of people who are waiting for something"},{"en":"the timing is right","tr":"zamanlama uygun","ex":"Three months later, the timing was right.","def":"it is a good moment to do something"}],"grammar":{"title":"The passive: focusing on the action","tr":"Passive (be + V3), eylemi kimin yaptığı değil eylemin kendisi önemli olduğunda kullanılır. 'Trust is built', 'can be traced back' gibi yapılar genel gözlemleri daha nesnel gösterir.","examples":["Trust tends to be built through small signals.","A 'no' can be traced back to one of three things.","The offer was turned down last year."]},"questions":[{"q":"According to the speaker, what is a 'no' rarely about?","options":["The timing","The product itself","Trust"],"a":1},{"q":"Which trust signal is mentioned?","options":["A large office","A famous investor","A customer who recommends you","A low price"],"a":2},{"q":"What changed at the clinic in those three months?","options":["Their waiting list grew much longer","They hired more audiologists","Their budget doubled"],"a":0},{"q":"What can we infer about the speaker's view of rejection?","options":["They lower the price immediately","They treat a 'no' as final","They see a 'no' as information and keep the door open"],"a":2}],"gaps":[{"s":"Last year, a clinic ___ us down.","a":"turned","hint":"geri çevirdi"},{"s":"Most refusals can be ___ back to trust, understanding or timing.","a":"traced","hint":"kökeni bulunabilir"},{"s":"People only ___ when the old way becomes too painful.","a":"switch","hint":"değiştirmek, geçmek"}],"order":[{"a":"Understanding depends on how simply you explain things."},{"a":"We stayed in touch for three months."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Bir alıcı sunumunu anlamak için bir mühendise ihtiyaç duysaydı, onu çoktan kaybetmiş olurdun.","en":"If a buyer needed an engineer to understand your pitch, you would already have lost them.","keys":["needed an engineer","would already have lost"]},{"tr":"Güven küçük işaretlerle oluşturulur.","en":"Trust is built through small signals.","keys":["is built","small signals"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Hesitant clinic owner","personaTr":"Kararsız klinik sahibi","scene":"Bir klinik sahibi ilgileniyor ama 'şimdilik değil' diyor. Asıl itirazı ortaya çıkarıp ilişkiyi canlı tutmalısın.","turns":[{"ai":"I can see the value of your device, but I'm not sure this is the right moment for us.","aiTr":"Cihazınızın değerini görüyorum ama bunun bizim için doğru zaman olduğundan emin değilim.","hint":"That's completely fair. Could I ask what's causing you the most trouble at the moment?","keys":["fair","most trouble","at the moment","could i ask"]},{"ai":"Well, patients are waiting six weeks for a hearing test, but switching systems feels risky.","aiTr":"Hastalar işitme testi için altı hafta bekliyor ama sistem değiştirmek riskli geliyor.","hint":"I understand. If you could try the device free for a month, would that reduce the risk for you?","keys":["free for a month","reduce the risk","try"]},{"ai":"Possibly. But I'd need to discuss it with my audiologists first.","aiTr":"Olabilir. Ama önce odyologlarımla konuşmam gerekir.","hint":"Of course. Shall I send you a short summary they can read, and follow up next week?","keys":["summary","follow up","next week"]}]}},"st-04":{"intro":"Bir distribütörle komisyon ve münhasırlık üzerine kararlı ama işbirlikçi bir pazarlık yürütüyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Partner","en":"Our standard commission is 25%, which reflects what it costs us to market a new product.","tr":"Standart komisyonumuz yüzde 25; bu, yeni bir ürünü pazarlamanın bize maliyetini yansıtıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"I appreciate that, but with our production costs, 25% would eat too far into our margin.","tr":"Bunu anlıyorum ama üretim maliyetlerimizle yüzde 25 kâr marjımızı fazlasıyla eritir."},{"who":"Me","en":"Realistically, we'd struggle to justify anything above 15%.","tr":"Gerçekçi olmak gerekirse, yüzde 15'in üzerindeki bir oranı gerekçelendirmekte zorlanırız."},{"who":"Partner","en":"If we went down to 15%, I'm not sure we could cover our marketing costs.","tr":"Yüzde 15'e insek pazarlama masraflarımızı karşılayabileceğimizden emin değilim."},{"who":"Me","en":"Then how about meeting in the middle: 20% for the first year, with a review after twelve months?","tr":"O zaman ortada buluşmaya ne dersiniz: ilk yıl yüzde 20, on iki ay sonra da bir değerlendirme?"},{"who":"Me","en":"That way, if the volumes are there, the terms can be adjusted to reflect it.","tr":"Böylece satış hacmi beklendiği gibi olursa şartlar buna göre ayarlanabilir."},{"who":"Partner","en":"That seems reasonable, although we'd want exclusive rights in Germany in return.","tr":"Bu makul görünüyor, ama karşılığında Almanya'da münhasır haklar isteriz."},{"who":"Me","en":"Exclusivity is something we'd be open to, provided a minimum sales target is agreed and met.","tr":"Minimum bir satış hedefi üzerinde anlaşılması ve bu hedefe ulaşılması şartıyla münhasırlığa açığız."},{"who":"Me","en":"It seems only fair that exclusive rights should be earned rather than simply given.","tr":"Münhasır hakların öylece verilmek yerine hak edilmesi gayet adil görünüyor."},{"who":"Partner","en":"Fine, let's have the lawyers draw it up and aim to sign next week.","tr":"Peki, avukatlara hazırlatalım ve gelecek hafta imzalamayı hedefleyelim."}],"vocab":[{"en":"eat into","tr":"(kârı) eritmek, azaltmak","ex":"25% would eat too far into our margin.","def":"to use up part of something valuable"},{"en":"justify","tr":"gerekçelendirmek","ex":"We'd struggle to justify anything above 15%.","def":"to give a good reason for something"},{"en":"cover costs","tr":"masrafları karşılamak","ex":"We need to cover our marketing costs.","def":"to have enough money to pay for expenses"},{"en":"meet in the middle","tr":"ortada buluşmak","ex":"How about meeting in the middle?","def":"to compromise by accepting something between two positions"},{"en":"volume","tr":"hacim, satış miktarı","ex":"If the volumes are there, the terms can change.","def":"the amount of products sold"},{"en":"be open to","tr":"...e açık olmak","ex":"Exclusivity is something we'd be open to.","def":"to be willing to consider something"},{"en":"provided (that)","tr":"...mesi şartıyla","ex":"Provided the target is met, you'll get exclusivity.","def":"only if"},{"en":"in return","tr":"karşılığında","ex":"They want exclusive rights in return.","def":"as an exchange for something"},{"en":"draw up","tr":"(sözleşme) hazırlamak","ex":"Let's have the lawyers draw it up.","def":"to write a formal document such as a contract"}],"grammar":{"title":"Passive with modals: can be adjusted, should be earned","tr":"'Modal + be + V3' yapısıyla kimin yapacağını vurgulamadan neyin yapılabileceğini ya da yapılması gerektiğini söyleriz. Müzakerede daha nesnel ve daha az kişisel duyulur.","examples":["The terms can be adjusted to reflect it.","Exclusive rights should be earned rather than simply given.","A minimum sales target must be agreed and met."]},"questions":[{"q":"Why does the speaker reject 25%?","options":["It would eat too far into their margin","The distributor is too small","They want to sell directly"],"a":0},{"q":"What does the speaker propose for the first year?","options":["15%","25%","20%"],"a":2},{"q":"What will happen after twelve months?","options":["The agreement will end","The terms will be reviewed","The commission will go up automatically"],"a":1},{"q":"Why does the speaker link exclusivity to a sales target?","options":["Because German law requires it","To make the distributor pay more commission","To protect the startup if the distributor doesn't sell enough"],"a":2},{"q":"What can we infer about the tone of the negotiation?","options":["Hostile and tense","Firm but cooperative","Very casual and unprofessional"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"25% would eat too far into our ___.","a":"margin","hint":"kâr marjı"},{"s":"How about meeting in the ___?","a":"middle","hint":"orta"},{"s":"Exclusivity is something we'd be ___ to.","a":"open","hint":"açık"}],"order":[{"a":"Exclusive rights should be earned rather than given."},{"a":"Let's have the lawyers draw it up."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Karşılığında Almanya'da münhasır haklar isteriz.","en":"We'd want exclusive rights in Germany in return.","keys":["exclusive rights","in return"]},{"tr":"Ortada buluşmaya ne dersiniz?","en":"How about meeting in the middle?","keys":["meeting in the middle"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Distributor","personaTr":"Distribütör","scene":"Almanya pazarına girmek isteyen deneyimli bir Hollandalı distribütörle komisyon ve münhasırlık şartlarını görüşüyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"Our standard commission is 25%, which is pretty normal in this market.","aiTr":"Standart komisyonumuz yüzde 25, bu pazarda oldukça normal.","hint":"I appreciate that, but with our production costs, 25% would eat too far into our margin.","keys":["margin","production costs","eat"]},{"ai":"If we went down to 15%, we couldn't cover our marketing costs.","aiTr":"Yüzde 15'e insek pazarlama masraflarımızı karşılayamayız.","hint":"Then how about meeting in the middle: 20% for the first year, with a review after twelve months?","keys":["meeting in the middle","20%","review"]},{"ai":"That seems reasonable, but we'd want exclusive rights in Germany in return.","aiTr":"Bu makul görünüyor ama karşılığında Almanya'da münhasır haklar isteriz.","hint":"Exclusivity is something we'd be open to, provided a minimum sales target is agreed and met.","keys":["open to","provided","sales target"]},{"ai":"Why tie it to a target? Don't you trust us?","aiTr":"Neden bir hedefe bağlıyorsunuz? Bize güvenmiyor musunuz?","hint":"Of course we do; it just seems fair that exclusive rights should be earned rather than simply given.","keys":["earned","fair","rather than"]}]}},"st-05":{"intro":"Ödeme yapan bir hastane müşterisinin şikayetini sakin ve profesyonelce çözüyorsun.","text":[{"en":"Yesterday we got a call from a hospital in Izmir, one of our paying customers.","tr":"Dün, ücret ödeyen müşterilerimizden biri olan İzmir'deki bir hastaneden bir telefon aldık."},{"en":"Their audiometer had frozen in the middle of a test, and the screen had gone completely black.","tr":"Odyometreleri bir testin ortasında donmuş ve ekran tamamen kararmıştı."},{"en":"The doctor told me she had a waiting room full of patients, so understandably she was furious.","tr":"Doktor bana bekleme salonunun hastalarla dolu olduğunu söyledi; bu yüzden haklı olarak çok öfkeliydi."},{"en":"The first thing I did was apologise and thank her for flagging it so quickly.","tr":"Yaptığım ilk şey özür dilemek ve sorunu bu kadar hızlı bildirdiği için ona teşekkür etmek oldu."},{"en":"Rather than guessing, I asked her a few questions to work out exactly what had happened.","tr":"Tahmin yürütmek yerine, tam olarak ne olduğunu anlamak için ona birkaç soru sordum."},{"en":"It turned out the problem was caused by a software bug rather than faulty hardware.","tr":"Sorunun arızalı donanımdan değil, bir yazılım hatasından kaynaklandığı ortaya çıktı."},{"en":"Our engineer sent an update remotely, and the device was up and running again within two hours.","tr":"Mühendisimiz uzaktan bir güncelleme gönderdi ve cihaz iki saat içinde yeniden çalışır hâle geldi."},{"en":"Later that day, I called her back to make sure everything was working as it should.","tr":"Aynı gün daha sonra, her şeyin olması gerektiği gibi çalıştığından emin olmak için onu geri aradım."},{"en":"If a customer had to wait days for a fix, I'd say we would lose their trust.","tr":"Bir müşteri bir çözüm için günlerce beklemek zorunda kalsa, bence güvenini kaybederdik."},{"en":"In my experience, a complaint that is handled well can actually make a relationship stronger.","tr":"Deneyimlerime göre, iyi yönetilen bir şikayet aslında bir ilişkiyi daha da güçlendirebilir."}],"vocab":[{"en":"flag something","tr":"(bir sorunu) bildirmek","ex":"Thanks for flagging the problem so quickly.","def":"to point out a problem so that people notice it"},{"en":"work out","tr":"anlamak, çözmek","ex":"I asked questions to work out what had happened.","def":"to understand or find the answer to something"},{"en":"be caused by","tr":"...den kaynaklanmak","ex":"The problem was caused by a software bug.","def":"to happen because of something"},{"en":"faulty hardware","tr":"arızalı donanım","ex":"The engineer checked for faulty hardware first.","def":"physical parts of a device that do not work correctly"},{"en":"remotely","tr":"uzaktan","ex":"Our engineer fixed the device remotely.","def":"from a different place, without being there"},{"en":"up and running","tr":"yeniden çalışır hâlde","ex":"The device was up and running within two hours.","def":"working normally again"},{"en":"understandably","tr":"haklı olarak, anlaşılır şekilde","ex":"Understandably, the doctor was furious.","def":"in a way that is easy to understand or accept"},{"en":"lose someone's trust","tr":"birinin güvenini kaybetmek","ex":"If we ignored complaints, we would lose our customers' trust.","def":"to make someone stop believing in you"},{"en":"handle a complaint","tr":"bir şikayeti yönetmek","ex":"A complaint that is handled well can build trust.","def":"to deal with a customer's problem"}],"grammar":{"title":"Passive: focusing on what happened","tr":"Eylemi kimin yaptığı değil, ne olduğu önemliyse passive kullanılır: be + V3. Şikayetlerde kimseyi suçlamadan olayı tarafsız anlatmaya yardımcı olur.","examples":["The problem was caused by a software bug.","A complaint that is handled well can make a relationship stronger.","The update was sent remotely."]},"questions":[{"q":"What was wrong with the device?","options":["It had frozen during a test","It had been dropped","Its headphones were broken"],"a":0},{"q":"Why was the doctor so angry?","options":["She had paid too much","Her waiting room was full of patients","The engineer was rude"],"a":1},{"q":"How was the problem fixed?","options":["An engineer travelled to Izmir","The hospital got a new device","An update was sent remotely"],"a":2},{"q":"What can we infer about the speaker's approach?","options":["They usually blame the customer","They try to understand the facts before acting","They prefer to avoid difficult calls"],"a":1},{"q":"According to the speaker, what would happen if a customer had to wait days for a fix?","options":["The customer would buy a second device","Nothing would change","The doctor would fix it herself","The company would lose their trust"],"a":3}],"gaps":[{"s":"It turned out the problem was ___ by a software bug.","a":"caused","hint":"kaynaklanmak"},{"s":"The device was up and ___ again within two hours.","a":"running","hint":"çalışır hâlde"},{"s":"Thank you for ___ the problem so quickly.","a":"flagging","hint":"bildirmek"}],"order":[{"a":"The problem was caused by a software bug."},{"a":"Our engineer sent an update remotely."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Sorun bir yazılım hatasından kaynaklandı.","en":"The problem was caused by a software bug.","keys":["was caused by","software bug"]},{"tr":"Cihaz iki saat içinde yeniden çalışır hâle geldi.","en":"The device was up and running again within two hours.","keys":["up and running","within two hours"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Angry doctor","personaTr":"Kızgın doktor","scene":"İzmir'deki bir hastanenin doktoru yoğun bir gününde arıyor: cihaz test sırasında dondu.","turns":[{"ai":"I'm in the middle of a busy clinic and your device has just frozen on me.","aiTr":"Yoğun bir kliniğin ortasındayım ve cihazınız az önce dondu.","hint":"I'm really sorry, and thank you for flagging it so quickly. Could you tell me exactly what's on the screen?","keys":["sorry","flagging","screen"]},{"ai":"Nothing, it's completely black, and it won't restart.","aiTr":"Hiçbir şey, ekran tamamen siyah ve yeniden başlamıyor.","hint":"It sounds like a software issue rather than faulty hardware, so our engineer can send an update remotely.","keys":["software","remotely","faulty hardware"]},{"ai":"Fine, but I've got a waiting room full of patients, so how long are we talking?","aiTr":"Peki, ama bekleme salonum hasta dolu; ne kadar süreden bahsediyoruz?","hint":"We should have it up and running within two hours, and I'll call you back to make sure it's working properly.","keys":["up and running","two hours","call you back"]},{"ai":"And what if this happens again next week?","aiTr":"Peki ya bu gelecek hafta yine olursa?","hint":"We're looking into the cause, but if it happened again, you'd get the same remote support straight away.","keys":["looking into","remote support","cause"]}]}},"co-03":{"intro":"Ortağının fiyat indirimi önerisine, onu kırmadan ama net gerekçelerle karşı çıkıyor ve alternatif sunuyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Partner","en":"I'd like to propose that we cut the price to 2,000 euros, which should help us close deals faster.","tr":"Fiyatı 2.000 euroya indirmemizi öneriyorum; bu, satışları daha hızlı bağlamamıza yardımcı olur."},{"who":"Me","en":"I can see where you're coming from, but I'm not convinced that's the right move.","tr":"Neden böyle düşündüğünü anlıyorum ama bunun doğru adım olduğuna ikna olmadım."},{"who":"Me","en":"Since each device costs us 1,500 euros to build, our gross margin would fall from about 60 percent to 25 percent.","tr":"Her cihazın üretimi bize 1.500 euroya mal olduğu için brüt kâr marjımız yüzde 60 civarından yüzde 25'e düşer."},{"who":"Partner","en":"Fair enough, but several clinics have told us the device is simply too expensive.","tr":"Haklısın ama birçok klinik bize cihazın düpedüz çok pahalı olduğunu söyledi."},{"who":"Me","en":"That's a valid concern, although I'd say the price itself isn't really the issue.","tr":"Bu haklı bir endişe, ama bence asıl mesele fiyatın kendisi değil."},{"who":"Me","en":"It seems that most clinics don't yet see how much money the device would save them.","tr":"Görünüşe göre çoğu klinik, cihazın kendilerine ne kadar para kazandıracağını henüz görmüyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"If they could see the monthly savings in black and white, I think the price would be much easier to justify.","tr":"Aylık tasarrufu açık açık görebilselerdi, bence fiyatı savunmak çok daha kolay olurdu."},{"who":"Partner","en":"That's a fair point, but how would we actually show them that?","tr":"Haklı bir nokta ama bunu onlara gerçekte nasıl gösterirdik?"},{"who":"Me","en":"We could build a simple calculator which shows, for example, that a clinic doing 100 tests a month saves 1,500 euros.","tr":"Örneğin ayda 100 test yapan bir kliniğin 1.500 euro tasarruf ettiğini gösteren basit bir hesaplayıcı yapabiliriz."},{"who":"Partner","en":"All right, let's test that approach for two months before we touch the price.","tr":"Peki, fiyata dokunmadan önce bu yaklaşımı iki ay test edelim."},{"who":"Me","en":"Sounds good, and thanks for hearing me out.","tr":"Kulağa iyi geliyor, beni sonuna kadar dinlediğin için de teşekkürler."}],"vocab":[{"en":"close deals","tr":"satışı bağlamak, anlaşma yapmak","ex":"A lower price might help us close deals faster.","def":"to successfully finish a sale or agreement"},{"en":"I can see where you're coming from","tr":"neden böyle düşündüğünü anlıyorum","ex":"I can see where you're coming from, but I disagree.","def":"I understand why you think this (a polite start before disagreeing)"},{"en":"I'm not convinced","tr":"pek ikna olmadım","ex":"I'm not convinced that's the right move.","def":"I don't fully believe it is right"},{"en":"gross margin","tr":"brüt kâr marjı","ex":"Our gross margin would fall to 25 percent.","def":"the part of the price left after paying the cost of making the product"},{"en":"a valid concern","tr":"haklı bir endişe","ex":"That's a valid concern, but the price isn't the issue.","def":"a worry that is reasonable and should be taken seriously"},{"en":"I'd say","tr":"bence, diyebilirim ki","ex":"I'd say the price itself isn't really the issue.","def":"a soft way to give your opinion"},{"en":"justify the price","tr":"fiyatı gerekçelendirmek","ex":"Clear savings make it easier to justify the price.","def":"to show that a price is reasonable"},{"en":"in black and white","tr":"açık açık, yazılı olarak","ex":"They need to see the savings in black and white.","def":"clearly, in writing or in numbers"},{"en":"hear someone out","tr":"birini sonuna kadar dinlemek","ex":"Thanks for hearing me out.","def":"to listen to everything someone wants to say before you react"}],"grammar":{"title":"Second conditional: If they could..., ... would...","tr":"Şu an gerçek olmayan ya da varsayımsal durumlar için: If + geçmiş zaman, would + fiil. Toplantıda bir fikri daha yumuşak ve varsayımsal biçimde tartışmanı sağlar.","examples":["If they could see the savings, the price would be easier to justify.","If we cut the price, our margin would fall to 25 percent.","Would you agree if we tested it for two months?"]},"questions":[{"q":"What reason does the partner give for cutting the price?","options":["To close deals faster","To beat a competitor","To reduce production costs"],"a":0},{"q":"What would happen to the gross margin at 2,000 euros?","options":["It would rise to 60 percent","It would stay the same","It would fall to about 25 percent"],"a":2},{"q":"What have several clinics told the partner?","options":["The device is too slow","The device is too expensive","The calculator is confusing"],"a":1},{"q":"What does the speaker think is the real issue?","options":["The device needs new features","The software fee is too high","The sales team is too small","Clinics don't yet see the savings"],"a":3},{"q":"What can we infer about the partner at the end?","options":["They are still annoyed","They are willing to delay a decision on price","They now want to raise the price"],"a":1}],"gaps":[{"s":"I can see where you're ___ from, but I'm not convinced.","a":"coming","hint":"(bakış açısı) geliyorsun"},{"s":"If they could see the savings, the price would be easier to ___.","a":"justify","hint":"gerekçelendirmek"},{"s":"Thanks for hearing me ___.","a":"out","hint":"sonuna kadar"}],"order":[{"a":"I'm not convinced that's the right move."},{"a":"Let's test that approach for two months."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Bunun doğru adım olduğuna ikna olmadım.","en":"I'm not convinced that's the right move.","keys":["not convinced","right move"]},{"tr":"Bu haklı bir endişe ama bence asıl mesele fiyat değil.","en":"That's a valid concern, but I'd say the price isn't the real issue.","keys":["valid concern","real issue"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Business partner","personaTr":"İş ortağı","scene":"Ortağın cihazı bedava verip parayı yazılımdan kazanmayı öneriyor. Sen gerekçeleriyle karşı çıkıp bir test öneriyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"Here's a thought: what if we gave the device away for free and made our money on the software?","aiTr":"Bir fikrim var: cihazı ücretsiz verip paramızı yazılımdan kazansak?","hint":"I can see where you're coming from, but I'm not convinced. Each device costs us 1,500 euros to build.","keys":["coming from","not convinced","costs us"]},{"ai":"Sure, but clinics would sign up much faster if there were no upfront cost.","aiTr":"Evet ama başta hiç maliyet olmasa klinikler çok daha hızlı kaydolurdu.","hint":"That's a valid concern. However, if we did that, the software fee would have to be much higher.","keys":["valid concern","would have to","software fee"]},{"ai":"So you think clinics wouldn't accept a higher monthly fee?","aiTr":"Yani kliniklerin daha yüksek bir aylık ücreti kabul etmeyeceğini mi düşünüyorsun?","hint":"I'd say it's risky; our customers pay 99 euros a month now and seem happy with that.","keys":["I'd say","risky","99 euros"]},{"ai":"Fair enough. What would you suggest instead?","aiTr":"Peki, haklısın. Onun yerine ne önerirsin?","hint":"I'd suggest testing both models with a few clinics for two months and then comparing the numbers.","keys":["suggest","both models","two months"]}]}},"in-01":{"intro":"Bir demo gününde girişimini yatırımcılara ikna edici ve akıcı bir dille sunuyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Me","en":"Good afternoon, everyone — I'm {name}, founder of AIHEAR, and we're on a mission to make hearing tests available to everyone.","tr":"Herkese iyi günler — ben {name}, AIHEAR'ın kurucusuyum; işitme testlerini herkes için erişilebilir kılmayı misyon edindik."},{"who":"Me","en":"Roughly one in five people has some degree of hearing loss, yet the vast majority are never tested.","tr":"Her beş kişiden yaklaşık biri bir dereceye kadar işitme kaybı yaşıyor, ancak büyük çoğunluğu hiç test edilmiyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"The reason is a shortage of audiologists: in smaller towns, patients often wait months just to get an appointment.","tr":"Bunun nedeni odyolog eksikliği: küçük şehirlerde hastalar sadece randevu almak için çoğu zaman aylarca bekliyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"We've built an autonomous, AI-assisted audiometer that runs a full hearing test in under ten minutes, with no expert in the room.","tr":"Odada bir uzmana gerek kalmadan tam bir işitme testini on dakikadan kısa sürede yapan otonom, yapay zekâ destekli bir odyometre geliştirdik."},{"who":"Me","en":"The patient simply puts on headphones and presses a button, while the AI adjusts the test in real time.","tr":"Hasta yalnızca kulaklığı takıyor ve bir düğmeye basıyor; yapay zekâ ise testi gerçek zamanlı olarak uyarlıyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"We make money in two ways: a one-off device sale and a monthly software fee, which gives us recurring revenue.","tr":"İki yoldan para kazanıyoruz: tek seferlik cihaz satışı ve bize tekrarlayan gelir sağlayan aylık yazılım ücreti."},{"who":"Me","en":"Our prototype is already in its third version, and five clinics are paying customers.","tr":"Prototipimiz şimdiden üçüncü versiyonunda ve beş klinik ödeme yapan müşterimiz."},{"who":"Me","en":"In a study at two university hospitals, our results matched those of a trained audiologist in 94% of cases.","tr":"İki üniversite hastanesinde yapılan bir çalışmada sonuçlarımız, vakaların %94'ünde eğitimli bir odyoloğun sonuçlarıyla örtüştü."},{"who":"Me","en":"Behind all this is a team of six: three engineers, a doctor and two business people.","tr":"Tüm bunların arkasında altı kişilik bir ekip var: üç mühendis, bir doktor ve iki iş insanı."},{"who":"Me","en":"We're raising €500,000, which will allow us to complete CE certification and enter the European market.","tr":"500.000 € topluyoruz; bu yatırım CE sertifikasyonunu tamamlamamızı ve Avrupa pazarına girmemizi sağlayacak."},{"who":"Me","en":"If you'd like to hear more, I'd be delighted to take your questions.","tr":"Daha fazlasını duymak isterseniz sorularınızı memnuniyetle yanıtlarım."}],"vocab":[{"en":"be on a mission to","tr":"...yı misyon edinmek","ex":"We're on a mission to make hearing tests available to everyone.","def":"to have a strong goal you are working towards"},{"en":"some degree of","tr":"bir dereceye kadar","ex":"One in five people has some degree of hearing loss.","def":"a certain amount of"},{"en":"the vast majority","tr":"büyük çoğunluk","ex":"The vast majority are never tested.","def":"almost all of a group"},{"en":"shortage of","tr":"...eksikliği, kıtlığı","ex":"There is a shortage of audiologists.","def":"a situation where there is not enough of something"},{"en":"in real time","tr":"gerçek zamanlı olarak","ex":"The AI adjusts the test in real time.","def":"immediately, as things happen"},{"en":"one-off","tr":"tek seferlik","ex":"A one-off device sale brings in cash.","def":"happening only once"},{"en":"recurring revenue","tr":"tekrarlayan gelir","ex":"The monthly fee gives us recurring revenue.","def":"income that comes in regularly"},{"en":"paying customer","tr":"ödeme yapan müşteri","ex":"Five clinics are paying customers.","def":"a customer who pays for the product"},{"en":"take questions","tr":"soruları yanıtlamak","ex":"I'd be delighted to take your questions.","def":"to answer questions from an audience"}],"grammar":{"title":"Relative clauses: that and which","tr":"Defining relative clause ('that') neyi kastettiğimizi tanımlar; non-defining relative clause ('which', virgülle) ek bilgi verir. Sunumda tek cümlede daha fazla bilgi vermeni sağlar.","examples":["We've built an audiometer that runs a full hearing test.","We charge a monthly fee, which gives us recurring revenue.","We're raising €500,000, which will allow us to enter Europe."]},"questions":[{"q":"What causes long waiting times in smaller towns?","options":["Expensive devices","A shortage of audiologists","Bad internet"],"a":1},{"q":"What does the patient do during the test?","options":["Puts on headphones and presses a button","Answers questions from a doctor","Fills in a form online"],"a":0},{"q":"Why does the founder mention the monthly software fee?","options":["To show the product is cheap","To explain why the device is free","To highlight a source of recurring revenue that investors value"],"a":2},{"q":"What does the 94% figure show?","options":["How many customers renewed","How often results matched a trained audiologist","The company's gross margin"],"a":1},{"q":"What will the €500,000 be used for?","options":["CE certification and entering the European market","Opening a US office","Hiring ten more engineers"],"a":0}],"gaps":[{"s":"The vast majority are never tested because of a ___ of audiologists.","a":"shortage","hint":"eksiklik"},{"s":"The AI adjusts the test in real ___.","a":"time","hint":"zaman"},{"s":"The monthly fee gives us ___ revenue.","a":"recurring","hint":"tekrarlayan"}],"order":[{"a":"Our prototype is already in its third version."},{"a":"Five clinics are already paying customers."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Büyük çoğunluğu hiç test edilmiyor.","en":"The vast majority are never tested.","keys":["vast majority","never tested"]},{"tr":"Yapay zekâ testi gerçek zamanlı olarak uyarlıyor.","en":"The AI adjusts the test in real time.","keys":["adjusts","in real time"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Investor at a demo day","personaTr":"Demo günü yatırımcısı","scene":"Sunumun bitti. Yatırımcı ürününü, sonuçlarını ve yatırımı nasıl kullanacağını soruyor.","turns":[{"ai":"Thanks for that. What makes your solution different from a normal hearing test?","aiTr":"Teşekkürler. Çözümünüzü normal bir işitme testinden farklı kılan ne?","hint":"It's autonomous, so no expert needs to be in the room, and the test takes under ten minutes.","keys":["autonomous","no expert","under ten minutes"]},{"ai":"How do you know the results are reliable?","aiTr":"Sonuçların güvenilir olduğunu nereden biliyorsunuz?","hint":"In a study at two university hospitals, our results matched a trained audiologist in 94% of cases.","keys":["94","university hospitals","matched"]},{"ai":"And how does the business make money?","aiTr":"Peki şirket nasıl para kazanıyor?","hint":"We sell the device and charge a monthly software fee, which gives us recurring revenue.","keys":["recurring revenue","monthly software fee","sell the device"]},{"ai":"What would you do with our money?","aiTr":"Paramızla ne yapardınız?","hint":"We'd use the €500,000 to complete CE certification and enter the European market.","keys":["CE certification","European market","500,000"]}]}},"ai-03":{"intro":"Prototipini, klinik verileri ve yatırım ihtiyacını bir yatırımcıya profesyonelce sunuyorsun.","text":[{"en":"Thanks for making the time; I'd like to walk you through the prototype we've brought along today.","tr":"Zaman ayırdığınız için teşekkürler; bugün yanımızda getirdiğimiz prototipi size adım adım anlatmak istiyorum."},{"en":"In short, it's an AI-assisted audiometer designed to make hearing tests faster and more accessible without compromising on accuracy.","tr":"Kısacası bu, doğruluktan ödün vermeden işitme testlerini daha hızlı ve erişilebilir kılmak için tasarlanmış, yapay zekâ destekli bir odyometre."},{"en":"What you're looking at is the third version, and the first, believe it or not, was a laptop and a pair of headphones.","tr":"Gördüğünüz üçüncü versiyon; ilki ise inanır mısınız, bir dizüstü bilgisayar ve bir kulaklıktı."},{"en":"The main development phase has now been completed, so the core technology is essentially in place.","tr":"Ana geliştirme aşaması artık tamamlandı, yani temel teknoloji büyük ölçüde hazır."},{"en":"The device has also been validated in a blind study at two university hospitals, involving 200 participants aged 18 to 75.","tr":"Cihaz ayrıca iki üniversite hastanesinde, 18-75 yaş arası 200 katılımcıyla yapılan kör bir çalışmada doğrulandı."},{"en":"Its results matched those of a trained audiologist in 94% of cases, and the remaining 6% differed only slightly.","tr":"Sonuçları vakaların %94'ünde eğitimli bir odyoloğunkilerle eşleşti; kalan %6 ise yalnızca hafifçe farklıydı."},{"en":"Crucially, none of those differences changed the diagnosis.","tr":"En önemlisi, bu farkların hiçbiri tanıyı değiştirmedi."},{"en":"The study was published in a medical journal last spring.","tr":"Çalışma geçen bahar bir tıp dergisinde yayımlandı."},{"en":"Our focus now is on CE certification, which is required for a Class IIa device like ours.","tr":"Şu anki odağımız, bizimki gibi Sınıf IIa bir cihaz için zorunlu olan CE sertifikasyonu."},{"en":"We're raising €500,000 to get through certification and enter the European market.","tr":"Sertifikasyonu tamamlamak ve Avrupa pazarına girmek için 500.000 € topluyoruz."},{"en":"If we closed the round this quarter, I'd say the end of next year would be a realistic target for the CE mark.","tr":"Turu bu çeyrekte kapatabilsek, CE işareti için gelecek yılın sonu bence gerçekçi bir hedef olurdu."}],"vocab":[{"en":"walk someone through","tr":"birine adım adım anlatmak","ex":"Let me walk you through the prototype.","def":"to explain something to someone step by step"},{"en":"without compromising on","tr":"...den ödün vermeden","ex":"We made the test faster without compromising on accuracy.","def":"without making something worse in order to gain something else"},{"en":"be in place","tr":"hazır olmak, yerinde olmak","ex":"The core technology is now in place.","def":"to be ready and working"},{"en":"blind study","tr":"kör çalışma","ex":"The device was tested in a blind study.","def":"a study in which the people checking results don't know which method produced them"},{"en":"differ slightly","tr":"hafifçe farklı olmak","ex":"The remaining 6% differed only slightly.","def":"to be a little different"},{"en":"be required for","tr":"...için zorunlu olmak","ex":"CE certification is required for a Class IIa device.","def":"to be necessary because of a law or rule"},{"en":"close a round","tr":"yatırım turunu kapatmak","ex":"We hope to close the round this quarter.","def":"to finish raising a planned amount of investment"},{"en":"realistic target","tr":"gerçekçi hedef","ex":"The end of next year is a realistic target.","def":"a goal that can actually be achieved"}],"grammar":{"title":"Passive: present perfect and past","tr":"Kimin yaptığından çok sonucun önemli olduğu durumlarda passive kullanılır. Present perfect passive (has been + V3) bugüne uzanan sonuçları anlatır: The device has been validated. Past passive (was + V3) belirli bir geçmiş zamanı anlatır.","examples":["The main development phase has now been completed.","The device has been validated in a blind study.","The study was published in a medical journal last spring."]},"questions":[{"q":"What was special about the study design?","options":["It was a blind comparison with a trained audiologist","Patients tested themselves at home","It only included children"],"a":0},{"q":"What happened in the 6% of cases that differed?","options":["The diagnosis changed","The differences were slight and didn't change the diagnosis","The device stopped working"],"a":1},{"q":"Why does the company need CE certification?","options":["Investors asked for it","It makes the device cheaper","It is required for a Class IIa device"],"a":2},{"q":"What does 'believe it or not' suggest about the first prototype?","options":["It was very expensive","It was surprisingly basic","It was kept secret"],"a":1},{"q":"What does the speaker imply by 'I'd say' before the timeline?","options":["They are completely certain","They don't know anything about certification","They want the investor to decide","They are giving a careful estimate, not a promise"],"a":3}],"gaps":[{"s":"Let me walk you ___ the prototype.","a":"through","hint":"adım adım anlatmak"},{"s":"The device has been ___ in a blind study at two university hospitals.","a":"validated","hint":"doğrulandı"},{"s":"CE certification is ___ for a Class IIa device like ours.","a":"required","hint":"zorunlu"}],"order":[{"a":"The study was published in a medical journal."},{"a":"The core technology is essentially in place."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Cihaz kör bir çalışmada doğrulandı.","en":"The device was validated in a blind study.","keys":["validated","blind study"]},{"tr":"Ana geliştirme aşaması tamamlandı.","en":"The main development phase has been completed.","keys":["development phase","completed"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Investor","personaTr":"Yatırımcı","scene":"Londra'da deneyimli bir sağlık teknolojisi yatırımcısı prototipini ve verilerini sorguluyor.","turns":[{"ai":"I've seen a lot of health-tech prototypes this year, so what makes yours different?","aiTr":"Bu yıl bir sürü sağlık teknolojisi prototipi gördüm; sizinkini farklı kılan ne?","hint":"It's an AI-assisted audiometer that makes hearing tests faster and more accessible without compromising on accuracy.","keys":["without compromising","accuracy","accessible"]},{"ai":"Has it actually been tested on patients, or is it still a lab project?","aiTr":"Gerçekten hastalar üzerinde test edildi mi, yoksa hâlâ bir laboratuvar projesi mi?","hint":"It has been validated in a blind study with 200 participants, and the results matched a trained audiologist in 94% of cases.","keys":["blind study","200","94"]},{"ai":"What about the other 6%? That's what a doctor would ask me.","aiTr":"Peki ya kalan %6? Bir doktor bana bunu sorardı.","hint":"They differed only slightly, and none of those differences changed the diagnosis.","keys":["differed","slightly","diagnosis"]},{"ai":"Okay, so what would my money actually be used for?","aiTr":"Tamam, peki param aslında ne için kullanılacak?","hint":"The €500,000 would be used to get through CE certification and enter the European market.","keys":["CE certification","European market","500"]}]}},"in-02":{"intro":"Gelir modelini ve rakamlarını bir yatırımcıya profesyonel bir dille açıklıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Me","en":"Whenever I meet investors, the conversation sooner or later comes down to one question: how does the business actually make money?","tr":"Yatırımcılarla ne zaman görüşsem, konuşma er ya da geç tek bir soruya geliyor: Bu iş aslında nasıl para kazanıyor?"},{"who":"Me","en":"Our revenue is generated in two ways: through device sales and through a monthly software subscription.","tr":"Gelirimiz iki şekilde elde ediliyor: cihaz satışları ve aylık yazılım aboneliği."},{"who":"Me","en":"Each device is sold for €4,000, while it costs us around €1,500 to produce.","tr":"Her cihaz 4.000 €'ya satılıyor, üretimi ise bize yaklaşık 1.500 €'ya mal oluyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"That leaves us with a gross margin of roughly 60 percent, which is healthy for a hardware product.","tr":"Bu da bize yaklaşık yüzde 60'lık bir brüt kâr marjı bırakıyor; bu, bir donanım ürünü için sağlıklı bir oran."},{"who":"Me","en":"The second stream is a software fee of €99 a month that every clinic pays to keep using the system.","tr":"İkinci gelir akışı, her kliniğin sistemi kullanmaya devam etmek için ödediği aylık 99 €'luk yazılım ücreti."},{"who":"Me","en":"It may look small, but it's recurring revenue, and that's what investors tend to value most.","tr":"Küçük görünebilir, ama bu tekrarlayan gelir ve yatırımcıların genellikle en çok değer verdiği şey de bu."},{"who":"Me","en":"If we were working with 1,000 clinics, the subscriptions alone would bring in about €1.2 million a year.","tr":"1.000 klinikle çalışıyor olsaydık, yalnızca abonelikler yılda yaklaşık 1,2 milyon € getirirdi."},{"who":"Me","en":"At the moment, we have five paying customers, so most of that growth is still ahead of us.","tr":"Şu anda beş ödeme yapan müşterimiz var, yani bu büyümenin büyük kısmı hâlâ önümüzde."},{"who":"Me","en":"Our main costs are salaries, certification and marketing, and certification in particular is expected to be expensive.","tr":"Ana maliyetlerimiz maaşlar, sertifikasyon ve pazarlama; özellikle sertifikasyonun pahalı olması bekleniyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"Based on our current plan, we expect to break even and become profitable in our third year.","tr":"Mevcut planımıza göre üçüncü yılımızda başa baş noktasına ulaşıp kârlı hale gelmeyi bekliyoruz."}],"vocab":[{"en":"come down to","tr":"özünde ...e varmak","ex":"It all comes down to one question.","def":"to be mainly about one thing"},{"en":"generate revenue","tr":"gelir elde etmek","ex":"Our revenue is generated in two ways.","def":"to produce income"},{"en":"subscription","tr":"abonelik","ex":"Clinics pay a monthly software subscription.","def":"a regular payment to keep using a service"},{"en":"leave someone with","tr":"birine ... bırakmak","ex":"That leaves us with a gross margin of 60 percent.","def":"to result in something remaining"},{"en":"revenue stream","tr":"gelir akışı","ex":"The software fee is our second revenue stream.","def":"one source of income for a business"},{"en":"tend to","tr":"-me eğiliminde olmak","ex":"Investors tend to value recurring revenue.","def":"to usually do something"},{"en":"ahead of us","tr":"önümüzde","ex":"Most of our growth is still ahead of us.","def":"in the future"},{"en":"in particular","tr":"özellikle","ex":"Certification in particular is expensive.","def":"especially"},{"en":"break even","tr":"başa baş noktasına ulaşmak","ex":"We expect to break even in our third year.","def":"to earn exactly as much as you spend"}],"grammar":{"title":"The passive in business explanations","tr":"Odak işi kimin yaptığında değil, işin kendisinde olduğunda passive kullanılır (be + V3). Finansal açıklamalarda daha profesyonel ve nesnel bir ton verir.","examples":["Our revenue is generated in two ways.","Each device is sold for €4,000.","Certification is expected to be expensive."]},"questions":[{"q":"How is the company's revenue generated?","options":["Through grants and donations","Through device sales and a monthly subscription","Through advertising"],"a":1},{"q":"Why does the speaker call a 60% gross margin 'healthy'?","options":["It is good for a hardware product","It is higher than any software company's","It covers all the salaries"],"a":0},{"q":"Why does the speaker say the €99 fee 'may look small'?","options":["To admit it is not important","To complain about low prices","To point out that its real value is that it recurs"],"a":2},{"q":"What would 1,000 clinics bring in from subscriptions alone?","options":["About €120,000 a year","About €1.2 million a year","About €12 million a year"],"a":1},{"q":"What does 'most of that growth is still ahead of us' suggest?","options":["The company is still at an early stage","Growth has already peaked","Customers are leaving"],"a":0}],"gaps":[{"s":"The conversation sooner or later comes ___ to one question.","a":"down","hint":"özünde ...e varmak (come down to)"},{"s":"That leaves us with a gross ___ of roughly 60 percent.","a":"margin","hint":"marj"},{"s":"We expect to break ___ in our third year.","a":"even","hint":"başa baş (break even)"}],"order":[{"a":"Investors tend to value recurring revenue most."},{"a":"Most of that growth is still ahead of us."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Gelirimiz iki şekilde elde ediliyor.","en":"Our revenue is generated in two ways.","keys":["revenue is generated","two ways"]},{"tr":"1.000 klinikle çalışıyor olsaydık, abonelikler yılda 1,2 milyon € getirirdi.","en":"If we were working with 1,000 clinics, the subscriptions would bring in €1.2 million a year.","keys":["if we were working","would bring in"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Angel investor","personaTr":"Melek yatırımcı","scene":"Deneyimli bir melek yatırımcı gelir modelinizi ve rakamlarınızı sorguluyor.","turns":[{"ai":"Walk me through your revenue model, if you would.","aiTr":"Gelir modelinizi bana bir anlatır mısınız?","hint":"Revenue is generated in two ways: device sales and a monthly software subscription.","keys":["device sales","subscription","two ways"]},{"ai":"And what kind of margin are we talking about on the hardware?","aiTr":"Donanımda nasıl bir marjdan bahsediyoruz?","hint":"Each device is sold for €4,000 and costs about €1,500 to produce, which leaves us with roughly 60 percent.","keys":["60 percent","leaves us with","4,000"]},{"ai":"€99 a month doesn't sound like much, does it?","aiTr":"Ayda 99 € pek fazla gibi görünmüyor, değil mi?","hint":"It may look small, but if we had 1,000 clinics, it would bring in about €1.2 million a year.","keys":["1.2 million","would bring in","may look small"]},{"ai":"When do you expect to stop burning cash?","aiTr":"Nakit yakmayı ne zaman bırakmayı bekliyorsunuz?","hint":"We expect to break even and become profitable in our third year.","keys":["break even","third year","profitable"]}]}},"in-04":{"intro":"Şüpheci bir yatırımcının rekabet, kopyalanma ve risk sorularını gerekçeli ve dürüst cevaplarla karşılıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Investor","en":"Let me play devil's advocate for a moment: who are you really competing against?","tr":"Bir an şeytanın avukatlığını yapayım: gerçekte kiminle rekabet ediyorsunuz?"},{"who":"Me","en":"The established players make classic audiometers, which are reliable but still have to be operated by a trained expert.","tr":"Köklü oyuncular klasik odyometreler yapıyor; bunlar güvenilir ama hâlâ eğitimli bir uzman tarafından kullanılmaları gerekiyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"There are also hearing apps on the market, but none of them have been certified as medical devices.","tr":"Piyasada işitme uygulamaları da var ama hiçbiri tıbbi cihaz olarak sertifikalandırılmadı."},{"who":"Investor","en":"If one of those big manufacturers decided to copy you tomorrow, what would stop them?","tr":"O büyük üreticilerden biri yarın sizi kopyalamaya karar verse, onları ne durdururdu?"},{"who":"Me","en":"Our AI has been trained on thousands of real tests, and that kind of clinical data can't be bought overnight.","tr":"Yapay zekâmız binlerce gerçek testle eğitildi ve bu tür klinik veriler bir gecede satın alınamaz."},{"who":"Me","en":"I'd also say that large companies tend to move slowly, whereas a team of six can change direction in weeks.","tr":"Ayrıca büyük şirketlerin yavaş hareket etme eğiliminde olduğunu, altı kişilik bir ekibin ise haftalar içinde yön değiştirebildiğini söyleyebilirim."},{"who":"Investor","en":"Fair enough, so what's the biggest risk to the business?","tr":"Makul; peki işiniz için en büyük risk ne?"},{"who":"Me","en":"To be honest, it's certification, since the process could take longer than we've planned.","tr":"Dürüst olmak gerekirse sertifikasyon, çünkü süreç planladığımızdan uzun sürebilir."},{"who":"Me","en":"That's why we started early and are working with a regulatory consultant who has years of experience with the CE process.","tr":"Bu yüzden erken başladık ve CE sürecinde yılların deneyimine sahip bir mevzuat danışmanıyla çalışıyoruz."},{"who":"Investor","en":"I've heard plenty of founders claim they have no real risks, so I appreciate the honesty.","tr":"Gerçek bir riskleri olmadığını iddia eden pek çok kurucu dinledim, o yüzden bu dürüstlüğü takdir ediyorum."}],"vocab":[{"en":"play devil's advocate","tr":"şeytanın avukatlığını yapmak","ex":"Let me play devil's advocate for a moment.","def":"to argue against an idea to test how strong it is"},{"en":"established player","tr":"köklü oyuncu, yerleşik şirket","ex":"The established players make classic audiometers.","def":"a company that has been in a market for a long time"},{"en":"be operated by","tr":"... tarafından kullanılmak","ex":"The device has to be operated by an expert.","def":"to be used or controlled by someone"},{"en":"be certified as","tr":"... olarak sertifikalandırılmak","ex":"None of the apps have been certified as medical devices.","def":"to be officially approved as a particular type of product"},{"en":"overnight","tr":"bir gecede, çok kısa sürede","ex":"Clinical data can't be bought overnight.","def":"very quickly or suddenly"},{"en":"tend to","tr":"...me eğiliminde olmak","ex":"Large companies tend to move slowly.","def":"to usually do something or behave in a certain way"},{"en":"change direction","tr":"yön değiştirmek","ex":"A small team can change direction in weeks.","def":"to change your plans or strategy"},{"en":"regulatory consultant","tr":"mevzuat danışmanı","ex":"We're working with an experienced regulatory consultant.","def":"an expert who helps companies meet official rules and get approval"}],"grammar":{"title":"The passive with modals and the present perfect","tr":"Edilgen yapı modal fiillerle (can't be bought, have to be operated) ve present perfect ile (has been trained, have been certified) de kurulur. Eylemi kimin yaptığından çok sonuca odaklanır.","examples":["Classic audiometers have to be operated by a trained expert.","None of the apps have been certified as medical devices.","That kind of clinical data can't be bought overnight."]},"questions":[{"q":"What is the weakness of classic audiometers, according to the founder?","options":["They are unreliable","They need a trained expert to operate them","They are too cheap"],"a":1},{"q":"Why doesn't the founder see hearing apps as a serious threat?","options":["None of them have been certified as medical devices","They are only sold in the US","They are too slow"],"a":0},{"q":"What two advantages does the founder mention against big manufacturers?","options":["Lower prices and more staff","A patent and a big office","Hard-to-get clinical data and speed"],"a":2},{"q":"How is the company dealing with the certification risk?","options":["It is waiting for the investor's help","It started early and works with an experienced regulatory consultant","It has decided to skip the EU"],"a":1},{"q":"What can you infer about the investor from the last line?","options":["They think the company has no chance","They want the founder to hide the risks","They value honest answers about risk more than a perfect story"],"a":2}],"gaps":[{"s":"Classic audiometers still have to be ___ by a trained expert.","a":"operated","hint":"kullanılmak, çalıştırılmak"},{"s":"Large companies ___ to move slowly.","a":"tend","hint":"eğiliminde olmak"},{"s":"None of them have been ___ as medical devices.","a":"certified","hint":"sertifikalandırılmış"}],"order":[{"a":"That kind of clinical data can't be bought overnight."},{"a":"A team of six can change direction in weeks."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Uygulamaların hiçbiri tıbbi cihaz olarak sertifikalandırılmadı.","en":"None of the apps have been certified as medical devices.","keys":["none of","certified","medical devices"]},{"tr":"Süreç planladığımızdan uzun sürebilir.","en":"The process could take longer than we've planned.","keys":["take longer","planned"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Sceptical investor","personaTr":"Şüpheci yatırımcı","scene":"Şüpheci bir yatırımcı şeytanın avukatlığını yapıyor; her soruya sakin ve gerekçeli cevap ver.","turns":[{"ai":"Who are you really competing against?","aiTr":"Gerçekte kiminle rekabet ediyorsunuz?","hint":"The established players make classic audiometers, but they still have to be operated by a trained expert.","keys":["established","operated","expert"]},{"ai":"And what about all those hearing apps?","aiTr":"Peki o kadar işitme uygulamasına ne demeli?","hint":"None of them have been certified as medical devices, so clinics can't really rely on them.","keys":["certified","medical devices","none of them"]},{"ai":"If a big manufacturer copied you tomorrow, what would stop them?","aiTr":"Büyük bir üretici yarın sizi kopyalasa, onları ne durdururdu?","hint":"Our AI has been trained on thousands of real tests, and that data can't be bought overnight. We also move faster.","keys":["trained","overnight","faster","data"]},{"ai":"What's the biggest risk to the business?","aiTr":"İşiniz için en büyük risk ne?","hint":"To be honest, it's certification, which is why we started early and work with an experienced regulatory consultant.","keys":["certification","started early","consultant"]}]}},"fu-02":{"intro":"Bir gazeteciyle sağlık verilerinin etiği üzerine röportajdasın; hastaların verileri üzerindeki kontrolünü ve gizlilik ile daha iyi yapay zekâ arasındaki dengeyi tartışıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Journalist","en":"Health data is often described as the new oil, so who do you think it really belongs to?","tr":"Sağlık verileri sık sık yeni petrol olarak tanımlanıyor; sizce gerçekte kime ait?"},{"who":"Me","en":"I'd say it belongs to the patient, and they should have a real say in who uses it and for what.","tr":"Bence hastaya ait ve onu kimin, ne amaçla kullandığı konusunda gerçek bir söz hakları olmalı."},{"who":"Me","en":"That's where informed consent comes in: people need to be told clearly what is collected, why, and for how long.","tr":"Bilgilendirilmiş onam tam burada devreye giriyor: insanlara neyin, neden ve ne kadar süreyle toplandığı açıkça söylenmeli."},{"who":"Me","en":"Consent also has to be something patients can withdraw, not a box they tick once and forget about.","tr":"Onam ayrıca hastaların geri çekebileceği bir şey olmalı; bir kez işaretleyip unuttukları bir kutucuk değil."},{"who":"Me","en":"Whenever data is used for research, it should be anonymised so that individuals can't be identified.","tr":"Veriler araştırmada her kullanıldığında, kişilerin kimliği belirlenemesin diye anonimleştirilmeli."},{"who":"Me","en":"In Europe, GDPR treats health data as a special category, which means companies are held to much stricter standards.","tr":"Avrupa'da GDPR sağlık verilerini özel nitelikli bir kategori olarak görüyor; bu da şirketlerin çok daha sıkı standartlara tabi olması demek."},{"who":"Me","en":"Our own approach is to run the AI on the device itself, so test data never has to leave the clinic.","tr":"Bizim yaklaşımımız yapay zekâyı doğrudan cihazın üzerinde çalıştırmak; böylece test verilerinin klinikten hiç çıkması gerekmiyor."},{"who":"Journalist","en":"Critics would argue that if you kept more data, your AI would improve much faster.","tr":"Eleştirmenler, daha fazla veri tutsaydınız yapay zekânızın çok daha hızlı gelişeceğini söylerdi."},{"who":"Me","en":"They're not wrong, and that's the uncomfortable trade-off: more data generally leads to better models, but every extra copy is another privacy risk.","tr":"Haksız değiller ve rahatsız edici ödünleşim de bu: daha fazla veri genellikle daha iyi modeller demek, ama her ek kopya bir gizlilik riski daha demek."},{"who":"Me","en":"We've decided to accept slower progress, so the model is only improved with anonymised data from clinical studies where participants gave consent.","tr":"Daha yavaş ilerlemeyi kabul etmeye karar verdik; bu yüzden model yalnızca katılımcıların onay verdiği klinik çalışmalardan gelen anonim verilerle geliştiriliyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"In the long run, I believe trust will turn out to be worth more than data.","tr":"Uzun vadede güvenin veriden daha değerli olduğunun ortaya çıkacağına inanıyorum."}],"vocab":[{"en":"the new oil","tr":"yeni petrol","ex":"Some people call data the new oil.","def":"something extremely valuable in today's economy"},{"en":"have a say in","tr":"...de söz sahibi olmak","ex":"Patients should have a say in who uses their data.","def":"to have the right to influence a decision"},{"en":"come in","tr":"devreye girmek","ex":"That's where informed consent comes in.","def":"used to show the role that something plays in a situation"},{"en":"withdraw consent","tr":"onayı geri çekmek","ex":"Patients can withdraw consent at any time.","def":"to take back permission you gave earlier"},{"en":"tick a box","tr":"kutucuk işaretlemek","ex":"Consent shouldn't be a box you tick once.","def":"to mark a form, often without really thinking about it"},{"en":"be identified","tr":"kimliği belirlenmek","ex":"Individuals can't be identified from anonymised data.","def":"to be recognised as a particular person"},{"en":"special category","tr":"özel nitelikli kategori","ex":"GDPR treats health data as a special category.","def":"a type of personal data that the law protects more strictly"},{"en":"be held to a standard","tr":"bir standarda tabi tutulmak","ex":"Companies are held to stricter standards.","def":"to be expected to reach a certain level"},{"en":"in the long run","tr":"uzun vadede","ex":"In the long run, trust is worth more than data.","def":"over a long period of time"}],"grammar":{"title":"The passive in formal explanations","tr":"Kurallar ve süreçler anlatılırken passive (be + V3) sık kullanılır: 'data is anonymised', 'individuals can't be identified', 'companies are held to stricter standards'. Vurgu, işi yapan kişide değil sürecin kendisindedir.","examples":["Whenever data is used for research, it should be anonymised.","Individuals can't be identified.","Companies are held to much stricter standards."]},"questions":[{"q":"Who does the speaker think health data belongs to?","options":["The patient","Whoever collects it","The government"],"a":0},{"q":"According to the speaker, what should be true of consent?","options":["It is given once and forever","Patients can withdraw it","Only doctors can give it"],"a":1},{"q":"Why does test data stay in the clinic?","options":["The clinic has better computers","GDPR bans all data transfers","The AI runs on the device itself"],"a":2},{"q":"What can we infer about the company's decision?","options":["It plans to sell data later","It has chosen privacy even if the AI improves more slowly","It ignores the critics completely"],"a":1},{"q":"What does the speaker mean by 'trust will turn out to be worth more than data'?","options":["Data will soon become cheap","Trust can be bought with data","Keeping patients' trust is more valuable in the long term"],"a":2}],"gaps":[{"s":"Patients should have a real ___ in who uses their data.","a":"say","hint":"söz hakkı"},{"s":"Consent has to be something patients can ___.","a":"withdraw","hint":"geri çekmek"},{"s":"GDPR treats health data as a special ___.","a":"category","hint":"kategori"}],"order":[{"a":"Test data never has to leave the clinic."},{"a":"Trust is worth more than data."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Daha fazla veri tutsaydınız, yapay zekânız daha hızlı gelişirdi.","en":"If you kept more data, your AI would improve faster.","keys":["if you kept","would improve"]},{"tr":"Kişilerin kimliği belirlenemez.","en":"Individuals can't be identified.","keys":["can't be identified"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"Journalist","personaTr":"Gazeteci","scene":"Bir gazeteci, sağlık verilerinin etiği hakkında zorlayıcı sorularla seninle röportaj yapıyor.","turns":[{"ai":"Some say health data is the new oil. Who does it really belong to?","aiTr":"Bazıları sağlık verisinin yeni petrol olduğunu söylüyor. Aslında kime ait?","hint":"I'd say it belongs to the patient, and they should have a real say in who uses it.","keys":["belongs to the patient","real say","have a say"]},{"ai":"Isn't consent just a box people tick without reading?","aiTr":"Onam, insanların okumadan işaretlediği bir kutucuktan ibaret değil mi?","hint":"It shouldn't be; people need to be told clearly what is collected and why, and they can withdraw consent.","keys":["told clearly","withdraw","what is collected"]},{"ai":"How is your company's approach different?","aiTr":"Şirketinizin yaklaşımı nasıl farklı?","hint":"Our AI runs on the device itself, so test data never has to leave the clinic.","keys":["runs on the device","never has to leave","clinic"]},{"ai":"Wouldn't your AI improve faster if you collected more data?","aiTr":"Daha fazla veri toplasaydınız yapay zekânız daha hızlı gelişmez miydi?","hint":"Probably, but it's a trade-off; we only use anonymised data from studies where participants gave consent.","keys":["trade-off","anonymised","consent"]}]}},"in-03":{"intro":"Yatırımcının teklifini değerlendiriyor, değerlemeyi somut gerekçelerle yukarı çekmeye çalışıyorsun.","text":[{"who":"Investor","en":"We've been really impressed by the progress you've made, so we'd like to put an offer on the table.","tr":"Kaydettiğiniz ilerlemeden gerçekten etkilendik, bu yüzden masaya bir teklif koymak istiyoruz."},{"who":"Investor","en":"We're prepared to invest €500,000 in exchange for a 25 percent stake.","tr":"Yüzde 25'lik bir hisse karşılığında 500.000 euro yatırım yapmaya hazırız."},{"who":"Me","en":"Thank you, I appreciate that, although it would put our post-money valuation at only two million euros.","tr":"Teşekkür ederim, bunu takdir ediyorum; ancak bu, yatırım sonrası değerlememizi sadece iki milyon euroya indirir."},{"who":"Me","en":"I'd say that undervalues what we've already achieved.","tr":"Bence bu, şimdiye kadar başardıklarımızın değerini düşük gösteriyor."},{"who":"Me","en":"Our third prototype is being used by five paying customers, and our clinical study has been published in a medical journal.","tr":"Üçüncü prototipimiz ödeme yapan beş müşteri tarafından kullanılıyor ve klinik çalışmamız bir tıp dergisinde yayımlandı."},{"who":"Investor","en":"Those are good signs, but the device still hasn't been certified, which is where most of the risk lies.","tr":"Bunlar iyi işaretler ama cihaz hâlâ sertifikalandırılmadı ve riskin büyük kısmı da tam orada."},{"who":"Me","en":"That's fair, and it's exactly why we're raising this round: to finish certification and enter the European market.","tr":"Haklısınız; zaten bu turu tam da bu yüzden topluyoruz: sertifikasyonu tamamlamak ve Avrupa pazarına girmek için."},{"who":"Me","en":"If we were to meet you halfway, would €2.5 million post-money for a 20 percent stake work for you?","tr":"Sizinle ortada buluşsak, yüzde 20 hisse için yatırım sonrası 2,5 milyon euro size uyar mı?"},{"who":"Investor","en":"We could live with that, provided that we get a seat on the board.","tr":"Yönetim kurulunda bir koltuk almamız şartıyla buna razı olabiliriz."},{"who":"Me","en":"That's fine with us, since we're looking for a partner who will be actively involved, not just a cheque.","tr":"Bu bizim için uygun, çünkü sadece bir çek değil, işin içinde aktif olarak yer alacak bir ortak arıyoruz."},{"who":"Investor","en":"Then I think we have a deal, subject to due diligence.","tr":"O zaman sanırım anlaştık, tabii durum tespiti sürecine bağlı olarak."}],"vocab":[{"en":"put an offer on the table","tr":"masaya bir teklif koymak","ex":"The fund put an offer on the table last week.","def":"to make a formal offer that the other side can discuss"},{"en":"stake","tr":"hisse payı","ex":"They want a 25 percent stake in the company.","def":"a share of a company that someone owns"},{"en":"undervalue","tr":"değerini düşük biçmek","ex":"I'd say that undervalues what we've achieved.","def":"to say something is worth less than it really is"},{"en":"raise a round","tr":"yatırım turu toplamak","ex":"We're raising this round to finish certification.","def":"to collect money from investors in one funding stage"},{"en":"meet someone halfway","tr":"ortada buluşmak, orta yolu bulmak","ex":"We're ready to meet you halfway on the valuation.","def":"to accept a compromise between two positions"},{"en":"live with something","tr":"bir şeye razı olmak","ex":"We could live with that valuation.","def":"to accept something even if it is not perfect"},{"en":"provided that","tr":"...şartıyla","ex":"We'll invest, provided that we get a board seat.","def":"only if; on the condition that"},{"en":"actively involved","tr":"aktif olarak işin içinde","ex":"We want a partner who is actively involved.","def":"taking part in something and helping, not only watching"},{"en":"due diligence","tr":"durum tespiti, ayrıntılı inceleme","ex":"The deal is subject to due diligence.","def":"a careful check of a company before an investment is final"}],"grammar":{"title":"The passive: focus on the result","tr":"Kimin yaptığı önemli olmadığında edilgen yapı kullanılır: 'be + V3'. Zamanı 'be' fiili gösterir: is being used, has been published, hasn't been certified.","examples":["Our third prototype is being used by five paying customers.","Our clinical study has been published in a medical journal.","The device still hasn't been certified."]},"questions":[{"q":"What post-money valuation does the first offer imply?","options":["€2 million","€2.5 million","€3 million"],"a":0},{"q":"According to the investor, where does most of the risk lie?","options":["In the price of the device","In the missing certification","In the size of the team","In the competition"],"a":1},{"q":"What is the money from this round mainly for?","options":["Hiring a sales team in the US","Building a fourth prototype","Finishing certification and entering the European market"],"a":2},{"q":"Why is the founder happy to give a board seat?","options":["It is required by law","They want a partner who is actively involved","The investor offered more money for it"],"a":1},{"q":"What can we infer from 'subject to due diligence'?","options":["The deal is already signed","The investor wants to lower the price again","The investor will still check the company before the deal is final"],"a":2}],"gaps":[{"s":"We're prepared to invest €500,000 in exchange for a 25 percent ___.","a":"stake","hint":"hisse payı"},{"s":"I'd say that ___ what we've already achieved.","a":"undervalues","hint":"değerini düşük göstermek"},{"s":"We could live with that, ___ that we get a seat on the board.","a":"provided","hint":"...şartıyla"}],"order":[{"a":"Our clinical study has been published in a medical journal."},{"a":"We are looking for a partner who will be actively involved."}],"translate":[{"tr":"Sizinle ortada buluşmaya hazırız.","en":"We are ready to meet you halfway.","keys":["meet you halfway"]},{"tr":"Cihaz henüz sertifikalandırılmadı.","en":"The device hasn't been certified yet.","keys":["hasn't been certified"]}],"roleplay":{"persona":"VC fund partner","personaTr":"Risk sermayesi fonu ortağı","scene":"Fon ortağı resmî teklifini sunuyor; değerlemeyi gerekçelerle yükseltmeye çalışıyorsun.","turns":[{"ai":"We're prepared to invest €500,000 for a 25 percent stake. What do you think?","aiTr":"Yüzde 25'lik hisse için 500.000 euro yatırım yapmaya hazırız. Ne düşünüyorsunuz?","hint":"Thank you, but that would put our post-money valuation at only two million, which I'd say undervalues the company.","keys":["valuation","undervalues","two million"]},{"ai":"What makes you think the company is worth more?","aiTr":"Şirketin daha değerli olduğunu size düşündüren ne?","hint":"Our product is already being used by five paying customers, and our clinical study has been published.","keys":["paying customers","published","clinical study"]},{"ai":"But the device still hasn't been certified. That's a big risk for us.","aiTr":"Ama cihaz hâlâ sertifikalandırılmadı. Bu bizim için büyük bir risk.","hint":"That's fair, and that's exactly why we're raising this round: to finish certification and enter Europe.","keys":["certification","raising","fair"]},{"ai":"So where would you like to land?","aiTr":"Peki nerede anlaşmak istersiniz?","hint":"If we met you halfway, would €2.5 million post-money for 20 percent work for you?","keys":["halfway","2.5 million","20 percent"]}]}}};
